window.FWN_UNDEAD_LEGION_CHAPTERS=(window.FWN_UNDEAD_LEGION_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":1201,"title":"Chapter 1201: You Want My Tree","paragraphs":["Of course, that created another problem. Jester wasn’t human. Most ordinary people assumed he was. Revealing that the young man they had been watching online for months was actually an undead creature might create a rather interesting reaction.","The second possibility was that Jester was simply not influential in the right place. Michael might have been moving in the correct direction from the beginning. Perhaps Jester really could satisfy the requirement. He simply hadn’t reached the necessary threshold.","After all, being famous and being influential were different things. Jester was currently something close to an internet celebrity. But what actual influence did he possess?","Could his words alter events across Aurora?","At most, he could probably advertise something online and cause it to sell out. Simply becoming more popular online might not be enough.","Then there was a third possibility. One Michael liked considerably less.","What if an undead simply didn’t count?","The wording didn’t say creature. It said entity. That distinction might be important.","[Own an entity on the level of your Personal Influence.]","Entity was an extremely broad term. A person could be considered an entity. But so could an organization. A kingdom. A guild. A company. A territory. Perhaps even an artifact, depending on how the Origin Will defined things.","He wanted to ask it directly, but felt he should wait; it hadn’t even been half a year yet, and he didn’t want to waste the chance so soon.","Of course, as precious as the opportunity to speak directly with the Origin Will was, his advancement mattered just as much.","However, Michael had a feeling the Origin Battlefield might be where he finally found a breakthrough.","As for why the Universal Cornerstone didn’t count, perhaps it was because claiming it wasn’t the same as truly owning it, at least not according to the Origin Will. But this theory had holes, which made Michael feel a bit of dread for the future.","Michael’s eyes narrowed slightly.","\"The Origin Battlefield...\"","Perhaps that place really was the answer.","Currently, his other body was in the Origin Battlefield thanks to the use of his Legendary item, while other awakeners could not access it.","Aside from not being able to leave his territory for some reason, all was fine.","In any case, it would open for him again soon. Though there was no designated time when the battlefield reopened, Michael felt that other awakeners like him shared a vague awareness that it would be soon.","He couldn’t explain why, but he knew the Origin Battlefield would reopen soon.","Michael looked at the quest panel one final time. Then he dismissed it.","\"Enough.\"","There were more immediate matters to deal with.","Michael glanced around. Then he paused.","\"Where’s Isabella?\"","The ghost tilted her head.","Michael’s perception immediately expanded. Several kilometres away, he finally sensed the familiar violet soul flame.","\"...She really ran that far?\"","To be fair, considering what he had just done to the mountain, he couldn’t blame her.","Michael rose into the air.","\"Please wait for me here.\"","Michael accelerated. A few moments later, he found Isabella still moving away from the ruined region.","\"Isabella.\"","The Skeleton Chief immediately stopped and turned.","\"Senior?\"","\"Yes.\"","\"You’re alive.\"","Michael’s expression flattened.","\"Were you expecting something else?\"","Isabella hesitated. Her gaze moved past him toward the distant destruction.","The upper half of a mountain was gone. Dozens of kilometres of terrain had been transformed into a frozen wasteland. Enormous crystalline formations continued growing around the impact zone.","\"...No, Senior.\"","Michael sighed.","\"Come back.\"","Isabella obeyed immediately.","Soon they were back at the ghost’s location, and together they all headed toward the site of the Nether Soul Tree.","Soon, the familiar ravine appeared. Or rather, what remained of it. Fortunately, the area surrounding the Nether Soul Tree had been far enough from Michael’s attack that it remained mostly intact.","The strange black tree still stood alone. The moment the ghost saw it, she accelerated. She reached the tree and immediately wrapped both arms around the trunk.","Michael stopped nearby.","Michael watched the ghost cling to the Nether Soul Tree for several seconds before speaking.","\"You know, since you’re coming with me anyway... wouldn’t it make sense to bring the tree too?\"","The ghost’s silver eyes narrowed at him.","Michael raised both hands.","\"I’m not taking it from you.\"","She continued staring.","\"I’m serious.\"","Michael pointed toward the tree.","\"You clearly don’t want to leave it behind, and I don’t particularly want to make repeated trips into the Netherworld just because you suddenly decide you miss your tree.\"","The ghost looked at the Nether Soul Tree. Then back at Michael.","Michael continued.","\"I can create an environment rich in dark-element energy suitable for it.\"","The ghost’s expression gradually became thoughtful. Several seconds passed before she finally nodded.","\"Okay.\"","Michael smiled.","Then the ghost added, \"You pay me.\"","Michael’s smile vanished.","\"...What?\"","She released the tree and floated toward him.","\"You want my tree.\"","\"I don’t want your tree.\"","\"You said you want to move it.\"","\"That’s because you’re coming with me.\"","\"Yes.\"","\"And you want me to bring it.\"","The ghost nodded.","\"So why am I paying you?\"","Her expression became confused.","\"Because you’ll use it.\"","Michael opened his mouth. Then stopped.","Technically, she isn’t wrong.","The Nether Soul Tree was a Three-Star Epic treasure. There was absolutely no chance Michael would move something that valuable into the Mausoleum and never make use of it.","Even if he didn’t cut it apart, the energy it produced alone was valuable.","Just because Michael could create his own Epic-grade treasures, even Epic-grade ones, didn’t mean he could dictate the end results of an evolution. That was far beyond his control.","With thousands of experiences now, Michael had seen two creatures from the same race take two different evolution routes. While he could influence the direction, what he’d get in the end wasn’t his to command.","This was why Michael still found some treasures very valuable, regardless of grade or how easily he could create them."]},{"number":1202,"title":"Chapter 1202: Return","paragraphs":["In the future, once he finally made the ghost truly submit to him, or at least trust him fully enough to do anything he wanted, he could evolve this tree to Legendary grade. Its effect would be even greater.","Michael’s eyelid twitched at the ghost’s intentions.","\"That doesn’t mean I should pay you to move it.\"","\"You’ll use it.\"","\"That’s for the future to decide.\"","The ghost stared at him. Michael stared back.","She pointed toward the tree.","\"Crystals.\"","\"No.\"","\"Crystals.\"","\"No.\"","The ghost floated closer.","Michael folded his arms.","\"You’re getting greedy.\"","Her expression remained completely serious.","\"You said work gets crystals.\"","\"Yes.\"","\"You move my tree.\"","\"That’s me working.\"","She paused.","Michael immediately continued.","\"If anything, you should be paying me.\"","The ghost’s silver eyes widened. Soon she wore a wounded expression on her face.","Michael could practically see her reconsidering the entire situation.","Behind him, Isabella’s violet soul flames flickered strangely. Michael ignored her.","The ghost eventually pointed toward the tree again.","\"But you’ll use it.\"","Michael sighed.","\"Yes.\"","\"Then crystals.\"","\"No.\"","\"Why so stingy?\"","\"You...!\"","His home training won out in the end. Finally, after so many refusals, the ghost gave up.","\"Okay.\"","Michael relaxed.","Over the next few minutes, Michael focused entirely on preparing a suitable location for the Nether Soul Tree. This was already becoming a familiar process.","His consciousness spread throughout the Mausoleum of Endless Dominion, passing across the enormous independent world until he reached one of the remaining regions naturally saturated with dark-element energy.","There were noticeably fewer of those regions now.","Between the Soul Preservation Flame, the numerous dark-element resources he had gathered throughout the Netherworld, the undead settlements he had relocated, and several other treasures requiring specialized environments, Michael had already consumed a surprising number of the Mausoleum’s naturally valuable locations.","Still, there remained enough.","Michael soon selected a suitable region. The land there stretched across an enormous black plain surrounded by jagged mountain ranges.","Dark-element mana naturally gathered between the peaks before flowing downward into the basin below, creating an environment considerably richer than most parts of the Mausoleum.","Michael began modifying it immediately. The ground beneath the selected area slowly sank. A massive depression formed. The surrounding mountains shifted slightly as Michael redirected several natural streams of dark-element energy toward the center.","Michael deliberately avoided making the environment identical to the Netherworld.","The Nether Soul Tree had already proven capable of surviving naturally within an environment saturated with death and soul energy, so there was no need to reproduce every characteristic of the realm of the dead.","Instead, he simply ensured that the basic element most closely associated with the tree remained abundant.","By the time Michael finished, the entire region had changed. Thin streams of pale mist drifted above the black ground. Dark-element mana continuously gathered from the surrounding mountains.","It was easily one of the richest environments inside the Mausoleum.","Fortunately, the Mausoleum was enormous. Even if naturally exceptional regions were limited, Michael could always alter ordinary environments later using treasures, formations, resources, or the Mausoleum’s own abilities. For now, this was more than sufficient.","Michael returned his attention to the Nether Soul Tree. His mana spread underground. Unlike when he had harvested the dark crystal mine, Michael moved carefully.","The tree itself was far too valuable to risk damaging simply because brute force was faster.","His mana traced the roots individually. Some extended several dozen metres underground. Others intertwined with natural veins of energy beneath the ravine.","Michael gradually separated the surrounding earth from the larger landscape. Cracks appeared several dozen metres away from the trunk. They travelled downward rather than inward, forming an enormous block around the entire root system.","The ground trembled. Large sections of black stone broke free.","Several minutes later, an enormous mass of earth containing the Nether Soul Tree slowly rose from the ravine. The pale-blue flames surrounding its branches flickered but remained stable. None of the major roots had been damaged.","Michael immediately opened the Mausoleum. Space distorted beside the floating section of land before expanding into an enormous gateway. Beyond it lay the newly prepared region.","Michael guided the entire mass through. The moment the Nether Soul Tree entered the Mausoleum, the surrounding energy reacted.","Michael lowered the enormous section of earth into the prepared depression. The surrounding land shifted. Stone connected with stone. Earth closed around the edges. Within seconds, the transplanted section had completely merged with the new environment.","The Nether Soul Tree stood exactly as it had before. Only its surroundings had changed.","The silver lines beneath its black bark gradually brightened, and the pale-blue Soul Flames floating around its branches expanded slightly. Several smaller flames appeared between them.","Michael watched carefully for several moments. There were no signs of rejection.","The ghost entered the Mausoleum immediately afterward. Her translucent figure crossed the gateway and appeared beside the tree. She remained near it while Michael continued monitoring the surrounding energy flow.","Isabella followed shortly after.","Michael adjusted several minor details. The energy concentration was increased slightly around the roots. The dark-element streams flowing down from the surrounding mountains were redistributed more evenly.","A section of land nearby was flattened to provide space for any future resources or undead Michael might decide to place within the region.","Only after confirming that the environment remained stable did Michael finally stop.","Everything they had gathered throughout the expedition was now safely stored.","Michael allowed his perception to sweep across the Mausoleum one final time. The once relatively empty world was beginning to feel noticeably different.","There were still enormous stretches of untouched wilderness, but life, or rather undeath this time, had begun appearing throughout it.","Skeleton settlements occupied one region. Ghosts wandered through another. Various weaker undead roamed through forests, valleys, plains, and ruins previously left empty.","Michael withdrew his consciousness.","The spatial gateway gradually contracted. Then it disappeared completely.","The Netherworld became silent again.","However, Michael had only just settled when a panel appeared in front of him.","After dropping a short sentence to both the skeleton and the ghost, telling them to remain where they stood and that he’d be back soon, Michael disappeared from his location.","Soon he was back at the place he had left Lucky to evolve.","Yes.","Lucky was done with his evolution to an Epic-grade Three-Star creature, just in time to match Michael’s return."]},{"number":1203,"title":"Chapter 1203: The First One {Editted!!}","paragraphs":["The clearing Michael remembered was gone. In its place stood a creature so enormous that the surrounding trees barely reached its shoulders.","Lucky had grown again.","His new body stood nearly forty metres tall even while resting on all fours. Thick greyish-green fur covered him from head to tail, though unlike the vibrant fur of an ordinary living beast, his coat looked strangely dry. Individual strands resembled withered grass, rough and almost lifeless, with darker patches spreading along his back and limbs.","His enormous paws pressed deeply into the earth. Each one was large enough to crush a small building beneath it, ending in thick black claws that curved into the ground.","His body had also become considerably more muscular. Powerful shoulders rose beneath the dry fur, while his chest and limbs carried enough mass to make his previous form appear almost immature in comparison.","However, the most noticeable change was his back.","A huge pair of wings extended from behind his shoulders. Even folded, they were enormous, resting along both sides of his body and extending almost to the ground. They were covered in the same greyish-green fur near their base, gradually transitioning into darker colours toward their ends.","Lucky’s head had changed as well. His skull appeared broader, his muzzle longer, and two enormous fangs protruded slightly from beneath his upper lips. Despite his size, there was nothing clumsy about his appearance. His proportions remained almost unnaturally balanced.","Then his eyes opened.","Bright green eyes immediately locked onto Michael.","The enormous wolf remained still for several seconds before slowly lowering his massive head. The movement alone displaced the surrounding air.","Michael approached without hesitation. Lucky’s head eventually stopped only a short distance above the ground, bringing his enormous muzzle close enough for Michael to reach.","Michael raised one hand and placed it against the side of Lucky’s face.","The sensation wasn’t warm. It couldn’t be, as Lucky was still an undead. There was no beating heart hidden beneath that enormous chest, no warm blood circulating through his veins, and his body didn’t produce the natural heat expected from a creature of his size.","Yet neither did he feel like a corpse.","Michael’s talent had long since pushed his undead beyond something as simple as animated bodies. Every evolution refined them. Their bodies became increasingly complete, and even the flaws normally associated with undead creatures gradually disappeared as they approached the most perfect form their species could possibly attain.","Lucky was perhaps one of the clearest examples. The dry fur beneath Michael’s hand shifted naturally beneath his fingers. Muscles responded beneath the skin. Lucky’s green eyes moved with awareness, following Michael even as his enormous head remained lowered.","There was intelligence there.","Lucky wasn’t alive. But calling him dead didn’t feel entirely correct either.","Living dead. Michael couldn’t think of a more appropriate description. And after reaching Epic Three-Star, that contradiction had only become more pronounced.","However, as Michael continued examining Lucky’s new form, a faint sense of conflict gradually appeared in his eyes. It had nothing to do with Lucky’s appearance. The problem was how quickly he had awakened.","Normally, that would have been the usual outcome. But this time, Michael had been hoping for something more.","Rank Five.","Michael still had no idea what exactly would happen when one of his undead crossed that threshold. Rank Five was the Demigod realm. It was an enormous qualitative transformation, and Michael doubted such an advancement could happen quietly.","Rank Four certainly hadn’t. When Lucky had first crossed into Rank Four, a lightning tribulation had descended. The advancement itself had caused an obvious phenomenon. Yet this time, nothing had happened.","No tribulation. No strange phenomenon. Lucky had simply finished evolving and awakened.","That alone was enough for Michael to understand that Lucky hadn’t reached Rank Five, even without a deep look at the panels that followed its evolution. Despite becoming an Epic Three-Star creature, he was still Rank Four.","Michael’s hand continued moving through the enormous wolf’s dry fur as he accepted the result. He couldn’t deny that he felt slightly disappointed. After seeing how absurdly powerful Lucky had become with each evolution, a small part of Michael had hoped that reaching Three-Star Epic would somehow push him directly across the boundary separating Rank Four from Rank Five.","Apparently, things weren’t going to be that convenient.","Still, the disappointment lasted only a few seconds.","Lucky’s aura was terrifying. Michael had sensed it the moment he entered the clearing, but only after standing directly beside Lucky did he properly appreciate how much the creature had changed.","The pressure naturally radiating from Lucky’s enormous body was immense. It wasn’t deliberately released, as Lucky wasn’t trying to intimidate him, nor could he. But Michael could feel the sheer amount of power contained within him.","More surprisingly, Michael realized it was even stronger than the pressure he had felt from the Undead High Drake.","That genuinely shocked him. The Undead High Drake was already an absurd Rank Four existence. Its enormous body, draconic bloodline, physical strength, and accumulated foundation made it one of Michael’s strongest undead, if not his strongest undead. Saying it was one of Michael’s strongest undead, rather than simply the strongest, was because of the existence of Beginning.","Yet Lucky’s presence now surpassed it. Not by such an overwhelming margin that the High Drake suddenly felt weak, but enough that Michael could clearly distinguish between them.","There was also another reason Michael wasn’t too disappointed.","The moment he confirmed Lucky hadn’t reached Rank Five, Michael had already made a decision.","Lucky was going to evolve again. Lucky was going to become Michael’s first Legendary-grade undead.","The thought should probably have required considerably more consideration than Michael was currently giving it. After all, Legendary grade was completely different from Epic. Michael had already seen enough evidence to understand how enormous the difference between grades became at higher levels.","The real problem was control. Michael still couldn’t properly control a Rank Five undead. A Demigod was simply too far above him.","However, Michael’s experiences over the past few days had repeatedly shown him that losing absolute control didn’t automatically mean losing everything. The Undead High Drake and Bone Dragon had already demonstrated that. The ghost had demonstrated it even more clearly.","Michael believed that even if he couldn’t directly force a sufficiently powerful undead to obey every command, the connection between creator and creation should still exist. More importantly, unless the undead possessed strong malice toward him, they wouldn’t necessarily attack him simply because his control weakened.","And Lucky was perhaps the undead Michael trusted most to test that theory.","Sentiment certainly played a role in Michael’s decision. He wasn’t going to pretend otherwise. But sentiment wasn’t the only reason. Lucky was also an excellent experiment.","Eventually, Michael would have to begin evolving more of his undead into Legendary grade. Avoiding it simply because he couldn’t guarantee absolute control over the resulting Rank Five existence would only delay the inevitable. Someone had to be first. Lucky was as good a choice as Michael could possibly make.","If the evolution succeeded and Lucky remained cooperative, Michael would gain his first Legendary undead and learn considerably more about how his connection behaved when one of his creations entered Rank Five.","After all, if a Legendary-grade undead with dragon blood could still obey him, didn’t that mean he could go a little all out?","Even if Lucky stopped obeying him completely, Michael would learn from that too. It wouldn’t even necessarily be a loss. If the worst happened, Lucky simply wouldn’t leave the Mausoleum. Michael had no problem doing that. The Mausoleum of Endless Dominion was enormous enough to contain him indefinitely, and Michael possessed overwhelming authority over the world itself.","In that sense, it was the perfect testing ground. A sanctuary if everything went well. A cage if it didn’t.","Michael’s gaze returned to the enormous wolf before him. Lucky remained completely unaware that Michael had already decided to gamble with his next stage of existence.","Michael slowly withdrew his hand from the greyish-green fur. The disappointment from earlier had completely disappeared.","If Three-Star Epic wasn’t enough to produce a Demigod, then so be it. He would simply go one step further.","Legendary grade.","\"Infinite Evolution! Show me your limit!\"","[Cost of Evolution: 1,000,000 Evolution Points]","[Confirm Evolution?]","[Yes]","The moment the confirmation went through, the numbers plummeted. One million Evolution Points disappeared from Michael’s possession in an instant.","Even though he had already known the cost, actually watching such an enormous amount vanish still produced a strange emptiness in his chest.","Fortunately, Michael didn’t have much time to mourn his suddenly impoverished state.","The enormous wolf’s bright green eyes widened. Then his head snapped upward.","\"AWOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOO!\"","The howl exploded across many regions in the Mausoleum.","Michael’s expression changed immediately. The surrounding forest bent outward as though struck by an invisible wave. Leaves exploded from branches. Smaller trees were uprooted completely, while the earth beneath Lucky’s paws cracked in every direction.","Michael’s robes whipped violently around him.","Then the ground moved.","A thick greyish-green vine erupted from below. It was enormous. The vine was thicker than the trunks of many ancient trees within the surrounding forest, its surface dry and rough, almost identical in colour to Lucky’s fur.","Then another appeared. And another. And another.","Within seconds, the entire clearing began collapsing. Hundreds of vines tore through the ground simultaneously.","BOOM!","Michael immediately shot into the air. A vine erupted directly beneath where he had been standing a fraction of a second earlier. It continued upward for dozens of metres before curving inward toward Lucky.","Michael accelerated. The situation was developing much differently than Lucky’s previous evolutions.","More vines emerged beyond the clearing. They twisted around one another, climbing higher and higher as their tips curved toward a single point above Lucky.","Michael shot through one of the rapidly shrinking openings just before two enormous vines intertwined behind him.","Within moments, the entire clearing was enclosed.","Michael stopped several hundred metres away in the air.","What had once been a forest clearing now contained an enormous dome."]},{"number":1204,"title":"Chapter 1204: More Evolution [1]","paragraphs":["The dome was enormous. From a distance, it resembled some monstrous plant that had suddenly taken root in the middle of the Mausoleum.","Hundreds of greyish-green vines had woven themselves together so tightly that there was almost no space between them. Some were thicker than ancient trees, while others were considerably thinner and filled the remaining gaps, wrapping around the larger vines in layer after layer.","Within seconds, Lucky had completely disappeared from sight.","The vines didn’t stop growing after the dome closed. They continued crawling across one another, tightening and reinforcing the structure until the outer surface became difficult to distinguish as individual plants. Smaller roots sprouted from the vines and dug into neighbouring ones, binding everything together into what almost resembled a single living shell.","Their colour was wrong as well, making it look like there was very little vitality to it. Despite being plants, the vines weren’t the vibrant green one would normally associate with life. Their surfaces were greyish-green and dry, with sections appearing withered enough that one would think of them as dead. Yet the amount of vitality contained within them was terrifying.","Michael hovered several hundred metres away and watched as a faint light appeared. The entire interior of the dome seemed to illuminate.","Thin lines of light appeared between the overlapping vines, spreading across the structure like cracks.","For several seconds, it looked as though something inside was about to erupt.","The surrounding space trembled. Several beams nearly forced their way through the gaps. Yet before any of them could escape, the vines reacted and tightened. More vines emerged from the ground and wrapped around the dome. The tiny openings disappeared one after another as another layer formed over the first.","Soon, the light vanished. A few seconds later, it returned brighter, and the vines tightened again to reinforce the dome.","This repeated several times as the mana in the surrounding region continued to drastically reduce.","At first, the change was subtle. Mana naturally existed everywhere inside the Mausoleum, especially within this region. Michael had specifically chosen areas like this for his more powerful undead because of their naturally superior environments.","But now every trace of mana in the surroundings was being dragged toward the dome. The speed increased rapidly. Within several hundred metres, the mana concentration visibly decreased.","Then the affected area expanded.","One kilometre.","Two.","Five.","Michael’s expression gradually became serious.","The dome had transformed into an enormous bottomless pit. Mana rushed toward it from every direction. Elemental particles that normally drifted naturally throughout the environment were pulled toward Lucky and disappeared the moment they touched the vines.","The plants themselves seemed desperately hungry. Their roots spread farther underground, penetrating deep into the earth as they searched for more energy. Some reached nearby mana veins and immediately began draining them.","A while later, Michael extended his perception and was surprised by what he discovered.","There was almost nothing.","The area immediately surrounding the dome had practically become a mana-dead zone. Mana entering the region couldn’t remain for more than a few moments before being seized and dragged toward Lucky.","Even Michael felt a faint pulling sensation against the mana inside his body. It wasn’t enough to threaten him but the fact that Lucky’s evolution could affect him at all from this distance was impressive.","Michael moved farther away, but didn’t try to stop the process. Instead, he redirected several nearby streams of mana toward this region.","Michael continued watching when his expression suddenly changed as his perception sharpened. Thoughts that had previously required conscious effort became easier to follow, while concepts that had remained vague seemed to lose some of their obscurity.","Michael immediately recognized the sensation.","Comprehension enhancement.","It was a normal phenomenon that accompanied the evolution of his undead, with the degree of effect based on what grade the evolution was. Until today, the most effective ones belonged to when his undead were evolving to One-Star Epic grade.","Michael still didn’t completely understand why it happened. Perhaps it was a consequence of a lifeform undergoing such a fundamental transformation. Perhaps the process itself caused certain principles normally hidden within the world to become temporarily clearer.","Whatever the reason, Michael had experienced it enough times to recognize it immediately and had benefited from it several times already.","But this...","Michael slowly took a deep breath.","This was on another level entirely. The difference was so enormous that for a moment he wondered whether his already abnormal comprehension had somehow undergone another permanent transformation.","Of course, it hadn’t. The effect was external.","Michael’s eyes brightened.","Lucky’s evolution this time might take at least a week to a few weeks. Perhaps even longer. If this comprehension phenomenon remained active throughout the entire process, he wouldn’t need to feel bad about having other important matters to attend to right now.","Michael took one final look at the enormous dome. The greyish-green vines continued tightening around one another while mana poured toward them from every direction. Occasional flashes of light still escaped through tiny gaps before being smothered by newly grown layers.","Lucky’s evolution had only just begun. There was nothing more Michael needed to do here.","His figure disappeared.","When Michael reappeared, the environment around him had completely changed. He now stood on an enormous island elsewhere within the Mausoleum.","The island stretched for hundreds of kilometres, surrounded on every side by dark blue water. Mountains occupied its northern region, dense forests covered much of the east, while enormous plains and rocky valleys divided the remaining landscape.","Michael had specifically chosen somewhere this large because of what he was about to do.","For several seconds, nothing happened.","Then the tattoos previously hidden on different parts of his body began to appear. One after another, they glowed, and soon ash poured from Michael’s skin, spreading several metres away from him to form humanoid shapes.","After their appearance was fully revealed, Michael turned to observe the eight standing in front of him.","Prince, Fade, Ghost, Lily, Spartan, Gale, Purple, and Blue.","Compared to the others, who looked to be somewhere within their early to late twenties, the latter two appeared to be somewhere in their late teens.","Eight figures stood around Michael.","\"Master.\"","Their greetings overlapped.","Michael nodded. He didn’t waste much time before getting to work.","Yes, Michael planned to evolve all eight. He would have done more, but he needed undead like Beginning to stay as they were in case of emergencies, and others needed to remain unevolved to maintain a certain level of strength, thanks to the passive states they granted him.","The island was large enough that each evolution could occur far away from the others.","Prince was sent toward the northern mountain range. Lily received a location within the western plains where there was little nearby terrain she could accidentally destroy after waking up.","Spartan was placed within an enormous rocky valley. Fade received a forested region toward the south. Purple and Blue were separated as well, despite the two normally remaining close to one another. Ghost was placed the farthest away. Gale was closer to the edge of the island.","It took some time to position everyone.","Once Michael finished, he rose high above the island. From here, the seven locations might be impossible to see directly with ordinary eyesight, but that didn’t matter. The entire Mausoleum was his. Michael could perceive every one of them clearly.","Evolution panels appeared before him one after another.","This was something he had already decided to do after confirming Lucky’s condition. Before today, Michael had still been somewhat cautious about pushing too many of his strongest undead farther along their evolutionary paths. Rank Five remained the greatest concern.","Lucky had changed that.","Three-Star Epic. Lucky had reached that level and still remained Rank Four. This made Michael even more aware of the gap between Rank Four and Rank Five. Simply piling evolutionary potential onto an undead wasn’t necessarily enough to force it across.","For Michael, that was excellent news. He had been restraining himself partly because he didn’t want to suddenly find himself surrounded by undead he could no longer properly control. Now that concern had weakened considerably. If even Lucky required Legendary grade to break through, Michael could afford to be considerably more aggressive with everyone else.","Michael began confirming the evolutions.","Evolution Points disappeared rapidly.","The effect across the island was immediate.","The northern mountains lit up as a pillar of energy erupted from Prince’s location. Several seconds later, another glow appeared far across the western plains.","Then another.","And another.","From Michael’s position high above the island, the scene became increasingly spectacular. Eight distant regions began shining. Different energies spread outward from each location as the evolutions began simultaneously.","Michael hovered above everything and watched.","* * *","A/N: Thank you all so much for the continued support!!! Seriously, it means the world and keeps me going on this story.","If you’re enjoying it, throwing a vote my way helps way more than you’d think, so consider casting one if you’ve got a spare!","Also, if you haven’t voted for the Shadow Slave event yet, please help out a little if it’s within your power.","More Chapters on the way, so stay tuned. Thanks for reading!"]},{"number":1205,"title":"Chapter 1205: More Evolution [2]","paragraphs":["Though none of the eight were evolving to Legendary grade like Lucky, Michael felt almost as much anticipation watching their individual transformations begin. Every one of them interested him for a different reason.","Ghost, for example.","Michael was particularly curious about how powerful it would become. Right from Rank One, it was already an abnormal existence.","Even among Michael’s undead, where abnormalities had practically become normal, Ghost stood out. After all, its actual physical strength was even greater than Beginning’s, who was a giant.","Now Michael was evolving it again. Though he could be almost sure it wouldn’t become a Demigod from this evolution, strength didn’t always correspond perfectly with Rank.","Michael genuinely wondered whether Ghost, after evolving, would possess enough combat power to contend with an early Rank Five existence that wasn’t specialized in strength.","And even if it couldn’t, in the Origin Battlefield he’d have another strong general in his legion.","Aside from Ghost, there was also Prince.","Michael felt a different kind of anticipation toward Prince. If there was one undead he regarded similarly to Lucky, it was Prince. Both had been with him from the very beginning.","Back when Michael’s understanding of Infinite Evolution had still been shallow, he had revived three Forest Wolves. Three ordinary Common-grade creatures. Unfortunately, only two remained today.","Lucky and Prince.","The third Forest Wolf had long since disappeared from his legion, lost in the battle in Hell.","After these two, there was Lily.","Lily’s evolution interested Michael for another reason entirely. Her race and grade. Michael wanted to know what came after Giant.","Alongside Beginning, the two of them had remained as Three-Star Extraordinary grade giants for a considerable amount of time, but an evolution of this level could produce a meaningful racial transformation.","Predicting the exact result of Infinite Evolution was nearly impossible. He could influence an evolutionary direction to an extent, but the final result depended upon the undead itself, its accumulated foundation, abilities, experiences, affinities, and whatever principles Infinite Evolution used when determining the most suitable path.","That unpredictability was part of what made every major evolution interesting.","Among Michael’s truly notable Rank Four undead, only these remained Extraordinary grade.","Because of this, Michael had a suspicion that though Lucky had proven that Three-Star Epic wasn’t automatically enough to enter Rank Five, that didn’t necessarily mean no undead could do it.","If Michael had to choose undead capable of breaking that boundary while still within Epic grade, Beginning and Lily were among his strongest candidates. Especially Beginning.","Perhaps One-Star Epic wouldn’t be enough. In fact, Michael doubted it would be. But Three-Star Epic? There was hope.","The Demigod ghost he had brought from the Netherworld was great proof of that possibility.","Michael wanted to observe Lily first, as her evolution would provide another reference point.","However, while Ghost, Prince, and Lily each gave Michael something to anticipate, what he looked forward to most was what evolution would do to Spartan.","Spartan was special for a reason that had very little to do with the undead himself. He was Michael’s experiment. More specifically, an experiment for Michael’s own future evolution.","During Spartan’s previous evolution, Michael had deliberately used a few fire-related Law Seeds as fuel. After all, undead like Spartan and the Undead High Drake were different from the others, as they didn’t have grades.","Evolution would not do anything to their rank, but if he added related Law Seeds to the mix, a change would occur.","Thanks to those seeds, Spartan had successfully crossed into Rank Four. More importantly, he had done so while evolving into a True Human.","That placed Spartan’s current race at the exact same level as Michael’s. Michael was also a True Human. And unlike Spartan, Michael had remained one for quite some time.","It wasn’t because Infinite Evolution had reached its limit with him. Michael knew he could evolve again. The option existed. He simply hadn’t dared to press it yet, as there were too many unknowns.","The first was secrecy.","The Mausoleum of Endless Dominion was unquestionably one of his greatest secrets, and perhaps in the future it would become impossible to hide. But even the Mausoleum couldn’t compare to Infinite Evolution. Anything directly connected to his talent was a life-and-death secret.","Michael could reveal powerful treasures. He could reveal absurd undead, and he could reveal abilities that made other people question where he had obtained them, but Infinite Evolution itself was different.","Before doing anything that might expose even a fraction of its true nature, Michael needed to consider the consequences carefully.","Until today, practically nothing directly related to his talent had been exposed to outsiders. The Evolution Essence Crystal was the only real exception. Other people had seen it before. Even then, they didn’t understand what it truly represented.","Lily was the only outsider who knew its actual function, and even she didn’t understand its true value or how fundamentally important it was.","Michael had no idea what phenomenon his next racial evolution would produce. Michael’s previous evolution to True Human had also been anything but subtle. If he evolved somewhere outside the Mausoleum, or if it couldn’t manage his evolution and produced an enormous phenomenon, hiding it afterward might be impossible.","Then there was another problem.","Time.","Michael’s last racial evolution had rendered him unconscious for three entire days. And that had been his previous evolution. The next one would almost certainly be more extreme.","Ten days? A month? Several months?","Michael had absolutely no idea.","The past three months had admittedly been the most peaceful period of his life in quite some time, at least before the Origin Battlefield revealed itself. There had been no desperate war requiring his constant presence, as even the unrest in his empire in the Land of Origin had been forcefully suppressed.","But peaceful didn’t mean Michael could simply close his eyes whenever he wanted and disappear from the world for an unknown amount of time. Especially now, when his Rank Advancement Quest had a five-year deadline.","**","A/N: Sorry for the previous update rate. We’re back to 2-4 a day. Thank you for the continued support!!!!"]},{"number":1206,"title":"Chapter 1206: More Evolution [3]","paragraphs":["With his luck, he could enter an evolution expecting to wake up a week later and somehow open his eyes four years afterward with his Rank Advancement Quest politely informing him that he had three days remaining.","The possibility sounded ridiculous, but Michael wasn’t willing to discover whether it actually was.","Then there was the third problem.","Evolution Points.","Before Michael took control of the Empire and gained access to its enormous resources, his accumulation of Evolution Points had been completely insignificant. Knowing he could evolve and actually possessing enough Evolution Points to do so were two very different things. Every major evolution became increasingly expensive.","His personal evolution had always existed as an option. Putting aside the fact that he had an entire legion to develop, even when he had a lot of Evolution Points to use, spending an enormous amount on himself without knowing what the result would be wasn’t something he could casually do.","After all, after possessing millions of Evolution Points, Michael knew he’d need three million points to evolve. Such a jump felt demonic and unreasonable to him.","After all, the previous evolution had only cost a few thousand. However, though he felt it was unreasonable, he could see a pattern.","Evolution to High Human cost 100 Evolution Points, and its performance could roughly be compared to a Two- to Three-Star Extraordinary grade creature. True Human cost around 2,500 Evolution Points, which could be compared to a One- to Two-Star Epic grade creature. This was 25 times the cost it took to evolve to a High Human.","Comparing the changes being a True Human brought to him, Michael could indeed say a True Human was worth more than 25 times a High Human. But what was three million?","That was one thousand two hundred times the cost it took to evolve to a True Human.","Though compared to monsters, who needed evolution more than intelligent races that could become Demigods even without evolving their race, making it make sense that monsters would cost less to upgrade, something Michael had theorized in the past, three million was still a huge jump.","This made Michael feel that perhaps his next evolution would be comparable to a Three-Star Legendary creature, or even better.","Would this evolution bring him into the territory of Myth grade?","However, there was no way for Michael to know, and the greater expectations made him even more unwilling to risk anything or spend a lot during his Rank Advancement Quest duration.","Unfortunately, with several crises now hanging over his head, Michael needed to start looking for major power boosts, which brought him back to Spartan.","If evolving himself directly carried too many unknowns, there was a simple alternative. He could test the process on someone else first. And Spartan was perfect.","Both were True Humans. Naturally, Michael wasn’t foolish enough to assume their evolutionary paths would be identical simply because they currently shared the same race.","Two creatures of the exact same species could evolve in completely different directions depending on their individual foundations. But Spartan could still answer several important questions.","What came after True Human? Would another racial evolution automatically push a True Human into something beyond Epic grade, or straight into Legendary? Most importantly, what kind of phenomenon would occur?","If Spartan’s evolution caused something so absurd that even the Mausoleum struggled to contain it, Michael would know to be considerably more careful when eventually attempting his own.","Before today, Spartan had been an experiment Michael wanted to conduct eventually. Now Michael could afford to stop postponing it.","His perception focused entirely on the rocky valley. Crimson light continued spreading between the mountains.","Michael had deliberately prepared Spartan’s evolution differently from the others. Prince, Ghost, Fade, Purple, Blue, and Lily were being strengthened because Michael wanted stronger undead. Spartan was being strengthened for the same reason. But he was also going first.","A pathfinder.","If Michael eventually intended to discover what existed beyond his own True Human race, he preferred seeing someone else walk through that door before him.","And depending on what emerged from the valley once Spartan’s evolution finished, Michael might finally decide whether it was time for him to follow.","However, for now, nothing was happening.","However, Michael wasn’t done yet.","His figure disappeared from above the island. When he reappeared, he stood in a completely different region of the Mausoleum.","It was far away from Lucky’s evolution and equally distant from the island where the other seven undead were undergoing their transformations.","Michael raised one hand. An object appeared above his palm.","It resembled a strange candle, though calling it one wasn’t entirely accurate. Its body was pale white with faint golden patterns running along its surface.","Heavenly Enlightenment Incense.","One of the three Epic-grade treasures Michael had managed to obtain from the Origin Battlefield. Among everything he had acquired there, this was one of the items he considered most valuable to his immediate advancement.","Its purpose was simple. Comprehension. Once activated, the incense could temporarily increase the user’s comprehension ability.","For Michael, who needed to somehow comprehend a Domain before even reaching Rank Four, its value was obvious.","Especially now, when Michael had also discovered a method of experiencing Ice Wheel through the Demigod ghost’s possession. Everything was beginning to align almost perfectly.","There was only one problem.","The Heavenly Enlightenment Incense was consumable. Once he used it, it would eventually disappear. Michael had no idea when he would find another one.","The Origin Battlefield might contain more, but there was absolutely no guarantee he would ever encounter the same treasure again.","Using it now could dramatically accelerate his progress toward comprehending a Domain. But once it was gone, it was gone.","Michael stared at the incense for several moments. Then his eyes gradually narrowed.","There was another possibility. A gamble.","Michael closed his eyes. His consciousness extended toward the Heavenly Enlightenment Incense.","It wasn’t the ordinary perception he used to inspect an object. Instead, he activated a skill he rarely had opportunities to use.","The one used to connect his soul to an inanimate object."]},{"number":1207,"title":"Chapter 1207: Finally Done","paragraphs":["\"It actually worked!\"","Though he suspected there wouldn’t be any issue in the first place, doubt still existed, since this was an item that had been mysteriously produced by the Origin Battlefield. Only the heavens knew if it had a locked grade. Fortunately, it didn’t.","Heavenly Enlightenment Incense","Grade: Epic ★★★","Description: A supreme treasure born naturally within regions blessed by the Origin Will.","Once ignited, the incense releases Heavenly Enlightenment Mist.","Depending on the quantity burned and the intensity of the flame, the user’s comprehension may increase by up to ten times.","Duration and effectiveness depend upon the amount consumed.","Just its current effect was already terrifying.","Even before meeting the Demigod ghost, Michael had placed enormous importance on the Heavenly Enlightenment Incense. At the time, he hadn’t possessed any clear direction for comprehending a Domain before Rank Four. Everything he knew about Domains suggested that attempting to create one while his Law Seed remained incomplete was practically unreasonable.","Still, Michael had been certain of one thing. Even if the Heavenly Enlightenment Incense couldn’t directly help him comprehend a Domain, it would significantly reduce the difficulty he faced in the future.","Ten times comprehension. That wasn’t a small increase, as such an enhancement could turn years of comprehension into months. For Michael, whose comprehension had already reached a ridiculous level after repeatedly improving his body and soul, the effect would be even more valuable.","He could use the duration to deepen his understanding of the Law of Echoed Existence. Even if he failed to make any progress toward his Domain, whatever understanding he gained wouldn’t simply disappear when the incense stopped burning. Comprehension wasn’t borrowed power. Once he understood something, it became his.","As long as the Heavenly Enlightenment Incense didn’t have some ridiculously short effective duration, Michael had always been confident he could gain something substantial from it.","But the situation was completely different now.","He had Ice Wheel. Through Divine Incarnation Possession, he could temporarily carry and experience the foundation of an actual Demigod’s Law World. The first use alone had pushed his Domain comprehension from zero to 2.5%.","Then there was Lucky. The comprehension phenomenon produced by Lucky’s evolution to Legendary grade was already vastly greater than anything Michael had experienced from previous evolutions. If the effect remained throughout the evolution, he potentially had days or even weeks to take advantage of it. Even if it ended soon, he’d just evolve another undead to Legendary. The cost was high, but it was worth it.","Together with these two, there was the Heavenly Enlightenment Incense.","*What would happen if he combined all three?*","However, Michael still wasn’t satisfied, since the possibility for a greater result was present.","*What would happen if he evolved the Heavenly Enlightenment Incense?*","Though the possibility it would turn into something else existed, Infinite Evolution only did things based on foundation. It wouldn’t turn a sword into a spear if you didn’t first hand it a spear to use.","This would be the same even if he evolved the Heavenly Enlightenment Incense to Legendary grade. At that stage, what could he expect? Would it be a longer duration at reduced efficiency, or greater efficiency at reduced duration?","The possibilities were many, but it was a risk worth betting on.","Fortunately, taking the gamble was possible at all, since not only could he link his soul with the treasure, but on his panel he could already see that he could evolve it. If the treasure had possessed some strange restriction, like a locked grade, due to being created by the Origin Battlefield or the Origin Will, there was a possibility that his talent simply wouldn’t have been able to interfere with it.","But the panel floating before him had eliminated that worry.","[Heavenly Enlightenment Incense]","[Epic ★★★ → Legendary ★]","[Cost: One Million Evolution Points.]","Michael stared at the number for several seconds. After spending one million Evolution Points on Lucky and then evolving seven more undead immediately, with one costing three million afterward, his previously enormous reserve had already suffered considerably.","Still, Michael didn’t dismiss the panel. Instead, he closed his eyes in pain and closed the deal.","The moment the choice was made, the Heavenly Enlightenment Incense reacted. The pale object erupted with light.","Michael’s eyes narrowed as the incense suddenly escaped his grasp and shot upward. Within seconds, it had risen hundreds of metres into the sky, leaving behind a long trail of pale golden-purple radiance.","Then the sky changed.","Dark clouds appeared directly above it. Black clouds rolled across the sky in enormous layers, spreading outward at a frightening speed, continuing to expand until they reached fifty kilometres.","Soon, an enormous portion of the sky had been completely covered.","The Heavenly Enlightenment Incense hovered at the center of everything.","Mana throughout the region surged toward the incense. The initial pull wasn’t particularly impressive, but its intensity increased with every passing second.","Streams of mana rose from the ground. The surrounding mountains began releasing accumulated elemental energy. Mana hidden within underground veins was dragged upward, while the ambient mana covering the region rushed toward the sky.","Michael’s expression gradually changed as it was absorbing even more than Lucky.","The range continued expanding as the incense indiscriminately devoured mana from its surroundings.","Michael immediately intervened. As ruler of the Mausoleum, he redirected several distant mana streams toward the region. The world itself responded to his authority, guiding enormous amounts of energy toward the evolving treasure.","Fortunately, this world was large and didn’t have a huge number of heavy consumers, so he had just enough to satisfy the consumption of evolving it to Legendary grade.","The Heavenly Enlightenment Incense swallowed everything. Its pale body was barely visible anymore. Only an enormous sphere of golden-white light remained beneath the dark clouds.","Michael continued observing and noticed there was something missing.","Comprehension. Or rather, the enhancement of it.","Lucky’s evolution had almost immediately produced that strange phenomenon. Michael’s mind had become clearer, difficult concepts had become easier to process, and his ability to comprehend everything around him had increased to a degree. The seven evolutions occurring elsewhere had also contributed to the phenomenon to varying degrees.","Yet the Heavenly Enlightenment Incense produced nothing, which was strange, since of all the things he was currently evolving, this should have been the one most likely to produce such a phenomenon. It was literally a treasure created for enlightenment.","However, though he was worried, there wasn’t much he could do, and there also didn’t seem to be any major problem yet.","Michael gave the enormous sphere of light one final worried glance and disappeared.","Just like Lucky’s evolution, he expected this one to also take a while. He only had one Legendary-grade item, which was this Mausoleum, and that had come from merging two items at the very peak of Epic grade, resulting in a swift creation. It would surely be different for the incense, and though he did not know exactly how long it would take, he expected it to be very little time.","Also, there was still one more thing he wanted to do.","When Michael appeared again, he found himself standing in another empty region of the Mausoleum.","Soon another object appeared in his hands. It was in the shape of an orb.","[Rune Annihilation Sphere]","Grade: One-Star Epic","Description: A disposable treasure created by compressing an enormous quantity of destructive energy within a runic shell.","Once activated, the sphere detonates after a brief delay, releasing catastrophic force over a wide area.","Effects: Releases a devastating explosion equivalent to the full-force magic attack of a Peak Rank Four powerhouse.","The explosion ignores most forms of ordinary elemental resistance. Effective destruction radius scales with the surrounding environment.","Restrictions: Single Use.","This was the second treasure he had managed to snatch from the Origin Battlefield. Compared to the Heavenly Enlightenment Incense, its value was admittedly lower. It was only One-Star Epic, but like the former, it was disposable. Once activated, the Rune Annihilation Sphere would destroy itself together with whatever unfortunate target happened to be nearby.","However, calling it less valuable did not mean it was weak.","Michael rotated the orb slowly between his fingers. He could feel the destructive energy sealed inside. If used properly, there was a genuine possibility of instantly killing a Peak Rank Four supernatural. Of course, actually accomplishing that depended on circumstances.","Michael’s fingers tightened slightly around the orb. Since he was already evolving everything today, there was no reason to leave this behind.","Michael closed his eyes. Once again, he activated the strange ability that allowed his soul to establish a connection with inanimate objects.","When the connection was formed, a panel appeared.","[Rune Annihilation Sphere]","[Epic ★ → Epic ★★★]","Michael confirmed the evolution without hesitation.","[Yes]","The Rune Annihilation Sphere reacted immediately. Michael instinctively released it. The orb floated several metres above his palm.","A pillar of dark red light rose from it before stopping several dozen metres overhead, and mana began surging toward it.","However, compared to Lucky’s evolution or the Heavenly Enlightenment Incense, the reaction was almost lacking.","Just the usual stuff.","The evolution was proceeding normally.","Michael gave the treasure one final glance. Then his figure vanished.","A moment later, he appeared beside the newly transplanted Nether Soul Tree."]},{"number":1208,"title":"Chapter 1208: Taboo Creature","paragraphs":["The moment Michael appeared beside the newly transplanted Nether Soul Tree, something cold slammed against him.","\"...!\"","A pale face appeared directly against his own.","Michael’s heart nearly jumped out of his chest.","The ghost had practically flown into him. Her translucent body pressed against his front while both hands rested on his shoulders. Her silver eyes were wider than usual, and there was none of the lazy calm she normally carried.","Michael recovered quickly.","\"What happened?\"","The ghost didn’t immediately answer. Her head turned sharply toward one direction. Then another. Her spiritual perception seemed to sweep across the surrounding region repeatedly, but the expression on her face only became more confused.","\"I don’t know.\"","Michael’s brows furrowed.","\"You don’t know?\"","The ghost slowly released him but remained unusually close.","\"Something is happening.\"","Michael’s expression became serious.","\"What?\"","She shook her head.","\"I don’t know. All I know is it’s something amazing.\"","After a bit more communication between them, Michael figured out that the ghost seemed to be sensing something taking place somewhere within the Mausoleum.","Something significant enough that even without seeing it, it had disturbed her. Yet strangely enough, she couldn’t identify where it was coming from.","Michael raised an eyebrow.","Lucky’s evolution was taking place extremely far from here. The Heavenly Enlightenment Incense was even farther away.","Michael had deliberately separated the major evolutions specifically because he didn’t know what kind of phenomena they might produce. The Mausoleum wasn’t some small spatial storage treasure either. It was an enormous independent world.","Yet the ghost had still sensed something.","\"As expected of a Demigod.\"","The ghost looked at him. Michael didn’t explain.","This was another reminder of just how different Rank Five beings were. At","Rank Five, the connection Demigods possessed was far deeper than that of a being like Michael.","Perhaps what the ghost was sensing was the rules of the Mausoleum reacting to the two Legendary-grade evolutions.","Fortunately, it was happening here and not in Aurora. Compared to the Mausoleum, where he was like a god, in Aurora he would have had to pray he wasn’t ambushed by Demigods from the demonic supernaturals’ side, since hiding evolutions of this level would be difficult for him right now without a storage treasure.","Michael’s gaze remained on the ghost for several more seconds before he finally looked away.","Only then did he remember someone else was supposed to be here.","His perception spread across the surrounding region, and it didn’t take long to find Isabella, who was standing near the edge of the prepared basin, partially hidden behind one of the black stone formations surrounding the Nether Soul Tree.","Michael’s expression became strange as she wasn’t simply standing there but was shivering.","The Skeleton Chief’s entire frame trembled faintly. Her violet soul flames had shrunk considerably, and both hands were wrapped tightly around her staff as though it were the only thing keeping her upright.","Michael turned toward the ghost.","\"What did you do to her?\"","The ghost blinked in confusion.","\"Nothing.\"","The ghost’s expression remained completely innocent.","\"She was like that after you left.\"","Michael’s eyes narrowed slightly, and he looked back toward Isabella before he started walking up to her.","The Skeleton Chief noticed him approaching almost immediately. Her violet flames brightened slightly, though the trembling didn’t completely stop.","Michael examined her carefully. There were no obvious injuries. Her soul flame was stable. Her bones were intact apart from the minor damage from earlier.","\"Are you fine?\"","Isabella looked at him.","\"Yes, Senior. I’m just glad you’re back.\"","\"...\"","Michael gave her a strange look before ignoring her. His attention returned to the ghost.","She had already floated back toward the Nether Soul Tree and was resting against one of its branches, but her silver eyes still occasionally shifted toward the distant horizon.","Michael shook his head and waved one hand.","Space distorted directly in front of him. The next moment, a figure appeared, and a boy stood before Michael.","He appeared somewhere around sixteen or seventeen years old. Long black hair fell loosely past his shoulders, framing a refined face that looked strikingly similar to Michael’s own, though noticeably younger.","His eyes were bright green. A long green coat rested over his body, tailored neatly enough to give him an almost aristocratic appearance despite his apparent age.","The moment his form stabilized, the boy looked toward Michael. He immediately straightened before placing one hand across his chest and giving an elegant bow.","\"Master.\"","Michael nodded. Before he could say anything else, the ghost disappeared from beside the Nether Soul Tree and reappeared directly between him and Jester.","Whoosh!","Michael’s eyes twitched.","Jester remained bowed for another moment before slowly raising his head.","The ghost floated inches away from him. Her silver eyes moved across his face before she started circling him. Jester’s green eyes followed her calmly.","The ghost stopped directly in front of him and leaned closer. Her spiritual perception swept across his body. Jester didn’t react.","Michael watched silently as the ghost’s expression gradually changed from curiosity to confusion, then something resembling mild disgust.","Her silver eyes narrowed.","\"What a taboo creature.\"","Michael’s eyebrow rose while Jester only gave a simple smile.","The ghost floated around him once more, examining him from another angle.","\"So wrong. Very wrong.\"","The ghost continued studying Jester for several more seconds before losing interest and disappearing.","Whoosh.","A moment later, she was back beside the Nether Soul Tree. Her body floated upward until she settled among several of the pale-blue Soul Flames surrounding its branches.","She leaned against the trunk, rested one cheek on her hand, and stared blankly into the distance.","Just like that, she returned to daydreaming.","Michael gave her a glance before looking at Jester.","Jester’s expression remained perfectly composed, though there was something slightly strange in his green eyes.","Michael did not think the ghost’s assessment was entirely wrong. Among every undead he had ever created, Jester had always been the strangest.","Whether it was his existence, his abilities, or even the way he behaved, Michael had encountered a good number of powerful beings by now. Yet very few had ever managed to reproduce the same subtle eeriness Jester possessed."]},{"number":1209,"title":"Chapter 1209: Demigod Corpse","paragraphs":["There was something fundamentally uncomfortable about him.","In that sense, Michael could understand exactly why the Demigod ghost had reacted the way she did.","If someone at her level could examine Jester for only a few seconds and immediately describe him as taboo, then perhaps Michael’s instincts back when Jester had first appeared hadn’t been exaggerated at all.","However, times had changed. Michael no longer regarded Jester with the same suspicion he once had.","The caution hadn’t completely disappeared. But somewhere along the way, Michael had accepted him completely.","Perhaps it was because Jester had never betrayed his trust. Or perhaps it was because he had repeatedly helped him. Or perhaps it was simply because of how deeply Jester had become involved with his family.","He spent more time around Aunt Mia and his sister than even Michael did after his awakening, not only protecting them but filling the void left by his absence.","At some point, Michael had even begun thinking of Jester less like an undead servant and more like a strange member of the family, without consciously realizing it.","Michael activated Detect, his gaze immediately moving toward Jester’s level.","\"...\"","Jester had dropped by four levels.","Michael’s expression didn’t change much, as he wasn’t surprised.","After all, this wasn’t the first time. Divination had a cost. Most of the time, ordinary questions or predictions only consumed energy. However, when Jester attempted to look at something significantly beyond his current ability, the price could become considerably heavier.","If the amount of energy required exceeded what he could normally supply, something deeper would be consumed instead, which in Jester’s case was his accumulated level.","Michael had seen it before.","The most impressive example remained Shojo. The result had been enormously profitable.","Michael stared at the teenager before him. Jester continued smiling calmly.","Michael didn’t ask anything. He didn’t need to, as he felt he had already gotten the answer.","There had been far too many strange coincidences throughout his trip into the Netherworld. Isabella alone was already suspicious. Thanks to her, he had been led through one valuable location after another. That alone could still be called luck.","But afterward? Everything was far too convenient.","Michael wasn’t arrogant enough to believe the universe simply liked him that much.","Still, Michael had no complaints. The result had worked entirely in his favour.","Michael dismissed the panel. Jester’s smile remained unchanged.","Michael finally turned his attention toward the actual reason he had summoned him.","The resurrection ritual.","Over the next several minutes, the quiet region surrounding the Nether Soul Tree gradually transformed. Michael and Jester began working.","Michael first cleared an enormous circular region several hundred metres from the Nether Soul Tree. After filling it with a huge amount of dark crystals and covering it up, the ground flattened beneath his authority over the Mausoleum until not even a single uneven stone remained.","Then Jester began placing materials.","Rich black crystals harvested from the Netherworld were embedded into the ground at carefully measured intervals. Grave Flowers were positioned at several major nodes, crushed into fine powder and used to draw portions of the formation. Michael personally handled the more valuable resources.","Line after line gradually appeared across the ground. Circles overlapped with circles. Runes intersected with geometric patterns. The final structure became increasingly complicated with every passing minute.","Isabella remained at a distance, watching silently.","The Demigod ghost had initially returned to daydreaming beneath the Nether Soul Tree. That lasted until Michael began drawing energy from the tree.","A thin stream of pale-blue soul energy flowed from one of the floating flames around the Nether Soul Tree before entering a channel Michael had prepared.","The ghost appeared beside him almost immediately.","Her complaints began.","Michael acted as though he had absolutely no idea what she was talking about.","Another stream of energy entered the ritual. The ghost complained again. Michael remained remarkably focused on his work.","By the third time, her expression had become increasingly dissatisfied.","Michael continued pretending not to understand the issue until the timing felt appropriate. Then negotiations began.","The result was surprisingly efficient. One Evolution Essence Crystal for four branches, which the ghost accepted.","Michael suspected the newly awakened hunger for evolutionary essence had temporarily destroyed whatever instinct for bargaining she possessed.","The four branches separated from the Nether Soul Tree one after another. Together with the branch she had given him earlier, Michael now possessed five. That was more than enough.","Michael processed them carefully.","Two were placed directly into four opposing sections of the ritual after being split lengthwise. The remaining three were ground down and mixed with several soul-related materials before being used to reinforce the innermost circle.","The effect was immediate, as pale-blue light began flowing through the formation. The lines previously drawn across the ground brightened one after another.","Dark energy mixed with soul energy. The two did not clash. Instead, the Nether Soul Tree’s material acted almost like a bridge between them, allowing the different forms of energy to circulate smoothly through the increasingly complicated structure.","Michael stepped backward and examined everything.","The ritual circle now covered an enormous area.","Three major rings surrounded the center.","The outer ring gathered and stabilized energy. The middle ring handled soul reconstruction and spiritual anchoring. The innermost ring was devoted almost entirely to the corpse itself. Countless smaller formations existed between them.","Jester stood on the opposite side of the ritual, making several final adjustments.","Michael carefully checked every connection again, and only when he found there were no errors he could detect did he relax. Considering Jester had also examined it, Michael was reasonably confident there wasn’t some hidden flaw waiting to turn the entire thing into an explosion.","The energy within the formation continued rising.","Michael walked toward the center.","Space distorted beside him, and a corpse appeared. The moment it entered the Mausoleum, the surrounding mana reacted.","The body of the female Demigod descended slowly before settling at the exact center of the innermost circle.","Even dead, she was extraordinary."]},{"number":1210,"title":"Chapter 1210: Demigod Panel","paragraphs":["Her body looked almost untouched by time. The skin retained its colour, and the muscles had not decayed.","Even the faint pressure naturally produced by her flesh remained powerful enough that an ordinary Rank Three probably wouldn’t have been comfortable standing nearby.","There was too much vitality for something dead. But Michael had already confirmed the truth repeatedly. She was dead. Completely.","Of course, he had made sure this was specifically the case the moment she entered the Mausoleum.","After bringing her into the Mausoleum, Michael had been extremely thorough. Every trace of consciousness he could find had been examined.","Anything that looked even remotely suspicious had been suppressed, removed, or destroyed.","Michael did not want to spend all this effort gathering resurrection materials just for the original owner to suddenly wake up halfway through and ask why he was touching her.","Now there was no consciousness remaining. The body was genuinely an empty husk. An unbelievably powerful empty husk, but an empty husk nonetheless.","Michael crouched beside her. His expression became serious. The next step required something from him personally.","Michael raised one hand. A goldish-red bead gradually emerged above his palm. It was his Blood Essence.","Michael’s face became slightly paler as the bead formed. He didn’t use much, as even a small amount of Blood Essence carried considerably more significance than litres of ordinary blood.","Michael brought his finger toward it. The bead stretched into a thin stream as he lowered his hand toward the Demigod’s forehead.","Carefully, Michael began drawing a pattern.","The pattern wasn’t particularly large. It occupied only the center of her forehead, but every stroke was deliberate. The symbol resembled several overlapping rings surrounding a central vertical mark.","The final stroke connected.","Buzz.","The blood pattern glowed. For the briefest instant, the Demigod’s entire body trembled.","When he saw there was no issue, Michael stood up and distanced himself.","Jester had already moved beyond the innermost circle. Isabella remained much farther away. Even the ghost was watching from beside it with visible curiosity.","Michael raised both hands, and the entire ritual circle came alive. Michael’s robes lifted despite the complete absence of wind.","Michael’s eyes locked onto the corpse. The pattern drawn in his Blood Essence brightened, and the innermost formation activated.","BOOOOOOM!","A pillar of black and pale-blue light erupted around the dead Demigod.","The pillar did not disappear quickly. For the first few minutes, it only grew denser. Black energy surged upward from the outer formation while pale-blue soul light circulated through the middle ring. The two streams twisted around one another before continuously pouring into the body at the center.","The pressure throughout the region increased.","Michael remained outside the ritual and watched every change carefully.","Minutes became tens of minutes. Then an hour passed. The ritual continued without interruption.","Dark crystals buried beneath the formation gradually lost their shine. The Grave Flowers withered one after another as the soul energy contained within them was extracted.","The powdered Nether Soul Tree branches lining the inner formation burned with pale-blue fire, but instead of turning to ash, they slowly dissolved into energy and entered the Demigod’s body.","Two hours passed.","Michael did not move. Jester remained nearby as well, occasionally adjusting the flow of energy whenever one section of the formation became unstable.","The ghost, on the other hand, had lost interest long ago. After watching the ritual for a while, she returned to the Nether Soul Tree and resumed floating lazily around its branches.","Only Isabella remained visibly tense. The more she watched Michael make his moves, instead of becoming more reassured, she only grew more unsettled.","She really wanted to know how this figure knew her father or what relationship they could possibly share.","Several hours passed like this before something changed.","The enormous pillar of black and pale-blue light suddenly contracted.","Michael’s eyes sharpened.","The energy that had been continuously rising into the sky began collapsing inward.","The outer ring dimmed first. Then the middle ring. One rune after another disappeared from the ground as the remaining energy was dragged toward the center.","The massive formation that had remained active for hours began shutting down section by section.","Michael straightened, feeling a little anxious.","Even the ghost looked over again.","The final stream of pale-blue light entered the body. Then everything stopped.","Silence descended. The remaining light disappeared.","Michael stared toward the center of the ritual. The female Demigod remained lying exactly where he had placed her.","For several seconds, nothing happened.","Then one finger moved.","Michael’s heartbeat immediately accelerated.","Another finger twitched.","A few seconds later, her eyes opened. They were blank, with no trace of the consciousness that had once inhabited the body. Only a new soul, created through Michael’s necromancy using the body’s previous foundation.","The woman slowly sat upright. The remaining dust from the destroyed ritual slid from her body. Then she stood.","BOOM!","The ground beneath her feet cracked.","Michael felt the pressure immediately.","Demigod. There was no doubt.","The resurrection had succeeded.","A smile slowly appeared on his face.","He had done it. His first Demigod undead. Not an undead temporarily pushed into Rank Five. Or an ally hired through Evolution Essence Crystals. An actual Rank Five undead belonging to him.","The woman stood motionlessly at the center of the ruined formation, awaiting instruction.","Before Michael could examine her more carefully, the ghost disappeared from beside the Nether Soul Tree. She appeared directly in front of the newly resurrected Demigod.","Her silver eyes widened with curiosity. She floated around the woman a few times, her spiritual perception sweeping through the new undead from head to toe.","The female Demigod did nothing.","\"Weak.\"","Michael’s expression twitched.","The ghost circled her one last time.","\"Weaker than me.\"","Then, having seemingly learned everything she cared to learn, she disappeared again and returned to her tree.","Michael ignored her.","Of course she thought the new undead was weak. The ghost was Level 112 with a Three-Star Epic race and had likely spent an absurd amount of time accumulating her foundation.","Michael didn’t know how strong she truly was, but he suspected even a Level 120 would struggle to do anything to her.","This undead had only just been resurrected.","Michael’s attention remained locked on the woman with excitement.","\"Status.\"","A translucent panel appeared.","[Name: ???]","[Race: Human]","[Level: 103]","[Trait: Blood Sovereign Physique]","[Skills: Blood Dominion, Crimson Regeneration, Blood Marionette, Scarlet Torrent, Blood Mist, Blood Sacrifice, Heartseeker Curse, Blood Clone, Crimson Prison, Blood Devouring...]","[Domain Law Technique: Sea of Blood Armour]"]},{"number":1211,"title":"Chapter 1211: Three Hours","paragraphs":["Michael’s gaze instantly dropped toward the bottom.","There it was again.","[Domain Law Technique: Sea of Blood Armour]","His eyes brightened. Exactly like the ghost. So it really was something associated with Rank Five.","Michael stared at the name.","\"Sea of Blood Armour...\"","Michael remembered what this Demigod had been capable of while alive. The enormous sea of blood. The way blood had seemed almost endless around her. The absurd regeneration. If Sea of Blood Armour was connected to all of that, the show of power made even more sense now.","Michael tried opening the information but got nothing. Just like Ice Wheel before he synchronized with the ghost, the system refused to reveal the deeper details. Or maybe it simply couldn’t.","Michael wasn’t disappointed, as he had expected not to get anything.","Instead, his gaze returned to the rest of the panel.","Level 103. Only three levels into Rank Five. That explained part of the difference between her and the ghost, but since she had a special physique, she should be much stronger than an ordinary Level 103 Demigod, given that she had been able to fight and hold her own for a while against his two enhanced undead.","Michael’s gaze moved back toward the top of the panel.","[Race: Human]","His expression gradually became strange.","\"Human...\"","Michael studied the woman again. She might not be a High Human, but her physique clearly compensated for much of that weakness. Michael knew how absurd it was.","The amount of vitality contained within it was monstrous. Even after sustaining repeated injuries from his temporarily enhanced undead, she had continued fighting for a considerable amount of time.","The Blood Sovereign Physique alone probably allowed her physical foundation to compete with, or perhaps even exceed, some High Humans of the same level.","But that was exactly what made Michael’s expression become stranger.","Comparable wasn’t the same as actually being one.","But what would happen if she became a High Human?","Michael’s heartbeat accelerated slightly. At higher levels, races stopped holding an overwhelming advantage like they used to, but their advantage didn’t disappear and was still significant. It just wasn’t as overwhelming as before.","Michael was just beginning to consider whether he should try evolving her directly when something appeared before his eyes.","A translucent panel unfolded without warning.","[Origin Battlefield Announcement]","[The Origin Battlefield will reopen in 3 Hours.]","[All qualified Awakeners are advised to prepare for entry.]","[Several modifications have been made to the Origin Battlefield following the conclusion of the previous opening period.]","[Details regarding these changes will be revealed upon entry.]","[Countdown: 02:59:59]","Michael stared at the panel.","\"...\"","The countdown immediately began decreasing.","02:59:58.","02:59:57.","His thoughts about evolving the Demigod temporarily stopped.","The Origin Battlefield was reopening in three hours. More importantly, something had changed.","Michael’s eyes remained on the third line.","[Several modifications have been made to the Origin Battlefield.]","That was vague. The Origin Battlefield hadn’t exactly been safe before. Only the heavens knew what difference this made now.","Michael’s expression became thoughtful. Three hours wasn’t much time for anything huge, but fortunately, he was already mostly prepared.","Michael’s gaze remained on the countdown for several seconds.","02:58:41.","02:58:40.","Three hours really wasn’t much time. But it was enough for something small.","His gaze slowly returned to the female Demigod. More specifically, to the first line of her status.","[Race: Human]","Michael’s expression became thoughtful again. He had already been considering it before the Origin Battlefield announcement interrupted him, and after thinking about the matter for a little longer, he couldn’t find any reason to hesitate, nor was he planning to.","He needed power. Inside the Origin Battlefield, Michael was practically untouchable, but if he wanted to give Aunt Mia and Lily their lives back, he would have to return to Aurora to check the situation.","Michael’s gaze returned to the newly resurrected Demigod.","A Rank Five subordinate was already an enormous improvement. But if he could make that Rank Five subordinate stronger for almost no meaningful cost, why wouldn’t he?","More importantly, evolving from Human to High Human was cheap. Ridiculously cheap compared to everything Michael had just spent Evolution Points on.","The Evolution Points required were almost insulting after watching millions disappear from his panel throughout the day. And unlike other evolutions, evolving to High Human didn’t need days.","Michael glanced at the Origin Battlefield countdown again.","A little under three hours. That should be enough. And even if it wasn’t, there was nothing forcing him to wait here.","Michael still needed to return to Aurora before the Origin Battlefield reopened. He also needed to speak with Lily. Perhaps by the time he finished that conversation, the female Demigod’s evolution would already be complete.","Michael made his decision, his eyes briefly shifting toward the Nether Soul Tree.","The silver-eyed ghost remained lazily resting against one of its branches. Her eyes were half closed. At first glance, it looked as though she had completely stopped paying attention to everything around her.","Michael knew better now. Her perception was terrifying. Friendly or not, contracted or not, there were some things he simply wouldn’t expose.","The ghost knowing about Evolution Essence Crystals was already considerably more than Michael would want outsiders to know.","His thoughts moved.","The female Demigod disappeared. Michael followed her location through his connection to the Mausoleum. He selected an isolated plain far from every other ongoing evolution.","Only then did Michael call upon Infinite Evolution remotely.","The familiar panel appeared before him.","[Human → High Human]","[Confirm Evolution?]","Michael didn’t hesitate.","[Yes]","Michael then withdrew his attention and turned toward Jester.","\"You’re coming with me.\"","Jester bowed slightly.","\"Of course, Master.\"","Michael’s gaze then shifted toward Isabella.","The Skeleton Chief was still standing near the edge of the basin. She had stopped trembling as badly as before, but something about her remained noticeably tense.","Michael stared at her for a moment. There was still the matter of her father. He hadn’t forgotten. But right now wasn’t the best time.","\"Isabella.\"","Her violet soul flames immediately focused on him.","\"Yes, Senior?\"","\"When I’m free, we’ll talk properly about your father.\"","Isabella remained silent for several seconds. Then she lowered her head.","\"Understood, Senior.\"","Michael nodded. That was enough for now.","As for the ghost, Michael didn’t disturb her.","With one thought, space folded around himself and Jester, and the two disappeared.","The region surrounding the Nether Soul Tree became quiet again.","Isabella remained standing where Michael had left her.","The ghost continued daydreaming."]},{"number":1212,"title":"Chapter 1212: Task [1]","paragraphs":["Day and night might be hard to distinguish in the Mausoleum, but in the house Michael kept his family in, it was bright whenever they wanted it to be.","Currently, Aunt Mia was in the kitchen making bread while Lily was meditating on the sofa when Michael and Jester appeared in the parlour.","Lily’s eyes opened almost immediately. Her meditation stopped the moment she sensed the two in the parlour.","She turned to look at them with an unmistakable look of envy appearing in her eyes.","Teleportation. It remained one of the abilities she wanted most. Unfortunately, every time she had asked about learning something similar, the answer had been disappointing. According to both Michael and Jester, spatial abilities were not something she could reasonably expect to possess anytime soon.","Lily didn’t doubt them. That didn’t make watching Michael casually appear inside the house any less annoying.","\"Welcome back, Cousin.\"","Michael nodded.","\"Thanks.\"","Lily glanced toward the kitchen.","\"Mom’s in the kitchen.\"","\"I know. I’ll greet her now.\"","Lily was already shifting her legs as though preparing to stand when Michael added,","\"Stay there. We need to talk.\"","Lily’s expression changed slightly, seeing the serious look on Michael’s face. She slowly settled back into her previous position.","\"Okay.\"","On the other hand, Jester gave Lily his usual polite greeting. Lily returned it without much thought. After greeting her, Jester quietly went his own way.","Michael headed toward the kitchen. His greeting with Aunt Mia didn’t take particularly long. As usual, her reaction to seeing him carried an almost perfectly balanced mixture of happiness and worry.","Michael reassured her as much as he reasonably could without explaining much. Some things were simply better left unsaid. Especially while she was making bread.","After spending a short while with her, Michael returned to the parlour.","Lily was still where he had left her.","Michael walked over and dropped onto the sofa beside her. His back sank into the cushions as his head tilted backward. For several seconds, Michael simply remained there.","Lily turned toward him and studied his face.","\"You look tired.\"","\"I am.\"","Michael rubbed his face with both hands before leaning forward.","\"The Origin Battlefield is opening again, but before that, there are a few things I need to discuss with you.\"","Lily didn’t look surprised. After all, Lily was an Awakener too. Just like Michael, she had been informed the moment the Origin Battlefield announced its reopening. She simply hadn’t considered it important enough to immediately stop what she was doing.","Michael wasn’t particularly surprised by that reaction either. Lily’s attitude toward the Origin Battlefield, from what he could tell from her return, was somewhat different from what he expected.","Perhaps it was because she had been exposed to someone like him for too long. Or perhaps it was because Michael had personally raised her foundation to the point where she was considerably stronger than most Awakeners around her level.","Either way, Lily didn’t seem to possess much fear toward the Origin Battlefield.","Michael knew that. And if he was being truthful, it worried him slightly.","Confidence was good. Lack of fear could also be good. But the Origin Battlefield was not a place where someone could afford to become careless, especially once others realized that killing fellow Awakeners could provide experience points with little consequence, since who would ever know or be able to find them in such an inaccessible realm?","Still, Michael didn’t want to destroy Lily’s confidence by constantly filling her head with frightening possibilities. He had already given her power, and Jester had trained her extensively using methods Michael knew were anything but gentle, or moral, to a degree. Lily had enough combat power to protect herself, so he decided to trust her. That was the reason he hadn’t spoken much after she recounted her last experience.","Michael straightened slightly on the sofa.","\"As usual, be careful once you enter.\"","Lily nodded immediately.","\"I will.\"","\"I mean it.\"","Michael’s expression remained serious.","\"The Origin Battlefield isn’t somewhere you should start treating casually just because the last time went well.\"","Lily’s expression became slightly more attentive.","Michael continued.","\"You’ll probably need to spend most of your time there if you want to complete your required duration.\"","Lily nodded again. That much she already understood. The Origin Battlefield needed active participation, and remaining outside for too long would only make fulfilling the required time unnecessarily difficult.","Michael leaned back slightly.","\"But needing to stay there for long doesn’t mean you need to sleep there. When you need proper rest, come back to the Original World. Sleep here. Recover here. Eat properly if you need to. Then return.\"","Lily nodded obediently.","\"Okay.\"","Michael watched her for a moment. At least she wasn’t stubborn about things like this.","Lily could be innocent. And if Michael was being less generous with the wording, somewhat naive. But she wasn’t stupid. More importantly, she wasn’t proud enough to believe being stronger than most people around her level made her invincible.","The previous Origin Battlefield opening had simply gone unusually well for her. A large part of that had been because of Timi. Lily had met him shortly after entering, and the two had become friends relatively quickly. Timi wasn’t much weaker than Lily herself, which meant Lily had spent a considerable portion of the previous opening travelling with someone strong enough that neither of them had to constantly protect the other.","Their journey had therefore been relatively safe. Michael knew she understood that.","The problem was that there was no guarantee things would happen the same way again. The Battlefield had already announced changes. They didn’t know what those changes were.","Lily might not appear near Timi this time. They could be separated by enormous distances. The dangers could be greater. The environment could change. The rules themselves might be different.","Michael had no idea.","Lily seemed to notice what he was thinking.","\"I know, Cousin.\"","Michael looked at her.","\"I got lucky last time.\""]},{"number":1213,"title":"Chapter 1213: Task [2]","paragraphs":["Michael’s eyebrow rose slightly.","Lily continued.","\"I met Timi early, and we stayed together for most of it. I know it might not happen again.\"","Michael’s expression relaxed slightly.","\"As long as you understand.\"","Lily gave a small nod.","\"I do.\"","Michael sank slightly deeper into the sofa. That handled the first thing.","\"There’s something else. Two things to be specific. The first is more important.\"","Michael looked at her for a moment before asking, \"Did you enter a Level Three region last time?\"","\"Yes. But we didn’t stay long. Timi said Level Two regions were already starting to become a bit dangerous for us, so going deeper without a need wasn’t worth it.\"","Michael nodded slowly.","\"That was the right decision. But this time, I actually want you to enter a Level Three region.\"","Lily’s eyes widened.","Yoo! Wasn’t he the one who told her not to go courting death?!","\"There’ll be risk involved, so don’t force anything. If the situation becomes too dangerous, leave immediately. I don’t care what you find there if getting it means putting yourself in a situation you can’t handle.\"","Michael hadn’t finished speaking when Lily suddenly leaned closer.","\"I know, I know. Hurry and tell me what you want me to do.\"","Michael paused. Lily’s excitement caught him slightly off guard.","What Michael didn’t know was that this was the first time she could remember him speaking to her like this. Not telling her to stay safe. Not giving her something. Not preparing protection around her. He actually needed something from her.","For more than a year, Michael had changed Lily’s life so completely that her first fifteen years sometimes felt strangely distant. Things she once worried about constantly barely existed anymore.","Money. Safety. Resources. Her future. Even her mother’s life had changed.","Unlike Aunt Mia, Lily wasn’t burdened by the same complicated guilt toward Michael, but she still understood that almost everything good in her current life had become possible because of him. And sometimes, quietly, she wondered what she had ever done for him in return.","Very little. Michael was always protecting her. Always giving. Lily rarely had anything he actually needed.","So hearing that Michael wanted her to do something for him produced an excitement she didn’t completely understand herself.","Michael, naturally, knew none of this but simply decided not to ruin her enthusiasm.","\"Fine.\"","Lily immediately focused.","Michael continued.","\"I suspect every Level Three region has something important hidden inside it.\"","Michael’s expression became thoughtful.","\"I can’t guarantee every Level Three region follows exactly the same structure, but based on what I saw last time, I think there’s a high chance each one contains a major treasure or something equivalent.\"","Lily nodded slowly.","Michael continued.","\"That’s what I want you to look for. Enter a Level Three region. Explore it properly. Find whatever the most valuable thing inside is.\"","Michael paused before emphasizing the next part.","\"If it’s too dangerous, forget it.\"","Lily nodded.","\"I mean that.\"","\"I know.\"","\"If getting it requires you to gamble your life, leave.\"","\"Okay.\"","\"But if the danger is something you can actually handle...\"","Michael’s eyes narrowed slightly.","\"Then make sure you take it.\"","Lily’s lips slowly curved upward.","\"Got it.\"","Lily’s thoughts had already moved elsewhere. Hearing Michael’s words made her remember the announcement from the previous Origin Battlefield opening.","Michael’s name had been broadcast to every Awakener. She still didn’t know the full significance of what he had done, but she remembered how unusual the announcement had been.","Perhaps this treasure was connected to that. Perhaps whatever Michael had found inside his own Level Three region was what caused the announcement.","Lily’s eyes gradually brightened.","If that was true, would her name be announced too?","The thought sent another wave of excitement through her.","Michael noticed the change in her expression and, after a brief hesitation, decided to ignore it and move on to the next thing.","\"Anyway, that’s the first thing.\"","Lily nodded eagerly for him to continue.","Michael rested one arm against the back of the sofa.","\"The second matter is actually related to Timi.\"","Lily’s eyes immediately brightened.","\"Timi?\"","\"Yes.\"","For some reason, Lily suddenly felt like several good things were happening today. First, Michael had actually given her something important to do in the Origin Battlefield. Now he was bringing up Timi on his own.","Lily leaned slightly closer.","\"Do you want to help him?\"","Michael looked at her.","\"And his world,\" Lily quickly added. \"They’re really pitiful there.\"","Michael already knew some of what she was referring to from what Lily had told him previously. Humanity in Timi’s world was surviving, but surviving was probably the most generous description one could use. People were still dying. A lot of them. Entire regions remained dangerous, resources were limited, and whatever disaster had transformed Timi’s Earth was still far from resolved.","Lily continued.","\"If you could help them somehow, maybe...\"","Michael immediately interrupted her.","\"Lily.\"","She stopped.","Michael gave her a strange look.","\"What exactly do you think I am?\"","Lily tilted her head in confusion.","Michael pointed toward himself.","\"Do I look like some omnipotent supreme being?\"","\"No...\"","\"Because you’re talking like I can casually save an entire world whenever I feel like it.\"","Lily’s excitement weakened.","Michael leaned back against the sofa.","\"I’m strong compared to many people around us, but I’m still human.\"","There were limits to what he could do.","Lily’s shoulders lowered slightly.","\"Oh.\"","Michael noticed her disappointment. He allowed it to remain for only a moment before continuing.","\"That doesn’t mean I can’t do something else.\"","Lily’s head immediately rose.","\"What?\"","Michael almost laughed at how quickly her expression changed. He raised two fingers.","\"That’s the second task.\"","Lily became attentive again.","\"If you meet Timi this time, ask him something for me.\"","\"What?\"","Michael paused briefly before answering.","\"Ask him to name ten popular countries from his Earth.\"","\"...\"","Michael waited.","Lily’s expression gradually became confused.","\"Countries?\"","Michael nodded.","\"The ones almost everyone there would know.\""]},{"number":1214,"title":"Chapter 1214: Let’s Grab The Ghost First","paragraphs":["Lily continued staring at him. Of all the things she had expected Michael to ask, that had been nowhere on the list.","\"What for?\"","\"I need to confirm something.\"","Lily’s curiosity only increased.","\"Confirm what?\"","Michael shook his head.","\"I’ll tell you after I know whether I’m right.\"","Lily narrowed her eyes at him, but Michael remained unmoved. Eventually, she gave up.","\"Fine.\"","Michael nodded.","\"Just remember them properly. Ten recognizable countries. Preferably spread across different parts of his world.\"","Lily committed the request to memory. She still had absolutely no idea what Michael intended to do with the information.","However, she had already pieced together one important thing. Whatever Michael was thinking about, the answer Timi gave might determine whether Michael could help his world. That alone was enough for her.","\"I’ll ask him.\"","\"Good.\"","Lily nodded seriously.","\"If I meet him, I’ll make sure I get the names.\"","Michael relaxed slightly. That was all he needed for now.","Whether his suspicion was correct or not would depend entirely on Timi’s answer.","Michael studied Lily for another moment before changing the subject.","\"What level are your two classes now?\"","Lily answered immediately.","\"Level Ten.\"","That meant both classes had reached their current limit. Level Ten. She could already attempt her next Rank Advancement whenever she wanted, provided she fulfilled the necessary requirements.","Michael nodded slowly.","\"Good. Do you remember what I told you about your Attribute Points?\"","Lily rolled her eyes slightly.","\"Yes.\"","\"Tell me.\"","Lily sighed but still answered.","\"If I can help it, I should keep them instead of immediately spending them. And if there’s an emergency and I need the extra strength, I can use them.\"","\"And if there isn’t?\"","\"I should wait until just before I advance to the next Rank, then use them.\"","Michael looked satisfied.","\"Why?\"","Lily stared at him.","\"You already know I know.\"","\"I want to hear you say it.\"","Lily’s lips twitched.","\"Because improving your attributes naturally becomes harder the higher they get.\"","\"Exactly.\"","Attribute Points were convenient. If you immediately dumped every Attribute Point you had into your stats, it would make your natural growth harder down the line.","Michael might not need this, thanks to his many advantages, but it was different for Lily. If possible, he wanted her foundation to be as strong as possible before each Rank.","Michael ignored the expression of annoyance on Lily’s face.","\"What was the other important thing I told you about Rank Advancement?\"","\"Don’t rush.\"","Lily continued.","\"If I can help it, I shouldn’t complete my Rank Advancement Quest the moment I satisfy the minimum requirements. And I should try to surpass them as much as I reasonably can.\"","\"Why?\"","\"So I’ll be stronger than people at the same Rank.\"","Michael gestured for her to continue.","Lily sighed.","\"If someone rushes through every advancement just because they can, they might level faster than me for a while.\"","\"But?\"","\"But it doesn’t matter.\"","Her expression gradually became more confident.","\"If my foundation is better every time I advance, I’ll catch up eventually.\"","Michael’s lips curved slightly.","Lily continued.","\"And when I do, I’ll leave them in the dust.\"","Michael nodded with satisfaction.","Rank Advancement Quests weren’t merely obstacles separating one Rank from another. They were opportunities. The minimum requirement represented what someone needed to advance. It didn’t necessarily represent what they were capable of achieving before advancing.","Michael reached over and rubbed the top of Lily’s head.","\"Good. You’re teachable.\"","Lily immediately tried moving away, but Michael’s hand followed.","Lily’s expression collapsed.","\"Michael, I’m sixteen!\"","Michael continued rubbing her head.","\"Stop treating me like I’m six!\"","\"You’re very teachable.\"","\"Cousin!\"","Lily slapped his hand away and hurriedly fixed her hair.","Michael leaned back with a faint smile.","Lily glared at him.","Michael’s smile widened slightly.","\"So dramatic.\"","\"I’m not dramatic!\"","Michael nodded solemnly.","\"Teenage rebellion.\"","Lily stared at him in disbelief. Then she grabbed one of the cushions beside her and threw it directly at his face.","Unfortunately for Lily, the cushion hit something. It just wasn’t Michael. The cushion passed through the space where his head had been a fraction of a second earlier and struck the back of the sofa.","Michael was already gone.","Several hundred kilometres away within the Mausoleum, space distorted. Michael appeared above an isolated plain.","The moment he arrived, his attention immediately settled on the figure standing below.","The female Demigod.","Just as Michael had expected, her evolution had already finished by the time he was done with Lily. The transformation from Human to High Human had never been particularly time-consuming compared to the absurd evolutions currently taking place elsewhere in the Mausoleum.","Michael descended slowly.","The woman stood silently where he had left her. At first glance, there wasn’t an enormous change in her appearance. Her body remained almost identical.","However, Michael immediately felt the difference.","Her aura had become considerably stronger. Before the evolution, her presence had already been enough to make most Rank Four beings uncomfortable simply by existing nearby. Now the pressure had deepened. It was denser.","The Blood Sovereign Physique had already given her an abnormal physical foundation for a Human. Adding the natural advantages of a High Human on top of that foundation had produced exactly the result Michael hoped for.","This was a considerable improvement. Michael suspected she could probably fight the enhanced Undead High Drake directly and force the battle into a genuine stalemate.","Michael slowly circled her.","He briefly considered comparing her to the Demigod ghost, but this was considerably harder. The ghost was a Level 112, Three-Star Epic creature. Her race was already exceptional, and the amount of time she had spent accumulating her foundation inside the Netherworld was unknown.","The female Demigod had only just become Michael’s undead. Even with the Blood Sovereign Physique and High Human race, Michael wasn’t confident she had reached the ghost’s level.","Perhaps she had. Perhaps she hadn’t. There were too many differences between them to judge purely from aura.","Still, even if she didn’t match the ghost now, she would when she evolved to True Human.","The temptation was strong. A True Human Demigod with the Blood Sovereign Physique. Michael didn’t even need to imagine too deeply to know the result would be ridiculous.","Unfortunately, now wasn’t the time. True Human evolution might still be relatively short compared to the massive transformations happening with Lucky and Spartan, but three days was still a considerable amount of time, since he wanted to enter Aurora before entering the Origin Battlefield to understand his situation better.","Michael stopped in front of her and observed her appearance for a while when a name surfaced in his mind.","\"Valeria.\"","The undead’s crimson eyes focused on him.","Michael repeated it.","\"Your name is Valeria.\"","The Blood Sovereign Demigod lowered her head.","\"Understood, Master.\"","Michael nodded.","Valeria. It suited her blooded appearance and abilities well enough.","\"Let’s go grab that ghost first.\""]},{"number":1215,"title":"Chapter 1215: Back","paragraphs":["Grabbing said ghost wasn’t hard. He just had to hand over another Evolution Essence Crystal.","Though this pained him very much, he didn’t feel it was a waste. But spending more than one hundred thousand Evolution Points in only a few hours was indeed painful, though. There was truly nothing better than having your own undead Demigod, but unfortunately, or fortunately, the ghost Demigod was special.","After all, with its possession skill, Michael himself could temporarily push himself to the Demigod level, increasing his own survivability.","After having the ghost hide inside him and reassuring Isabella again, he opened one portal connecting to one of the many hidden ones in Aurora and entered without hesitation.","The transition lasted only an instant before Michael found himself standing inside an enclosed cave.","Darkness surrounded him, but it meant little to his senses. His perception spread outward immediately, examining every corner of the underground chamber before eventually returning to the portal behind him.","The portal was stable, and the formations he had previously arranged around it were still functioning perfectly. Several layers concealed the spatial fluctuations it produced, preventing its energy from leaking outside the cave, while another formation continuously supplied enough energy to maintain the portal.","The portal was one of his most important escape routes. As long as it stayed hidden and operational, Michael could enter or leave the Mausoleum through this location without attracting unnecessary attention.","Michael didn’t immediately leave.","His perception penetrated the surrounding stone, spreading several kilometres outward as he searched for any unfamiliar presence.","Only after finding nothing did Michael move.","Rather than heading toward the cave’s concealed entrance, Michael stepped forward and sank directly into the ground. His body passed through the stone as though it didn’t exist.","A few moments later, Michael’s head emerged from the ground and stopped. His eyes swept across his surroundings before the rest of his body followed.","Michael had barely finished emerging from the ground when something separated from his body.","The ghost floated out from his chest.","However, unlike her usual appearance, she was considerably smaller, a deliberate choice on her part.","Michael looked at her strangely. Usually, the ghost’s humanoid form was roughly the size of an adult woman. Now she was barely larger than his palm, floating beside his shoulder like some strange spirit.","The ghost didn’t pay attention to his stare. Her silver eyes were already moving everywhere as she observed the sky above them. The distant mountains. Even the ground received several seconds of scrutiny.","There was obvious curiosity in her expression.","\"Is this one of the outside worlds you promised to show me?\"","Michael opened his mouth.","\"Ye...\"","\"There’s barely any mana.\"","Michael’s mouth closed.","The ghost looked increasingly dissatisfied as her spiritual perception spread outward.","\"The mana here is pathetic.\"","Michael gave her a look.","\"Obviously. It’s not the Netherworld.\"","The Netherworld was a higher realm filled with enormous amounts of death energy and mana. Comparing Aurora’s environment to it was hardly fair. It wasn’t to say it was little, but compared to the Netherworld or the deeper layers of Hell, it was indeed pitiful.","The ghost ignored his reasoning. She floated several metres away from him before suddenly stopping.","\"It’s also uncomfortable.\"","Michael’s eyebrow twitched.","\"It’s not the Netherworld.\"","The ghost turned toward him.","\"I know.\"","\"Then why are you complaining?\"","\"Because it’s uncomfortable.\"","\"...\"","Michael decided there was no point arguing.","Unfortunately, the ghost wasn’t finished. Her expression gradually became strange. She raised one translucent hand and stared at it before looking around again.","\"This world is resisting me.\"","This caught Michael’s attention as he turned to look worriedly at her.","Michael observed her more carefully. Now that she mentioned it, he could sense her aura seemed a bit restrained. It wasn’t particularly powerful. At least, it wasn’t enough to seriously affect a Demigod of her strength. But it was definitely there.","\"It seems the realm is suppressing you slightly as an outsider.\"","The ghost frowned.","That was the simplest explanation. Aurora possessed its own rules, and Michael already knew that outsiders at a certain level entering the world could experience suppression.","Still, Michael was somewhat surprised. He had always assumed this phenomenon primarily targeted intelligent foreign races entering a realm. Apparently, that assumption had been wrong.","Or perhaps it simply stopped mattering once an existence reached a certain level. At Rank Five, the influence a being possessed over the surrounding world was already fundamentally different from lower Ranks. A foreign Demigod entering Aurora might naturally attract the world’s attention regardless of what race they belonged to or if they were monsters.","It seemed that at a certain level of strength, a realm no longer discriminated. Outsider was outsider.","The ghost continued examining her tiny hand.","\"I don’t like it.\"","Michael sighed and comforted her for a few minutes.","The ghost looked toward the distant horizon again. Although she continued complaining, the curiosity in her silver eyes hadn’t diminished in the slightest.","It didn’t take long for her to return to Michael’s body.","With the ghost gone, Michael finally turned his attention toward why he had returned to Aurora in the first place.","He needed information. But the question was how to get it without exposing himself.","Michael stood silently for a while, considering his options.","He could capture someone from the Federation and simply extract whatever information he needed. Mind control was also an option. Finding an agent with sufficient clearance, controlling them, and having them hand over the credentials to their Supernatural Association account shouldn’t be particularly difficult.","There should be plenty of useful information there. Michael was curious about everything that had happened after his disappearance. There would definitely be some interesting information there.","Michael had his own Association account, but using it right now would be stupid. His device wasn’t even on him at the moment. If the Federation was monitoring him, which he was sure they were, logging into his account would practically be equivalent to announcing that he was back in Aurora.","Michael was still considering what he should do when his expression suddenly changed.","\"Hm?\"","Bright light appeared beneath his feet, along with a magic circle."]},{"number":1216,"title":"Chapter 1216: Kidnapped","paragraphs":["BOOM!","Several overlapping rings expanded across the ground, locking together as countless symbols illuminated simultaneously.","Michael immediately attempted to move, but nothing happened. His body hadn’t been physically restrained, yet the surrounding space itself seemed to have solidified.","Michael’s expression changed as he tried manipulating the void to escape, but nothing happened, yet again.","The Void was locked.","For the first time since emerging from the cave, Michael’s relaxed expression disappeared.","Someone had found him.","However, before Michael could panic, a small head emerged from his chest.","The ghost looked down at the formation.","\"Should I destroy it?\"","Michael paused, and his rapidly rising tension immediately eased.","Right. I’m not alone.","If the ghost was asking whether she should destroy the formation, then whatever had trapped him clearly wasn’t enough to trap her.","Michael looked down at the glowing runes. His first instinct was to tell her yes. Then he reconsidered.","\"No.\"","Michael’s eyes narrowed.","This might actually be useful.","He had returned specifically because he wanted information. Now that someone had gone through the trouble of finding him instead, why run? Michael wanted to know who was after him. More importantly, he wanted to know what had happened while he was gone.","\"Leave it.\"","The ghost tilted her head in confusion. Though she could understand the dynamics of the magic circle, she could tell it was one that initiated a forceful teleportation.","Michael continued.","\"But please pay attention. If whoever is behind this has something I genuinely can’t handle, don’t wait for me to tell you. Take over my body immediately.\"","The ghost’s silver eyes brightened slightly.","\"How many crystals?\"","The ghost began raising one finger when the formation suddenly erupted with light.","\"Wait, we haven’t...\"","Space twisted, and the two disappeared.","The sensation of forced teleportation disappeared almost as quickly as it came.","Michael’s feet touched solid ground. His eyes immediately moved.","He had appeared inside what looked like a basement. The room was large but almost completely dark, illuminated only by several dim light bulbs and the fading light of the teleportation formation beneath his feet. There were no windows. Only a single door existed at the far end of the room.","More importantly, Michael wasn’t alone.","Two figures stood several metres away. Both were completely covered in black. Long robes concealed their bodies while masks covered their faces, leaving practically nothing that could be used to identify them.","One stood farther back. The other was kneeling directly in front of the formation Michael had appeared upon, one hand pressed against the ground.","Michael immediately understood that this person had probably been responsible for activating the teleportation formation.","Michael’s perception spread outward instinctively, but it barely travelled several metres before stopping.","Locked again?","Thanks to another locking mechanism, Michael couldn’t sense what was beyond the walls or determine how deep underground he currently was.","They seemed pretty prepared.","That was the first thought that came to him.","The kneeling figure slowly raised his head while the standing figure suddenly laughed.","\"Hahaha!\"","The sound echoed throughout the basement.","\"Finally.\"","The kneeling figure stood.","\"Do you know how troublesome you’ve been?\"","Michael remained silent.","Fortunately, they were speaking the Universal Language. Michael understood every word perfectly.","The second figure cursed.","\"You disappeared to who knows where. Divination failed. Tracking methods failed. Even the marks prepared for you couldn’t locate anything.\"","Michael’s expression remained unchanged, but his thoughts moved rapidly.","Marks? How did they work, and why could they forcefully teleport him? The only other time this had happened to him was on his first day in the Origin Battlefield, and that had been due to a powerful Epic-grade treasure.","\"It was as if you’d completely vanished from this realm.\"","The man sounded increasingly irritated just remembering it.","The other figure chuckled.","\"Fortunately, for some unknown reason, you came back, saving us from suffering a loss on this mission.\"","His gaze travelled over Michael from head to toe.","\"As expected. You truly are just a brat still wet behind the ears.\"","The excitement in his voice became increasingly difficult to hide.","The kneeling figure laughed.","\"Without that army of undead surrounding you, what exactly are you?\"","Michael’s eyebrow moved slightly, but he didn’t say anything.","That seemed to make the two even more confident.","After all, according to their information, though this youth was strangely powerful for his rank, the greatest problem with Michael had never been Michael himself, but his undead.","Though the two of them were famous throughout the universe after countless assassination missions across hundreds of years, with not many failures, they were still only at the peak of Rank Four, with no path to the Rank above them anywhere close.","Attacking someone with a Demigod undead carried a huge amount of risk. Which was precisely why this basement had been prepared.","One of the figures spread his arms slightly.","\"You’ve noticed already, haven’t you?\"","\"The isolation.\"","The man’s voice carried obvious amusement.","\"Go ahead. Try and summon an undead. Even one.\"","He gestured toward the formation beneath Michael’s feet.","\"You won’t be bringing anything into this place.\"","Michael remained motionless. Before they had even spoken, he had already tried summoning his female Demigod but couldn’t. He could tell that if he forced his way, he’d be able to do it in a few seconds, which also showed how strong the method these two used was. But would they wait and allow him to do as he wished?","This was why he stopped.","In any case, he wasn’t scared. First was mainly due to the ghost hidden in him, and the other was because he could still use his Law. If he copied Wisdom’s Law, he’d be able to free himself from the lock and deal with these two, who he sensed and knew weren’t at Demigod rank.","However, before that, he wanted to know a few things.","Michael’s gaze moved between the two masked figures.","\"How did you do it?\"","*","A/N: Thanks for reading today’s Chapters! Please vote to support novel!"]},{"number":1217,"title":"Chapter 1217: Frozen Blocks","paragraphs":["Upon hearing his question, both figures became silent.","Then the one farther back sighed.","\"Why are they always like this?\"","His companion chuckled. He gestured toward Michael.","\"It’s always the same questions.\"","He began counting on his fingers.","\"Some start begging. Some ask how we found them. Some ask how their death came to be. Some desperately want to know who paid for their heads.\"","The second man laughed.","\"Occasionally, you get someone who spends their last few minutes threatening to kill your entire bloodline.\"","\"Those are entertaining.\"","Michael’s expression remained calm.","The first figure stared at him before shrugging. Perhaps because they were convinced Michael couldn’t escape, he didn’t seem particularly concerned about revealing anything.","\"Fine. It’s not like it’ll matter soon.\"","He walked toward the edge of the formation.","\"First of all, you weren’t even supposed to be our problem. We had just returned from another mission when we received a new order. Apparently, some rising star had offended someone some people shouldn’t have.\"","The other figure crossed his arms.","\"The pay was good, really good, for a target who was young and just a Rank Three Awakener brat.\"","Michael didn’t interrupt.","\"The information said you relied heavily on summoned undead. Dangerous ones, admittedly. But without them, from what we can see, you’re not much of a threat.\"","He laughed.","The second figure suddenly cursed.","\"Such an easy mission. Then your runaway ass disappeared.\"","Michael’s eyebrow twitched.","\"We came all the way here but couldn’t find you anywhere.\"","The first figure sounded very offended by the memory.","\"We would have taken a significant loss if you never returned. Fortunately, you eventually did.\"","Michael glanced down at the formation.","\"And this?\"","The first man shrugged.","\"That was the expensive solution.\"","He walked toward one side of the basement and kicked something. A pile of objects slid across the stone floor.","Clothes. Shoes. Several smaller personal belongings.","Michael’s eyes moved toward them.","\"We couldn’t find you directly,\" the man explained, \"so we stopped trying to find you.\"","\"We connected you to the formation instead.\"","The second figure crouched and picked up one of the shirts.","\"Things you’ve worn. Things you’ve touched repeatedly. Objects that have remained around you for long periods.\"","He tossed it back down.","\"Everything carries traces.\"","The first man continued.","\"Normally, that’s nowhere near enough to produce something like this, especially against someone with sufficient strength. So we used a treasure as the foundation.\"","\"A very expensive treasure,\" the other man complained.","The first figure continued.","\"The treasure established the connection. The formation amplified it. Your belongings gave us enough traces to anchor your fate to the spell.\"","Michael’s expression became slightly more serious.","Fate.","Thanks to Jester, Michael knew just how terrifying the matter of fate was. With it in the picture, something as ridiculous as this did seem possible.","The two seemed rather proud of themselves as they continued speaking, but Michael barely heard them anymore. His attention had settled completely on the pile.","There were several objects he recognized. One thing they all shared in common was they were from his apartment in aurora.","Michael stared at them, and he felt genuinely stupid.","It wasn’t entirely his fault to dismiss such a small detail, but against this bunch of experienced monsters who had lived for an unknown amount of years, he had indeed been careless and naive.","Michael felt a burning rage in his chest as his gaze continued moving through the pile. Then his expression froze on a few things there that weren’t his.","A piece of Aunt Mia’s clothing.","Another belonging he recognized as Lily’s.","Then Michael noticed several more.","His eyes slowly moved downward.","Among the pile were undergarments. They weren’t his.","Some belonged to Aunt Mia. Others belonged to Lily.","Michael stared at them.","His earlier embarrassment at overlooking such an obvious vulnerability vanished beneath something much colder.","Michael’s fingers slowly curled.","More importantly, another thought appeared.","If their method worked through personal belongings...","Could they have targeted Aunt Mia? Could they have targeted Lily?","These two could have dragged Lily here instead of him. Perhaps even Aunt Mia.","The thought of either of them suddenly being pulled from their home and appearing inside this basement before these two made something inside Michael snap.","The two assassins were still talking. Michael no longer cared. His gaze remained fixed on the pile.","When he finally spoke, his voice had become noticeably quieter.","\"Keep these two alive.\"","Both assassins stopped talking.","The one nearest the formation tilted his head.","\"Who are you talking to?\"","Michael didn’t answer.","Something cold emerged from his body, and the ghost slipped out through his chest.","She was still tiny at first, barely larger than Michael’s palm, but the instant she completely separated from him, her form expanded. Her feet never touched the ground. Long black hair drifted behind her as she floated beside Michael, and her silver eyes settled upon the two assassins.","The basement became cold as a thin layer of frost appeared across the floor.","The expressions beneath the two assassins’ masks couldn’t be seen, but their trembling bodies told Michael everything. The confidence that had filled the basement disappeared so completely it was almost amusing.","They were Peak Rank Four supernaturals. They knew what they were sensing.","\"Demigod...\"","The word escaped one man’s mouth as barely more than a whisper.","The other assassin immediately looked toward the formations covering the basement walls. His voice trembled.","\"No! That’s impossible! The isolation formation is working! So how is a Demigod here?!\"","It was then that realization struck the two: it wasn’t that the formation wasn’t working, but that the Demigod had already been summoned beforehand. Even before the circle appeared over Michael, the Demigod had already been inside him.","The ghost stared at them coldly.","Neither assassin attempted to run. There was nowhere to run, as they had personally ensured that the basement was isolated and the Void was locked. Spatial movement was impossible. Even their perception couldn’t penetrate the formations surrounding them.","Everything they had designed to prevent Michael from escaping now ensured that no one outside would even know what happened inside."]},{"number":1218,"title":"Chapter 1218: Fate Treasure","paragraphs":["One of the assassins took a step backward.","\"Wait. We can talk.\"","Michael didn’t respond.","\"We were hired! We don’t have any personal grudge against you. This was business!\"","The other assassin quickly added, \"We can tell you who hired us.\"","Michael’s gaze remained lowered.","\"We’ll tell you everything!\"","The first assassin seemed to become increasingly desperate as the ghost’s aura continued pressing down on him.","\"We’ve worked for hundreds of years. We have information. Treasures. Connections. Hidden bases. Anything you want.\"","The ghost’s head turned and looked toward Michael, apparently waiting for instructions.","Michael wasn’t looking at either assassin. His eyes remained fixed upon the pile of belongings scattered across the floor.","The longer he stared, the colder his expression became.","Michael had originally wanted them alive, since he wanted information, but the more he thought of the many possibilities that could have happened, he didn’t even want to see these two breathing.","Michael finally raised his eyes.","\"There’s no need to keep them alive. Having them in one piece is enough.\"","\"WAIT!\"","The ghost raised one hand.","Crack!","Neither assassin had the opportunity to do anything else.","Cold exploded through the basement. Frost covered both men from their feet upward. Their defensive energy reacted instinctively, but against the ghost’s power it accomplished almost nothing.","\"No!\"","In less than a second, both Peak Rank Four assassins had become motionless blocks of ice.","Silence returned to the basement.","The ghost did not immediately lower her hand.","Her silver eyes moved toward the formation beneath Michael’s feet. Then she casually flicked one finger.","Crack!","The magic circle that had required an expensive treasure, countless materials, and an enormous amount of preparation shattered. Several runes went dark simultaneously.","The spatial lock disappeared, and the restriction suppressing Michael’s perception collapsed immediately afterward, allowing his senses to spread beyond the basement for the first time since arriving.","Michael barely reacted. His expression remained cold as he walked toward the pile of belongings. He crouched beside them and placed them inside his storage space. He would sort through everything later.","Once he was done, Michael stood.","His gaze moved toward the two frozen assassins. The enormous blocks of ice remained exactly where they had been, with the two figures clearly visible inside.","Michael stared for several seconds, and his perception swept across them.","His eyebrow rose.","Their life forces were extremely weak, but they hadn’t disappeared.","\"They’re still alive.\"","The ghost looked at him and shrugged.","\"I can kill them now if you want.\"","The ghost continued casually.","\"They’ll die eventually, so no need to waste energy on something that just requires time.\"","\"...\"","Michael stared at her for several seconds, then he shook his head.","The more time Michael spent around this Demigod, the more he realized his first impression of her had been completely correct. She didn’t merely look lazy. She was lazy. Painfully lazy. It seems if something could be accomplished with ten units of energy, she wasn’t spending eleven.","Even following Michael around wasn’t some sudden burst of enthusiasm for exploring the universe. All she wanted was his Evolution Essence Crystals.","She was a crystal digger.","The ghost tilted her head.","\"What?\"","\"Nothing.\"","Michael looked away and placed the two in the Mausoleum.","With the two assassins safely stored inside the Mausoleum, Michael’s attention returned to the ruined formation. Or rather, what remained of it.","The ghost’s casual attack had destroyed most of it, but Michael could still sense something beneath the ground.","He walked toward the center of the ruined formation, crouched, and plunged one hand directly into the earth.","Crack!","His fingers tore through the stone and continued downward until they touched something solid. Michael grabbed it and pulled.","A circular disk emerged from beneath the floor. It was slightly larger than his palm and surprisingly thin. Its surface was dark grey, almost metallic, with countless tiny symbols arranged around several concentric rings. Michael could still feel a peculiar energy lingering within it.","\"This should be the treasure they mentioned.\"","Michael immediately recognized what it should be. The two assassins had said they used an expensive treasure as the foundation of the entire formation. Apparently, they had buried it underneath the center.","Michael wiped away the dirt before activating Detect.","[Anchor of Entangled Fate]","[Grade: Epic ★★]","[Description: A fate-related treasure capable of establishing an artificial connection between a designated target and a prepared anchor through sufficient traces of their existence.]","[The strength and stability of the connection depend on the quality and quantity of the target’s traces, the difference in strength between the user and target, and the supporting formation.]","[When sufficiently reinforced, the established connection can be used for tracking, restriction, and other effects.]","Michael’s expression became slightly serious.","\"Two-Star Epic.\"","No wonder. He had wondered how two Rank Four assassins had managed to forcefully teleport him without warning and temporarily interfere with his ability to summon his undead. The answer was sitting in his hand.","Michael turned the disk over. The treasure might only be Two-Star Epic, but he had personally experienced its effects and could not underestimate it.","\"This would fit Jester almost perfectly.\"","Jester’s Law was already deeply connected to divination. His abilities allowed him to glimpse possibilities, interfere with probability, and obtain information that should ordinarily have been beyond his reach.","Michael had always intended to eventually equip his important undead with treasures suited specifically to their abilities. The problem was finding suitable ones. Powerful treasures weren’t exactly lying around everywhere, and compatibility mattered almost as much as grade.","But this?","Michael turned the disk between his fingers. He could already imagine what Jester might accomplish with it.","Of course, Michael wasn’t giving it to him like this.","His gaze settled on its grade again.","[Epic ★★]","Michael’s lips curved slightly.","\"Two Stars is a little ugly.\"","Since he was going to give Jester a fate-related treasure, he might as well improve it first.","Three-Star Epic. That sounded much better.","Michael placed the Anchor of Entangled Fate into his storage space. Once he had the time, he would evolve it and hand it over to Jester.","Considering the four levels Jester had recently sacrificed through his divination just to help Michael’s trip through the Netherworld go smoothly, Michael felt he had more than earned it.","When all was done and he confirmed he didn’t miss anything, Michael had the ghost inhabit his body again before making his way up from the dark basement."]},{"number":1219,"title":"Chapter 1219: Sneaky","paragraphs":["Michael’s head emerged from the ground first.","He remained there for several seconds, his body still buried beneath the earth as his senses spread outward.","Above the basement stood an old, unimpressive house surrounded by several similar buildings. Beyond that were narrow roads, patches of undeveloped land, scattered houses, and considerably more vegetation than urban areas.","Was he in a rural area?","Though Aurora was developed, it wasn’t like the concept of rural areas or villages had disappeared.","Michael expanded his perception farther to fill capacity, and his expression gradually changed as familiar roads and sights entered his perception.","Michael finally pulled the rest of his body from the ground.","\"You’ve got to be kidding me.\"","He was actually in Brightgate City.","Technically, he was near its outskirts, in one of the less developed areas, but there was no mistaking it.","Upon entering Aurora, he had chosen another country, since he figured his home country would be quite the center of attention now. He didn’t think he’d be brought here.","Not only had those two broken into his family’s home and taken their belongings, they had actually stationed themselves not that far away.","Michael felt another wave of irritation.","\"What the hell is the Federation doing?\"","The two assassins were Peak Rank Four. That wasn’t weak. Rank Four beings were already important figures even on the scale of the universe, much less within an individual territory. Two foreign Peak Rank Four supernaturals entering Federation territory shouldn’t be something that went completely unnoticed.","At least, Michael didn’t think so.","The question was whether the Federation genuinely hadn’t noticed them. Or whether they had been permitted to enter.","Michael couldn’t confirm anything yet, but given his relationship with them, Michael felt the possibility wasn’t low.","\"I should also consider the fact that they underestimated me far too much.\"","At first, Michael had assumed they had underestimated him because of his age and Rank. That wasn’t exactly strange, as he was indeed young and only Rank Three, and most of his publicly displayed strength came from his undead. But there was one enormous problem with that reasoning.","Michael had beaten a Demigod to death.","Yet two Peak Rank Four assassins still thought he wasn’t special.","\"That’s weird.\"","Surely as assassins they weren’t stupid, right? Michael couldn’t help but wonder if it was because the Federation had controlled the situation afterward.","\"Did they suppress it?\"","He felt the possibility was high, since after exposing the Undead High Drake, he had expected his Rank Advancement Quest to also see some progress. But it got nothing, just like the case with Jester, even though this time they knew the undead belonged to him.","Michael stared at the sky for several more seconds before eventually shaking his head.","There were too many possibilities he could think of if he wanted. He didn’t have enough information to decide which was true, since some were indeed just nonsense theories caused by his lack of trust.","\"I’ll find out eventually.\"","For now, there was somewhere else he wanted to visit.","Michael hadn’t planned on staying in Aurora for particularly long, especially with the Origin Battlefield reopening soon, but since those two assassins had already dragged him back to Brightgate City, he might as well inspect his family’s apartment personally.","This entire situation had taught him a lesson. He had always known Jester’s abilities were strange and dangerous, but experiencing a fate-related method personally had made him realize just how vulnerable Aunt Mia and Lily could be to similar means.","\"I’ll have Jester check them when I return.\"","Michael was about to move when a familiar voice suddenly sounded inside his head.","\"My payment.\"","Michael stopped. He had almost forgotten this ghost’s greed.","The ghost continued from inside him.","\"You said if I...\"","\"Let’s calculate everything when we get back.\"","Michael continued before she could protest.","\"We’re not finished here yet. Something else might happen before we leave Aurora, and you might need to help me again.\"","The ghost remained quiet for a moment.","\"...Fine.\"","Michael could practically feel her reluctance.","Michael shook his head. He ignored her and looked toward the distant city.","His family’s apartment wasn’t particularly far from his current location with his present abilities.","Space distorted faintly around him. The next instant, Michael disappeared from the spot.","A few moments later he reappeared several streets away from his family’s apartment. His perception first swept across the neighborhood before settling on the familiar building.","After discovering no visible traps, Michael disappeared again.","This time, he appeared inside the apartment.","The moment his feet touched the floor, his expression darkened.","\"As I expected. This place has been tampered with.\"","The apartment was already in a somewhat ragged state, just like many buildings throughout Brightgate. The female Demigod’s actions a few days earlier had affected an enormous portion of the city. Although the worst damage had been concentrated elsewhere, the shockwaves alone had left their mark.","Cracks ran along several walls, and parts of the ceiling had fractured. From the outside, the entire building looked as though it had suddenly aged several decades. But Michael could distinguish that damage from everything else.","His eyes slowly moved through the apartment, and he could tell several places had clearly been searched and then deliberately arranged to make it seem as though nothing had happened.","He was currently in Wisdom State, so his senses were in an absurd state where even the smallest actions could be seen, and with his memory of a few days ago still very much clear, he discovered quite a few things.","Michael stood silently for a while before finally deciding that there was indeed no reason to leave anything behind.","He had first thought of maybe dropping a few undead to stand guard, since he had many Rank Four undead doing nothing or just keeping the house clean. But now he felt it was better to do the job properly.","Michael’s power spread throughout the entire building, and the entire apartment shook."]},{"number":1220,"title":"Chapter 1220: Help Me","paragraphs":["Rumble!","Then the building itself began to rise.","Walls trembled as dust fell from countless cracks. The entire structure gradually separated from the ground, but Michael was careful about what he took.","Whether it was pipes, electricity, or other utilities connecting the building to the surrounding infrastructure, they were carefully severed rather than ripped apart.","Only the building and its foundation rose.","Michael looked around one final time.","\"Good enough.\"","A second later, the entire building disappeared and entered the Mausoleum at once.","Where the apartment building had stood, only the exposed ground and disconnected utility points remained.","Michael disappeared immediately afterward.","What Michael hadn’t particularly considered was how absurd everything had looked to everyone else.","Since he had deliberately concealed his presence the moment he entered the area, nobody saw Michael.","One woman walking along the street stopped when she saw an entire building floating in the air without support.","Her mouth opened.","\"What...\"","Several other people noticed as well.","\"The building is flying!\" someone screamed.","Then, before their increasingly terrified eyes, the entire building vanished.","Completely.","Silence lasted perhaps two seconds before the street erupted.","\"DEMONS!\"","\"Run!\"","\"Call the authorities!\"","People rushed away from the empty plot while others stared from windows farther down the street.","One couldn’t exactly blame them for reaching that conclusion. Brightgate City had suffered far too much this year. The recent battle alone had left sections of the city looking like they had survived a natural disaster. At this point, whenever something spectacular and completely inexplicable happened, demons had become a perfectly reasonable first guess.","Fortunately for them, the culprit this time wasn’t a demon.","As for Michael, he was already several streets away. He found the panic somewhat amusing, but he didn’t have enough time to concern himself with this, as there was still something he wanted to do.","Michael’s perception spread outward. Among the ordinary civilians fleeing the area were several people whose reactions were noticeably different.","Michael’s eyes narrowed on them.","The Federation people, huh.","He wasn’t surprised.","Michael’s perception followed them and soon his attention settled on the strongest one. A middle-aged woman.","\"Found you. You’re perfect for now.\"","Her strength was comparable to a Rank Two Awakener and she could fly. With her ability to fly, she shot between buildings, already putting considerable distance between herself and the apartment.","Michael disappeared.","The woman had barely crossed another street when every instinct in her body screamed. Her head snapped around, but she found nothing, until she looked forward again and her pupils contracted.","Someone was floating directly in her path. Worse, she recognized who it was instantly.","\"Michael Nor...\"","Upon making eye contact with him, her body froze mid-air.","Michael drew closer.","The woman’s terror became increasingly visible.","Michael reached forward and grabbed the cusp of her collar.","\"I need to borrow you.\"","\"What?!\"","Space distorted, and the two disappeared.","* * *","The woman stumbled the instant solid ground returned beneath her feet.","Her eyes immediately swept across her surroundings.","\"Is this a basement?\"","Damaged stone covered the floor, while the remains of a complicated formation were still visible beneath them.","While she didn’t recognize the place, Michael did, as he had returned to the assassins’ basement.","Michael released the woman’s collar. She immediately jumped backward. Energy surged through her body as her translucent wings expanded behind her.","\"Don’t.\"","Michael’s voice stopped her.","The woman froze again as her senses came back. As someone in charge of monitoring Michael and his family, she of course had knowledge of him. While many argued the scariest thing about him was his undead, she knew their master was just as much of a monster as they were.","Her face visibly paled.","\"Sir Norman.\"","\"So you do know me.\"","The woman said nothing.","Michael wasn’t particularly surprised.","The woman cautiously looked toward the only exit before returning her attention to Michael.","\"What do you want?\"","\"Nothing complicated.\"","Michael smiled slightly.","\"I’ve been away for a few days. And apparently, a lot happened while I was gone.\"","The woman swallowed.","Michael continued.","\"So you’re going to help me catch up.\"","Over the next few minutes, Michael controlled the woman and had her hand over her phone before logging into her account on the Supernatural Association forum.","As expected, he was immediately met with an enormous amount of information concerning everything that had happened during his absence. Fortunately, there was nothing particularly surprising.","Numerous foreign races had indeed entered Aurora over the past few days. Some were human civilizations from other realms, while others belonged to completely different races. Despite the sheer number of powerful outsiders arriving, however, there had been no major conflicts between them and Aurora’s inhabitants so far.","Most people on the forum believed this was because the main target responsible for attracting them had yet to be found.","However, the situation surrounding him had changed considerably because of the information he had provided before disappearing. The possibility that Michael’s mysterious treasure wasn’t unique had spread among the outsiders. This revelation had significantly reduced the attention concentrated on him.","Several foreign groups had already left Aurora after confirming the information, apparently returning to their own worlds to prepare, while others remained within Aurora, either unwilling to abandon their original objective or waiting for further information.","This also explained the relative peace mentioned in the forum.","Michael continued going through the forum, searching for anything particularly relevant to himself, the Federation, or the events surrounding his disappearance.","Once Michael had gathered everything he considered important, he erased the woman’s memories of their encounter before disappearing from the basement.","Several seconds passed before the woman’s senses fully returned.","Confusion immediately appeared across her face as she examined her surroundings. She had no memory of entering the unfamiliar basement or any explanation for why she was standing there.","Her attention moved across the damaged floor and the remains of the destroyed formation.","She quickly checked herself for injuries before examining her belongings. Everything appeared normal.","However this only deepened her confusion."]},{"number":1221,"title":"Chapter 1221: Getting Closer","paragraphs":["The woman hurriedly tried to remember what had happened.","For someone at her level, suddenly regaining consciousness in an unfamiliar location with a gap in her memories was anything but normal.","There were abilities capable of manipulating memories, consciousness, and perception, but most were extremely difficult to defend against without specialized means. More importantly, anything capable of affecting her without leaving her aware that something had happened was almost certainly beyond her ability to resist.","That was the true source of her fear.","She forced herself to calm down and began carefully retracing her memories.","A name immediately came to mind.","Michael Norman.","She had been assigned to monitor his residence. Even with her relatively limited clearance, she knew enough about him to understand his importance.","Calling him the most brilliant individual Aurora had ever produced wouldn’t necessarily be an exaggeration, whether considering the period before Aurora’s introduction to the wider supernatural world or afterward. His growth was simply abnormal.","Unfortunately, Michael’s relationship with the Federation was complicated. The two sides seemed to constantly find themselves at opposite ends.","That alone wasn’t particularly unusual. Many powerful individuals and organizations outside the Federation’s direct command had complicated relationships with it.","The Federation couldn’t realistically expect every supernatural force within its territory to obediently follow its instructions.","Michael was simply a more troublesome case because of his potential. Someone progressing at his speed could very well become one of Aurora’s future guardians. That made monitoring him necessary.","Recently, however, her assignment had become incredibly dull.","For several days, there had been practically no movement around the Norman residence. Michael hadn’t appeared. Neither had his family.","Then, today, everything changed.","The woman suddenly remembered the building rising into the air before disappearing out of nowhere.","At the time, she hadn’t immediately connected the phenomenon to Michael. She had simply recognized that whatever could casually remove an entire building was far beyond her ability to handle.","Her first response had been retreat, flying away as quickly as possible, when someone had appeared directly in front of her.","The woman’s eyes widened as another memory fragment returned.","Yes!!! The one who had appeared in front of her had been Michael Norman!","He had appeared in her path without warning. She remembered him approaching and grabbing her by the collar.","And then... nothing.","Her memories ended there.","The woman slowly looked around the unfamiliar basement again. This time, the fear on her face was considerably worse.","As for Michael, he was already back inside the Mausoleum.","Although he would have liked to learn more about Aurora’s current situation, there wasn’t much he could do about it. His available sources of information were simply too limited.","Normally, Michael could have reached out to several people and slowly pieced together a clearer picture, but time was another problem.","The Origin Battlefield would reopen soon.","Michael sat near the edge of a mountain cliff, one leg hanging loosely over the side as he stared at the Mausoleum’s night sky.","There were no stars.","Instead, enormous curtains of green and purple light stretched across the heavens, occasionally mixing with shades of blue. They shifted slowly across the darkness, illuminating the enormous world beneath them with faint multicolored light.","Michael watched them quietly.","\"When I have time, I really need to create a force in the outside world.\"","His experiences in the Land of Origin had taught him exactly how useful having an organization under his control could be.","Originally, Michael hadn’t thought particularly deeply about ruling an empire. To him, the territory had primarily been something capable of producing resources and supporting his development.","However, the longer he ruled, the more he understood that the benefits weren’t limited to what the subjects received from their ruler. The ruler benefited enormously as well.","Information. Resources. Connections. Manpower. Influence.","There were countless matters Michael no longer needed to personally handle because others could handle them for him.","His current situation in Aurora was the perfect example of what he lacked outside the Land of Origin. Michael had returned after disappearing for several days and barely knew what had happened.","To obtain even basic information, he had been forced to grab a Federation agent and borrow her Association account.","If he possessed his own organization, things would have been completely different.","Of course, establishing something comparable to his empire in the real world wouldn’t be easy. But Michael wasn’t exactly starting from nothing anymore. He had thousands of undead, with an increasing number reaching Rank Four. He had several exceptionally powerful undead capable of acting independently, and most importantly, he had Jester.","With Jester’s strange abilities supporting an organization from the shadows, Michael could already imagine how useful such a force could become.","There was also another possibility.","If Michael’s suspicions regarding the Origin Battlefield were correct, then the Land of Origin itself might eventually become connected to the real world.","If that happened, Michael wouldn’t even need to build everything from scratch. He already had subjects and an established power structure.","Combining those foundations with his undead would make establishing a genuine force in the wider universe considerably easier.","There was another reason Michael wanted to try it.","His Rank Advancement Task.","Michael still hadn’t completely understood what the task expected from him. Creating a genuine force under his command in reality might finally allow him to confirm whether that was one of the requirements needed to progress it.","There was one problem with testing that theory inside the Land of Origin.","The Land of Origin was simply too large. It wasn’t divided into countless separate realms, sectors, galaxies, or other clearly defined territories where influence could be measured on increasingly greater scales.","As far as Michael understood, it was simply one enormous realm that bordered on seemingly endless.","His empire might seem enormous from the perspective of those living within it, but compared to the Land of Origin itself? It was insignificant.","Even establishing an entirely new empire and rapidly expanding it would affect only an unimaginably tiny portion of the greater realm.","That made it difficult for Michael to determine whether his Rank Advancement Task required influence on the level of a world, realm, sector, or something else entirely."]},{"number":1222,"title":"Chapter 1222: Velkaris","paragraphs":["The outside universe was different.","If Michael established a force capable of influencing an entire realm and his advancement progress changed, he would immediately have another clue regarding what the task required.","Michael remained seated on the cliff, considering several possibilities.","\"Master, I’ve found more details about what you asked me to investigate.\"","Michael’s thoughts stopped. He turned around.","Jester was sitting cross-legged several metres behind him. However, he wasn’t sitting on the ground. His entire body floated silently in the air.","Two severed heads hovered beside him, one on either side, both belonging to the assassins Michael had brought back from Aurora.","Jester’s normally unusual appearance had become considerably stranger. His eyes were completely golden.","Around him floated countless magic circles of varying sizes.","Some were barely larger than coins, while others stretched several metres across. They rotated at different speeds and angles, occasionally overlapping before separating again.","Strange symbols constantly appeared and disappeared across their surfaces.","Thin golden threads extended from the two severed heads and passed through several of the formations before eventually converging around Jester.","Michael immediately understood what he was seeing.","Divination.","Michael rose from the edge of the cliff and turned toward him fully. His attention settled on the two floating heads.","\"Was it necessary to kill them?\"","Jester’s lips curled upward. A quiet chuckle escaped him.","\"Master, you truly still have far too much light remaining in your heart.\"","Michael’s eyebrow twitched.","Jester casually rotated one of the severed heads with his finger. The golden threads attached to it trembled, causing several surrounding magic circles to shift alongside it.","\"For something like you, the dead are considerably more useful than the living.\"","His smile widened.","\"Besides, weren’t these two going to die regardless?\"","Michael couldn’t argue with that. The ghost’s ice had already reduced their life forces to practically nothing. Even if Jester hadn’t interfered, their deaths had merely been a matter of time.","\"Since they were going to die anyway, why make my work more troublesome?\"","Jester had barely finished speaking when something emerged from Michael’s chest.","The ghost floated out. She remained in her miniature form as she circled Jester curiously, silver eyes examining the countless rotating formations surrounding him.","\"As expected of a taboo creature.\"","Jester glanced at her briefly.","The ghost continued flying around him, occasionally moving dangerously close to one of the magic circles before shifting toward another. Neither Michael nor Jester paid much attention to her.","Michael went directly to the point.","\"What did you find?\"","Jester’s playful expression faded slightly.","\"Unfortunately, not as much as I would have liked.\"","The two heads rotated slowly beside him.","\"Both possessed restrictions within their souls and memories. The moment I attempted to reach certain information, portions of their memories began destroying themselves, and since you wanted speed, I could only aim to preserve what I could.\"","Michael wasn’t surprised. Professional assassins who had survived for so long would naturally possess precautions against soul and memory searching, even setting aside their natural protections.","Jester had still managed to salvage quite a bit before the restrictions completely activated, but most of what he discovered merely confirmed what Michael already knew.","However, Jester had uncovered one important detail.","\"They weren’t members of any organization.\"","Michael’s expression relaxed slightly.","\"Independent?\"","Jester nodded. They were essentially freelance assassins who had worked together for many years.","That was good. Michael would have killed them regardless, but at least their deaths wouldn’t immediately place another powerful organization on his list of enemies. Considering how many problems he already had, that was welcome news.","\"There is something more interesting, though.\"","One of the enormous golden formations behind Jester slowly rotated.","\"I couldn’t determine the exact identity of whoever commissioned your assassination, but I traced the origin of the commission.\"","Michael’s eyes narrowed.","\"Where?\"","\"The Velkaris Realm.\"","Michael immediately frowned.","Velkaris. The name pulled up an old memory.","Aurora had several neighboring realms, but two in particular possessed extremely poor relationships with it. Velkaris was one of them.","The reason wasn’t particularly complicated. Aurora was growing too quickly. Its introduction to the wider supernatural universe had happened relatively recently, yet its development had repeatedly exceeded expectations.","For distant realms, Aurora’s growth was merely something interesting to observe. For Velkaris, it was a potential disaster. The two realms were simply too close.","Unfortunately for Velkaris, there was very little it could openly do about Aurora’s rise without provoking consequences from other powers.","Michael’s expression gradually became thoughtful.","Perhaps the assassination order had less to do with the treasure he possessed than he initially thought.","The treasure had certainly made him a target for many outsiders, but Velkaris had another reason to want him dead.","He was from Aurora. More importantly, he was one of Aurora’s most promising Awakeners. If Velkaris already viewed Aurora’s rapid growth as a threat, then someone like Michael appearing would only make that concern worse.","A person like him was exactly the kind of existence an enemy realm might prefer to eliminate before he matured.","Michael’s eyes narrowed slightly. That possibility actually made more sense than someone simply placing a bounty because of his treasure.","Still, Michael wasn’t particularly interested in sitting around and guessing the exact motive. He had a name now. That was enough.","Michael’s expression gradually relaxed.","He wasn’t going there immediately. He had more important matters to deal with, and attacking an entire realm because of a suspicion would be idiotic. He needed to confirm exactly who had issued the commission and whether it represented an individual faction or something larger.","But eventually?","Michael would visit.","A friendly visit.","Whether it remained friendly afterward would depend entirely on what he discovered.","Jester watched him silently. The ghost was still floating around the surrounding magic circles, occasionally poking one with a translucent finger before pulling back when the formation reacted.","Michael was about to ask Jester something else when a familiar translucent panel suddenly appeared before him.","[Origin Battlefield Notice]","[The Origin Battlefield will become accessible in 10 Minutes.]","[All Awakeners are advised to prepare.]","[Countdown: 00:09:59]","Michael’s attention immediately shifted.","The time had finally come.","Whatever thoughts he had about Velkaris could wait.","The Origin Battlefield was opening again.","***","A/N: Mass Release next update. Thank you for the continued support!!"]},{"number":1223,"title":"Chapter 1223: New Feeling","paragraphs":["The notification remained in front of Michael, its countdown steadily decreasing.","Seeing it, Michael knew it was finally time to leave his current matters behind.","Velkaris, the assassins, the Federation, and everything happening in Aurora could wait. The Origin Battlefield was far more important, especially considering what had happened during his previous visit. There were many things he wanted to confirm but didn’t have the time to.","Michael shook his head and turned toward the two severed heads floating beside Jester.","With a thought, both disappeared into his storage space. Their bodies were already there as well.","Michael intended to revive the two assassins as undead. Unfortunately, there wasn’t enough time to do that now. Not that it mattered, since nothing prevented Michael from reviving them after entering the Origin Battlefield.","Michael then waved his hand toward Jester.","The next instant, Jester disappeared along with the countless golden formations.","Michael had sent him directly back to his family.","Though there was no need for Jester to constantly be with them, since this was his world and Jester had already confirmed that with the death of the two assassins, any ill fate they had was gone, he still had a family role to perform now and comfort Aunt Mia when needed.","Michael’s attention returned to the countdown.","[00:08:47]","The ghost, who had been floating nearby, looked around as though searching for something else that might interest her.","Finding nothing, her translucent body drifted toward Michael. Without saying anything, she passed directly through his chest and disappeared back inside his body.","Michael didn’t stop her.","After they returned to the Mausoleum, Michael had eventually paid her one Evolution Essence Crystal. Though she wished for more, the ghost had accepted it happily enough.","Michael had expected her to immediately return to the enormous tree she usually inhabited afterward. Instead, she had simply entered his body again and shown absolutely no intention of leaving.","Michael had asked why, and the answer had been surprisingly simple. His body was comfortable.","Michael could only assume this was another effect of Death’s Heir. His class naturally possessed an extremely high affinity with death-related existences. The Netherworld itself had already demonstrated that.","Apparently, that compatibility worked both ways. For the ghost, perhaps inhabiting Michael’s body seemed almost as comfortable as remaining within a suitable spiritual vessel. Perhaps this was why their harmony rate was so high, despite the two of them being at odds whenever they spoke.","Michael still found the situation somewhat strange. There was something inherently odd about knowing a fully conscious Demigod was casually living inside his body.","Still, he didn’t refuse.","If anything, keeping her nearby was convenient. There was something else he wanted to test once the Origin Battlefield opened: whether he could bring the ghost with him.","If she could enter alongside him, that would undoubtedly be useful. Keeping her inside his body was also considerably better than sending her back to the tree.","Otherwise, Michael could already imagine what would happen the next time he needed her. He would have to travel over, convince her to leave, and probably listen to another negotiation regarding how many Evolution Essence Crystals every individual action would cost.","This was much simpler.","Michael remained still for several seconds before another thought suddenly occurred to him.","\"Hey.\"","The ghost responded from somewhere within his body.","\"What?\"","\"I need to give you a name.\"","There was a short silence.","\"That has nothing to do with me.\"","Michael’s lips twitched.","\"It feels strange constantly referring to you as ’the ghost,’ even inside my head.\"","\"I don’t care.\"","Michael ignored her lack of interest.","\"Do you actually have a name?\"","This time, the ghost took slightly longer to respond.","\"No.\"","Michael’s expression changed slightly.","He had expected her to simply refuse to tell him, but she genuinely didn’t possess one. Considering how old she was, that was somewhat surprising, since even intelligent monsters, after a period of time, liked to give themselves a name. It might not be a good one, but it increased their sense of self.","Michael thought for a moment.","\"Then I’ll give you one.\"","\"How much?\"","\"What?\"","\"If you want me to accept a name, you have to pay.\"","\"...\"","Michael stared blankly into the distance.","This woman was unbelievable.","\"No.\"","\"Then I don’t need one.\"","Michael completely ignored her.","He considered several possibilities before settling on one.","\"Lunara.\"","Michael nodded to himself.","\"Lunara. That’s your name from now on.\"","A translucent head suddenly emerged from his chest. The ghost stared directly at him.","\"I didn’t agree.\"","\"You don’t have to.\"","\"Then it isn’t my name.\"","\"It is to me.\"","The ghost’s silver eyes narrowed. Michael calmly stared back at her.","\"Unless you already have another name, I’m calling you Lunara.\"","\"I told you. I don’t have one.\"","\"Perfect. No conflict, then.\"","The ghost stared at him for several seconds before slowly sinking back into his body.","A sudden chill spread through Michael’s chest. He barely had time to react before the cold rushed upward through his throat.","Michael’s expression changed.","\"Cough!\"","Something shot out of his mouth and struck the ground several metres away.","Michael stared at it.","It was a block of ice. Not a shard or a few frozen particles, but an actual baby fist-sized block of solid ice.","\"...\"","Michael slowly lowered his gaze toward his chest. There was no response from Lunara.","Michael said nothing. Instead, after several seconds, a smile slowly appeared on his face.","This is.... new.","His undead had always possessed different personalities. Lucky had his strange obsession with plants. Lily was gluttonous. Beginning had his own peculiarities, while Jester was practically impossible to describe normally.","However, none of them interacted with Michael quite like this.","Perhaps it was because Lunara wasn’t technically his undead yet. Their relationship was considerably less defined. She didn’t treat him as a master, nor did she possess the instinctive obedience most of his undead had toward him.","If she disliked something, she showed it.","Michael found the experience strangely refreshing.","Fun, even.","His smile remained as he looked toward the panel.","[00:03:21]"]},{"number":1224,"title":"Chapter 1224: Restriction and Poverty [1]","paragraphs":["There wasn’t much left for him to do.","Michael sat back down near the edge of the cliff and waited.","The enormous auroras continued flowing through the starless sky above him. Green, purple, and blue light slowly shifted across the heavens while the countdown steadily approached zero.","[00:01:00]","Michael rose. His expression became serious.","[00:00:10]","[00:00:09]","[00:00:08]","Michael checked everything one final time. His preparations were complete.","[00:00:03]","[00:00:02]","[00:00:01]","[Origin Battlefield is now accessible.]","The moment the notification appeared, countless points of light emerged around Michael’s body. They rapidly multiplied, covering him from head to toe.","Michael glanced down as his fingers began dissolving into tiny particles. The effect quickly spread across his arms, chest, and eventually his entire body.","A second later, Michael completely disappeared from the mountain cliff in a shower of light.","However, Michael did not immediately find himself inside the Origin Battlefield.","The sensation of teleportation disappeared, and when his vision returned, Michael found himself standing inside an enormous white room.","There were no doors, windows, decorations, or even visible corners. White extended in every direction, making it difficult to judge the actual size of the place.","Michael immediately became alert. His perception spread outward, but before he could properly investigate his surroundings, something floating several metres ahead caught his attention.","Michael blinked.","\"Lunara?\"","The ghost was no longer inside his body.","Her miniature figure floated within a translucent blue bubble roughly a metre across. She seemed completely unharmed, but the bubble prevented her from moving beyond its boundaries.","Lunara pressed one hand against its surface before looking toward Michael. Her expression wasn’t particularly concerned. If anything, she seemed mildly curious.","Michael was about to approach when a translucent panel appeared directly before him.","[Origin Battlefield Entry Inspection]","[Warning!]","[A higher-ranked lifeform has been detected accompanying the Awakener.]","[Current Destination: Fourth Layer]","[The detected lifeform exceeds the maximum level of power permitted within the Fourth Layer.]","[Entry in its current state is prohibited.]","Michael’s eyes narrowed slightly.","So it had actually worked.","He had always wondered what would happen if he had a Rank Five undead. Would he be forced into a higher layer, or would something else happen?","It seemed it was the latter that had just happened. Whether this would be different for the Fourth Layer specifically was something Michael did not know. What he guessed, however, was that his previous case might have been caused by his own personal power rather than his undead when it came to the decision.","Perhaps if he himself hadn’t been so ridiculous, and only his undead were above him in every form, he would still have remained in the Third Layer. The theory also explained why an Angel who was at Rank Three had been in the Fourth Layer as well but couldn’t match him.","As several thoughts flashed past Michael’s head, more lines appeared.","[Detected Lifeform: Special Spiritual Undead]","[Rank: Rank 5]","[The accompanying lifeform may enter the Fourth Layer under Forced Suppression.]","[Forced Suppression will restrict the lifeform’s accessible strength to the maximum level permitted within the Fourth Layer.]","[Suppression Fee: 50,000 Origin Points per hour.]","[Alternative Entry Permit: 1,000,000 Origin Points.]","[Duration: 24 Hours.]","[During the permit period, Forced Suppression will remain continuously active.]","Michael’s expression immediately became strange.","One million Origin Points.","This wasn’t cheap in any form. This was the first time Michael had seen Origin Points used again, outside of when he was operating his Universal Cornerstone.","At that time, he had to sell a Rare-grade herb for a measly 239 Origin Points. To reach one million, he’d need to sell a bit above four thousand Rare-grade herbs to afford using a suppressed Demigod in the Origin Battlefield for a day.","Even the cheaper option, 50,000 points per hour, wasn’t cheap either, since it was about how much he’d need to buy just the basic knowledge of the Elven race’s language.","Michael didn’t think it was worth it for him. Yes, Lunara was powerful, but suppressed a rank below, Michael didn’t think she’d necessarily be better than some of his undead.","Michael continued reading.","[If the Awakener does not wish to purchase Forced Suppression, the accompanying lifeform will remain temporarily detained within the Entry Inspection Space.]","[The accompanying lifeform will not be harmed.]","[The Awakener may retrieve the accompanying lifeform upon leaving the Origin Battlefield.]","[Please Select:]","[Hourly Suppression: 50,000 Origin Points/Hour]","[24-Hour Permit: 1,000,000 Origin Points]","[Temporary Detainment: Free]","[Origin points balance: Two hundred and thirty nine points]","Michael stared at the three choices.","His gaze slowly moved from the panel toward Lunara. The ghost was still floating comfortably inside the blue bubble, apparently completely unconcerned about being detained by the Origin Battlefield.","Michael, however, became thoughtful.","This is interesting.","The fact that Lunara could enter at all meant the Origin Battlefield wasn’t limited strictly to Awakeners and their contracted creatures. As long as they had a means like his, they could do the same.","There was something even more important about the appearance of Origin Points here.","As far as Michael knew, no other Awakener in the universe should even be aware that Origin Points existed. Michael himself had only discovered them because of the Universal Cornerstone. More importantly, the Universal Cornerstone remained the only method he knew of obtaining Origin Points. By selling resources to it, practically anything with sufficient value could be converted into Origin Points.","Michael’s expression gradually became serious.","The Origin Battlefield recognizing the same currency couldn’t possibly be a coincidence. If anything, it indirectly confirmed that the Universal Cornerstone possessed some deeper relationship with the Origin Battlefield.","Michael had already known the cornerstone was ridiculously valuable. But perhaps he had still underestimated its importance.","Michael glanced toward his miserable balance.","[Origin Points Balance: 239]","He had barely explored the functions of the Universal Cornerstone before everything started happening.","Such a possibility made Michael think about something else.","His gaze returned to Lunara."]},{"number":1225,"title":"Chapter 1225: Restriction and Poverty [2]","paragraphs":["If he could bring a Rank Five existence into the Fourth Layer by paying Origin Points, then others should be capable of doing the same.","That wasn’t particularly comforting, since he knew that while it might not be easy for others to claim a cornerstone like his, they would eventually do so.","Michael’s expression became thoughtful.","Fortunately, there was no reason to worry about that possibility yet.","He looked around the enormous white space again. There was no exchange platform or option to convert ordinary resources into Origin Points. The only choices presented to him concerned Lunara’s entry.","If another Awakener somehow arrived here with a higher-ranked companion but possessed no Origin Points, they would probably be forced to leave that companion behind. And if Michael’s current understanding was correct, the Universal Cornerstone remained the only known method available to him for obtaining Origin Points.","Michael’s eyes narrowed slightly.","That made possessing the cornerstone even more significant. It potentially gave him access to an entire currency system that the Origin Battlefield itself recognized. Perhaps, in a few years from now, this would be the supreme currency across the whole universe.","Michael stored that information away mentally. There was far too much he still didn’t understand.","For now, however, his situation was embarrassingly simple.","Michael looked at his balance again.","[239 Origin Points]","Then at the cheapest option.","[Hourly Suppression: 50,000 Origin Points/Hour]","\"...\"","Even if Michael wanted Lunara accompanying him, he couldn’t afford to keep her inside the Fourth Layer for even a minute.","His gaze moved toward the final option.","[Temporary Detainment: Free]","Michael’s expression relaxed.","At least poverty had made the decision easy.","Michael looked toward Lunara again. She floated lazily inside the blue bubble, occasionally pressing against its surface as though testing what exactly was keeping her contained.","Michael walked closer.","\"I need to go somewhere else for a while.\"","Lunara looked at him.","\"I’ll be back soon. You can stay here until then.\"","Michael had half expected some complaint, especially considering he had been the one to bring her along in the first place. Surprisingly, none came.","Lunara simply nodded. Perhaps from her perspective, waiting here for a while wasn’t particularly different from spending years inside that tree.","Michael smiled. He turned his attention toward the panel.","[Please Select:]","[Hourly Suppression: 50,000 Origin Points/Hour]","[24-Hour Permit: 1,000,000 Origin Points]","[Temporary Detainment: Free]","Michael selected the final option without hesitation.","[Temporary Detainment Selected.]","[Accompanying Lifeform will remain within the Entry Inspection Space.]","[The lifeform may be retrieved when the Awakener leaves the Origin Battlefield.]","[Proceeding with entry...]","Michael gave Lunara one final glance.","\"See you soon.\"","Light immediately surrounded him. The endless white room disappeared.","For a brief moment, Michael felt the familiar sensation of being pulled through space before his feet touched solid ground.","This time, he had truly arrived.","Michael’s senses immediately expanded. The sky above him was bright with no sun anywhere in sight. Thick white clouds drifted lazily across an enormous pale-blue sky.","Michael breathed in. The familiar atmosphere of the Origin Battlefield immediately entered his senses.","He was back.","Another familiar sight stood directly ahead of him.","The Universal Cornerstone.","The enormous structure remained exactly where he remembered it, its surface carrying countless patterns that seemed impossible to understand no matter how long he stared at them.","Michael’s eyes lingered on it for several seconds.","However, before Michael could approach it, he sensed someone beside him.","He turned.","Another Michael stood there.","The two stared at each other. This was his other body, the one connected to the Origin Battlefield and Land of Origin.","Neither needed to say anything. Michael simply nodded. The other Michael returned the gesture.","With a thought, spatial power surrounded his second body before it disappeared directly into the Mausoleum.","His job here was done. It needed to go back to the Land of Origin to test out something for him. There was also Arianne. It had been many days since he last saw her. He knew she’d be very mad at him. Thinking of how he’d have to calm her down made the two Michaels feel a slight headache.","Michael’s attention turned back to his territory.","After a moment of thought, he rose into the air. His body rapidly climbed higher until the Universal Cornerstone beneath him became little more than a structure at the center of an enormous expanse of land.","Only then did Michael properly examine everything his other body had accomplished during his absence.","\"Not bad.\"","The changes were immediately obvious.","The Level Three region he had claimed, or more accurately, the territory recognized as his Level One Domain, was enormous. Previously, most of it had simply been wilderness. That was still largely the case. Forests, hills, rivers, plains, and stretches of undeveloped land filled almost everything Michael could see.","However, three enormous circular walls now divided the territory.","The first stood near the outer boundaries of his domain. The second was considerably farther inward. The final wall surrounded the central region containing the Universal Cornerstone and the awakening temple.","From Michael’s current altitude, the three walls resembled gigantic rings carved into the landscape. Their scale became even more impressive when he descended slightly.","Each wall rose hundreds of metres into the air. They were equally ridiculous in thickness, possessing enough space at the top for large groups of people to move across without difficulty.","Michael didn’t need to investigate how they had been constructed. His other body was still him. The memories were there. Thousands of undead had participated in their construction, particularly those possessing abilities useful for manipulating earth, stone, metal, and other materials.","The result was far beyond an ordinary wall.","Michael approached the middle ring and placed a hand against its surface. His perception immediately spread through it.","Countless formations were hidden inside. For this, he had to thank Jester, who the other body had utilized in its free time. There were even numerous empty formation nodes deliberately left behind so additional arrays could be incorporated later.","The walls themselves didn’t possess an official grade. However, if Michael had to assign one based purely on their durability and the formations built into them, Extraordinary Grade would be the absolute minimum."]},{"number":1226,"title":"Chapter 1226: Three Walls","paragraphs":["Michael pulled his hand away.","His gaze traveled across the three enormous rings.","Their purpose was simple.","The outer wall separated the borders of his domain from everything beyond it. The second protected what Michael considered the inner territory. The third formed the central area around the Universal Cornerstone.","Outer Area. Inner Area. Central Area.","Currently, those distinctions were almost meaningless. As there were no settlements or subjects, aside from Michael’s undead and whatever monsters still existed within portions of the territory, most of the land was empty wilderness.","Yet Michael had ordered the walls constructed anyway.","He was preparing for something that hadn’t been confirmed.","The future of the Origin Battlefield.","Michael still didn’t know exactly what would happen when the battlefield underwent whatever transformation seemed to be approaching.","He didn’t know whether the Land of Origin would truly become connected to the real universe, and whether the territories established here would eventually become permanent lands, or whether ordinary living beings would one day be capable of inhabiting this place permanently.","But if even some of his suspicions proved correct, preparing now would save him an enormous amount of trouble later.","Michael rose higher again.","From here, another structure became visible. Or rather, something that couldn’t really be called a structure.","A gigantic transparent dome covered his entire territory. It stretched from one end of his domain to the other, rising high into the sky before curving downward at the opposite boundary.","Under normal circumstances, it was almost impossible to notice. Only when Michael focused could he see faint distortions moving across its surface.","Unlike the walls, this wasn’t something his other body had created. Michael couldn’t create something on this scale yet, even if he wanted to.","This was the Universal Cornerstone’s doing. More specifically, it was the only true defensive mechanism the cornerstone currently provided his domain.","Michael extended his perception toward the transparent barrier. The moment his senses touched it, he felt an enormous power completely different from the formations within the walls.","The three walls were impressive. This was on another level entirely.","The barrier was powerful, but it wasn’t free. Every activation consumed an enormous amount of accumulated mana. That was why Michael’s other body hadn’t simply kept it active indefinitely after claiming the territory. Doing so would have been wasteful, especially when there had been no immediate threat to the domain.","Only after the announcement that the Origin Battlefield would reopen had the barrier been activated again.","Michael floated in the air for a while, studying the almost invisible dome.","Now that he was personally here, however, keeping it active no longer felt necessary. If something powerful enough to threaten the territory appeared, he could simply activate it again.","Michael raised a hand, and the faint distortion covering the sky began to recede. Sections of the transparent dome vanished one after another until the enormous barrier completely disappeared.","Michael lowered his hand.","He had only just finished when a translucent panel suddenly appeared before him.","Michael’s expression changed immediately.","It wasn’t a notification from the Origin Battlefield, but his Rank Advancement Task.","[Rank Advancement Quest]","Comprehend A Domain [2.5% Progress]","A Death’s Heir is the future sovereign. Even young, every supreme has been stated to be special. Be Renowned.","[Influence Levels: Realmic, Multi-Realmic, Sectoric, Grand Sectoric, Galactic, Multi-Galactic, Cluster Sovereign, Supercluster Sovereign, Cosmic, Universal]","[Current Influence Level: Galactic]","[Progress: Complete]","[Own an entity on the level of your Personal Influence. Not less than three levels below. Progress: 25% (Multi-Realmic)]","[Owned Entity: The Eternal Crown: You have now revealed yourself to the world and have become a true heir waiting to turn sovereign.]","Have Five Hundred Rank 4 Subjects [Progress: 1968/500]","Time Limit: 4 Years, 9 Months.","Michael shook his head, feeling he had read incorrectly.","His eyes immediately returned to the third requirement.","[Own an entity on the level of your Personal Influence. Not less than three levels below.]","[25% Progress (Multi-Realmic)]","[Owned Entity: The Eternal Crown]","Twenty-five percent.","Michael’s expression changed.","The last time he had properly checked this requirement, its progress was zero, despite everything he had accomplished in the real world.","Now it had suddenly increased by twenty percent and had even jumped an evaluation grade, to Multi-Realmic.","\"Multi-Realmic?\"","Michael remained motionless in the sky as countless thoughts immediately began connecting.","Why now? What had suddenly changed enough to cause twenty percent progress?","Michael’s gaze lowered toward the final sentence.","[You have now revealed yourself to the world and have become a true heir waiting to turn sovereign.]","\"...\"","Michael tilted his head in confusion.","Several seconds later, laughter escaped him.","\"Hahaha!\"","Michael covered his face with one hand. His laughter became louder.","\"Seriously?\"","For three months. Three entire months he had been thinking about this requirement. He had even wondered whether he needed to conquer multiple realms before the requirement would progress. Yet the answer had been sitting directly in the wording of his class from the beginning.","Death’s Heir.","Michael slowly lowered his hand.","\"What exactly is an heir?\"","The answer was obvious.","An heir wasn’t simply someone possessing potential. An heir was someone recognized as inheriting something. Someone with a position. A foundation. A name that carried weight. Something they could eventually inherit and transform into their own authority.","Michael’s smile widened.","He had been so focused on becoming stronger that he had overlooked the most basic meaning of his own class. If he was truly an heir, then there needed to be something behind that title. Something that could represent him beyond his personal existence.","Michael’s previous actions hadn’t been wrong. Those were all necessary. He had simply skipped the true beginning.","Recognition of a force. But why had it just been recognized, and what exactly had been recognized?","Soon Michael knew the answer when he turned to look at the Origin Battlefield panel and discovered a new section outside the Origin Rankings.","[Origin Battlefield Territory Ranking]","The Eternal Crown (Michael Norman)","*","Please vote to support novel! More Chapters coming!"]},{"number":1227,"title":"Chapter 1227: Named Too Many Times","paragraphs":["Of course it had something to do with the Origin Battlefield again. It was almost like this place was designed to put him on a stage.","What was worse wasn’t even his name being at the top of a long, blank list, and the only one at that. It was what was happening to his Rank Advancement Task.","[Rank Advancement Quest]","[Current Influence Level: Galactic ]","[ Own an entity on the level of your Personal Influence. Not less than three levels below. Progress: 30% ( Multi-Realmic )]","The progress on his task was massively increasing.","[Progress: 50% ( Multi-Realmic )]","[Progress: 80% ( Multi-Realmic )]","[Progress: 99% ( Multi-Realmic )]","It didn’t take long to continue to the next evaluation.","[Progress: 20% ( Sectoric )]","[Progress: 50% ( Sectoric )]","It didn’t stop rising, showing that even more Awakeners were staring at the same thing Michael was right now.","However, it didn’t take long for Michael to wake up from his joy and confusion. He started sweating as even more changes began appearing on his Rank Advancement Task.","[Current Influence Level: Multi-Galactic ]","[Progress: 59% ( Grand Sectoric )]","Yes.","Even his Influence Level had risen a degree.","As for why this was the case, Michael believed it had to do with the thousands of Rank Four Awakeners staring at his name right now.","Fortunately, the speed of progress for the two requirements stopped not long after his Influence Level broke through to Multi-Galactic.","[Current Influence Level: Multi-Galactic ]","[Progress: 77% ( Galactic )]","Fortunately, nothing crazy happened, and he did not break through to the next evaluation of his Influence, which would be Cluster Sovereign.","This, however, also made him realize that simply being known might have already reached its limit for influencing his Influence Level, since if that weren’t the case, the thousands of Awakeners in this layer now, originating from countless realms, should have brought his Influence Level to perhaps even Cosmic level.","Michael had just wiped the invisible sweat off his face when another panel appeared before him.","Fortunately, it didn’t have anything to do with him this time and was for other Awakeners like him.","Well, it did still have something to do with him, though.","[Origin Battlefield Notice]","Following recent evaluations, the following functions have been implemented.","[Ranking Challenge System: Revision]","Each participant may now issue up to ten ranking challenges per month , an increase from the previous limit.","Each participant may likewise be challenged up to ten times per month.","The refusal limit remains unchanged. Each participant may refuse a challenge up to three times, up to three challenges per month. After this limit is reached, any further refusal will be treated as a forfeit.","All other conditions governing challenges, including combat resolution and range restrictions, remain in effect without alteration.","[Territory Ranking]","Similar in structure to the Origin Ranking, the Territory Ranking evaluates every registered domain currently established within the Origin Battlefield. Standing is determined by the comprehensive development of each territory and updates once every ten days.","Rewards for maintained rankings settle once every 182 days. Reward has nothing to do with current ranking but overall performance.","Ranking may also be seized through battle rather than development. Should the residents of two territories, each under their own Universal Cornerstone, engage one another in battle, victory may forcefully transfer standing between them regardless of prior progress.","Owners are advised to explore this function themselves.","[Dungeon System]","In recognition of awakener growth across the Origin Battlefield, the Dungeon System has been opened.","Portals leading into dungeons will now appear throughout various locations within the battlefield. A dungeon is a sealed space separated from the surrounding territory, generated with its own monsters, traps, and treasures independent of the outside world. Every portal is temporary and will collapse once its duration expires, along with anything left unclaimed inside.","Clearing a dungeon grants a chance to obtain a Dungeon Blueprint. Territory owners in possession of a Universal Cornerstone may use a Blueprint to convert a temporary portal into a permanent gateway, binding the dungeon to their domain indefinitely.","Further changes are to be expected following future evaluations.","The Origin Battlefield wishes all awakeners continued growth and development.","If there was one thing Michael had noticed since entering the Origin Battlefield again, it was how frequently the Universal Cornerstone kept appearing, far more than he had originally expected.","Origin Points. Territories. Permanent dungeons. The new Territory Ranking.","Even bringing beings above the permitted Rank into lower layers required a currency Michael only knew how to obtain through the Universal Cornerstone.","At this point, the message was becoming almost painfully obvious. If someone wanted to properly participate in the deeper functions of the Origin Battlefield, possessing a Universal Cornerstone wasn’t merely useful.","It might eventually become necessary.","The Origin Battlefield was practically telling every Awakener in existence that whatever advantages they currently enjoyed were incomplete without a cornerstone.","Fortunately, there was one good thing about that.","Michael was no longer the only known person who could possess one. That mattered a lot.","His previous situation had been dangerous partly because outsiders believed whatever treasure he possessed might be unique. Now every Awakener had been shown that domains could be established using Universal Cornerstones. The Territory Ranking had even openly revealed the concept.","Anyone sufficiently intelligent would quickly understand that Michael hadn’t received some impossible treasure no one else could ever obtain. Others could claim one too. They simply had to find one.","Michael suspected this alone would reduce some of the attention on him. Especially from the stronger races.","Why waste enormous resources hunting Michael across realms when they could instead mobilize their own Awakeners inside the Origin Battlefield and search for another Universal Cornerstone?","The Origin Battlefield actually had an enormous advantage over the Land of Origin when it came to something like that. People didn’t need to hide what they were here. Everyone participating was an Awakener. Their worlds and races might be different, but there was no mystery surrounding why they had entered.","More importantly, people from the same civilization weren’t necessarily isolated from one another forever. With suitable communication methods or other specialized means, Awakeners belonging to the same realm could probably locate one another and cooperate."]},{"number":1228,"title":"Chapter 1228: Challenge","paragraphs":["There were thousands of civilizations represented in this layer alone. Surely some powerful races had already developed methods allowing their people to gather together after entry.","Now that Universal Cornerstones had been openly revealed, that cooperation would become even more important.","Michael looked again at the empty rankings beneath his name. He doubted they would remain empty for long.","Strong races possessed too many advantages. Perhaps within days, more names would begin appearing beneath the Eternal Crown.","Michael wouldn’t even be surprised if some territories rose frighteningly quickly once an entire civilization began supporting them.","However, the opposite was equally true. Not every race was powerful, and not every realm possessed dozens or hundreds of exceptional Awakeners.","There could easily be small realms where only two Rank Four Awakeners had qualified for the Fourth Layer. Perhaps those two weren’t merely the strongest Awakeners from their realm participating in the Origin Battlefield. Perhaps they were two of the only Rank Four beings their entire realm possessed.","The difference between civilizations could be absurd.","For weaker realms like that, common sense should tell them not to provoke Michael Norman.","Unfortunately, Michael no longer trusted common sense nearly as much as before. The assassins in Aurora had taught him that lesson quite clearly. Greed could make people reckless. And ignorance could make someone suicidal without them ever realizing it.","Michael couldn’t simply assume weaker forces would leave him alone because attacking him was stupid. Neither could he dismiss the powerful ones.","Perhaps a major civilization would decide obtaining Michael’s already developed cornerstone was easier than searching for one themselves. Perhaps they would simply want the ranking position. The new rules had already stated that rankings could be seized through conflict between territories.","That alone guaranteed future wars.","Michael looked toward the three enormous walls surrounding his territory again. For the first time, they no longer seemed excessively cautious. If anything, they might not be enough.","Michael exhaled slowly.","There was still far too much to do before he could genuinely feel at ease.","\"However, putting everything aside, the Origin Battlefield truly is a place created for Awakeners.\"","Whether it was the Universal Cornerstone Store or the Dungeon System, one thing was certain. The future was sure to be exciting.","Michael had just closed his panel when another one appeared before him. This time, it was a familiar one.","[Challenge Request]","Three of them, arriving at once.","To think the ranking system had only just opened, and people were already lining up to challenge him.","Michael smiled.","Before, he hadn’t been entirely sure how he wanted to approach the rankings. Drawing more attention than necessary had never sounded appealing. But he’d already made his decision.","It was time to climb.","He was, for all intents and purposes, a naked man standing in the middle of the universe already. Worrying about a little more attention wasn’t going to change much at this point.","Michael dismissed the three incoming challenges without a second thought and opened the rankings himself instead, searching for the name sitting ten spots above his own.","His gaze stopped.","It was a familiar name. The first necromancer he had ever fought. The one from whom he had stolen the skeletal dragon and wyvern.","Michael’s smile widened. He didn’t hesitate. He selected the name and sent the challenge request.","Elsewhere, deep within the Fourth Layer, sprawled across a stretch of frost-blasted highlands, Varek stood at the center of it, atop a raised dais of bone and frozen earth, arms crossed, eyes fixed on the floating panel in front of him.","A single name currently occupied the very top of a list, sitting alone above a long stretch of empty space.","The Eternal Crown (Michael Norman)","Varek exhaled slowly through his nose.","\"...As expected. That boy is no ordinary individual. So young, and causing so much commotion on such a grand scale. Perhaps only a god can match this excitement.\"","Varek shook his head.","It was probably better to stay away from him. Some pride wasn’t worth making an enemy out of this person.","Varek had only just closed the panel when a new one materialized in front of him.","[Ranking Challenge Pending]","Challenger: Rank 198","Decision Time Remaining: 04:58","[Challenge Information]","Refusing this challenge will consume one refusal against this challenger.","Remaining Refusals Against This Challenger: 3/3","Remaining Universal Challenge Refusals This Month: 3/3","If all refusals against this challenger are exhausted, any further refusal will be treated as a forfeit.","Upon forfeiture, both participants will immediately exchange ranking positions.","Varek leisurely went to check who was Rank 198. For some reason, the name gave him a sense of déjà vu.","It was only when he saw the name of the person in Rank 198 that he realized why he felt something in the first place.","Michael had already returned to the ground.","He rolled his shoulders, twisted his neck from side to side, and stretched both arms behind his back. Ten challenges. That was enough to make a considerable jump if things went smoothly.","Michael was curious where he would end up after using all ten. There were several factors to consider. Opponents could refuse. Some might already be challenging others.","Still, starting from Rank 198, he expected to climb quite a bit.","Michael had just finished stretching when a panel appeared.","[Ranking Challenge Result]","[Your opponent has forfeited.]","[Challenge resolved without combat.]","[Ranking positions have been exchanged.]","[Previous Rank: 198 ]","[Current Rank: 188 ]","[Ranking Updated Successfully]","\"Tsk. What a shame. Would have loved to chat with an old friend at least.\"","Michael wasted no time. He opened the rankings again and selected another name ten positions above him.","[Challenge Request Sent.]","This time, there was no immediate response.","Michael waited patiently, flexing his fingers while watching the timer decrease.","Nearly a minute passed.","Then the panel suddenly changed.","[Challenge Accepted.]","[Preparing Battlefield.]","Michael smiled.","\"Good.\"","At least this one had some courage.","A faint spatial distortion immediately began forming around him as the Origin Battlefield prepared to transfer both participants into the designated arena.","\"Ohhh. This is new. No portals again?\""]},{"number":1229,"title":"Chapter 1229: Beautiful Scenery","paragraphs":["The last time Michael had entered a battle arena for the Origin Ranking, a portal had always opened first, a swirling gate he’d have to physically step through. Now, apparently, the Origin Will had decided that step was unnecessary.","Michael found himself standing in a place filled with nothing but darkness.","[Awaiting Opponent]","Please wait while the challenged party selects their desired arena.","Michael crossed his arms.","Right. There was this part.","Unlike a regular duel where both sides fought in a neutral setting, the ranking challenge system worked differently. The one being challenged got to choose the battlefield itself.","Like the Origin Will said, except for a few exceptions, everything in the world was balanced.","Michael waited patiently, curious what his opponent might choose.","The darkness held nothing but silence for a while.","Then, finally, a panel appeared.","[Battlefield Created Successfully]","Name: Sunreach Meadow","Description: A wide, open field bathed in constant sunlight beneath a cloudless sky. Warmth and Yang Energy permeate every corner of the battlefield.","Living creatures continuously recover vitality and warmth, while beings aligned with negative or death-based energies suffer a steady erosion of strength within the environment.","\"...Sunlight?\"","Of all the terrains available in a system, his opponent had picked an environment \"guaranteed\" to work against him specifically.","Michael scratched the side of his head, a smile spreading across his face.","\"This person might know a bit about me.\"","Though he was probably one of the most famous people in the universe lately, that didn’t mean every Awakener would be obsessed with him. Perhaps some still only knew his name and hadn’t bothered investigating any further, for whatever reason.","However, this opponent was likely part of the other side, someone who’d actually looked into him.","Unless it was pure coincidence, choosing this exact battlefield had to be deliberate, a way to counter him before the fight had even started.","The spatial distortion around him thickened, and Michael disappeared from the space of darkness.","The first thing that came to Michael was warmth. Then came the light.","He opened his eyes and, for several seconds, simply stood there without moving.","This place, Sunreach Meadow, was beautiful. Far more beautiful than its simple name suggested.","An endless sea of pale-golden grass stretched beneath Michael’s feet, each blade reaching slightly above his ankles and swaying in perfect waves whenever the wind passed through them.","From where he stood, the meadow continued in every direction until land and sky eventually became indistinguishable along the horizon.","There were no trees, mountains, or buildings. Not even a distant silhouette to break the landscape. Only an endless golden field.","Above it hung a vast blue sky so clear it almost looked unreal. There wasn’t a single cloud anywhere, and at its center burned an enormous golden sun.","Its light didn’t feel harsh. Instead, it covered the entire world in a warm brilliance, turning the grass into something resembling an ocean made from strands of molten gold.","Every few moments, the wind would sweep across the meadow. One section of grass would bend first, followed by another and another, creating enormous ripples that raced across the plains for kilometres before finally disappearing somewhere beyond sight.","Tiny particles of golden light floated among the grass. They rose slowly from the earth, drifted through the air like fireflies, then dissolved beneath the sunlight.","Michael extended his hand. One landed briefly against his palm.","It was warm.","\"Is this Pure Yang Energy?\" he wondered.","There was an incredible amount of it. The entire battlefield seemed saturated with vitality. If an ordinary living creature remained here long enough, even serious injuries would probably begin recovering faster than normal.","Unfortunately, there was something missing.","Life.","Michael’s perception spread outward.","There were no insects hidden beneath the grass. No birds in the sky. No beasts roaming the plains.","The entire beautiful world was completely empty, making the scenery strangely unsettling. It looked like the perfect summer meadow, yet there wasn’t a single living thing anywhere.","Not even his opponent.","Michael raised an eyebrow.","\"Where are you?\"","His voice travelled across the open field before gradually fading.","No answer came.","Michael glanced toward the horizon and smiled faintly.","\"I wouldn’t mind owning something like this.\"","The Mausoleum already contained mountains, rivers, forests, and enormous plains. But this place possessed an atmosphere of its own. If not for the fact that someone was somewhere inside this seemingly endless world waiting to fight him, Michael could have easily mistaken it for a place created purely for rest.","Another gust of wind moved through the grass. Michael’s long black hair shifted behind him.","He closed his eyes briefly, feeling the Yang Energy pressing against his body. However, aside from a faint discomfort settling somewhere beneath his skin, Michael found himself mostly fine.","The other party had been right in choosing this environment. Dense light energy on this scale would have been devastating for most necromancers. It was a smart, targeted choice.","But Michael wasn’t an ordinary necromancer.","For one thing, he wasn’t like the others whose energy carried the residue of their profession, the countless hours spent digging graves, the grim rituals many necromancers dabbled in that gradually corroded their own bodies and left their constitution weaker than others of the same level.","Even mages were physically better compared to most necromancers.","Michael’s energy had never been built like the others. What flowed through him was simply darkness, pure and undiluted, untouched by the practices that usually came bundled with the class.","But that darkness was only true of his energy. Deep down, beneath the class, beneath the title, he was still a True Human, one with affinity toward every element, not just death or darkness.","Becoming Death’s Heir had massively suppressed most of those affinities, pushing the dark element so far forward that it dominated everything else almost entirely. But suppressed wasn’t the same as gone.","The others still existed inside him, quietly, even if only at the level of a minor genius by comparison."]},{"number":1230,"title":"Chapter 1230: Lumin Mothkin","paragraphs":["And then there was his monstrous vitality.","No ordinary necromancer carried a body capable of shrugging off environments built specifically to punish undead-aligned beings. In truth, Michael had already stood several levels above his class long before Death’s Heir had ever entered the picture.","This meadow, beautiful and lethal as it was meant to be, simply wasn’t enough.","Michael raised one hand and summoned his undead.","Beginning appeared beside him as one undead after another materialized around him.","Within seconds, a thousand undead had spread across the golden meadow.","Almost immediately after Beginning’s arrival, Michael had noticed a difference. The effect of Sunreach Meadow was far more obvious on them than it had been on him. Thin wisps of energy constantly leaked from several undead before being burned away by the sunlight.","Michael narrowed his eyes. This was, after all, his first time fighting in an environment this disadvantageous.","On him, the environment had barely been an inconvenience. On other undead, however, it was a real suppression.","Still, none of them were collapsing. Some undead, like Beginning with its special Law, weren’t significantly suppressed at all.","Michael glanced toward Beginning, then turned to look at the other hundreds of undead under him.","\"Find any other living being in this place and kill it.\"","Watching the groups divide into groups of fifty, Michael himself took off.","Far away from Michael’s position, hidden within the endless golden plains, something moved.","A creature no larger than a human child crouched among the tall grass, its body almost perfectly blending with the light surrounding it.","Four thin wings extended from its back. They resembled butterfly wings at first glance, delicate and almost transparent, but countless golden patterns covered their surfaces.","Whenever sunlight passed through them, those patterns bent the light strangely, causing the creature’s outline to blur and disappear.","Its race was known as the Lumin Mothkin.","Despite their fragile appearance, they were one of the rarer races naturally aligned with light. Unlike most light-related species, however, the Lumin Mothkin were not known for healing, purification, or direct combat.","They were assassins.","Their bodies could merge with surrounding light, suppress their presence, distort perception, and even briefly turn themselves almost completely invisible beneath sufficient illumination.","Unfortunately, their race itself was insignificant on the wider scale of the universe, as they possessed no Demigod. The strongest known member of their race had remained trapped beneath that threshold for as long as they could remember.","Even reaching Rank Four was considered an achievement worthy of being recorded in their history.","The creature hiding among the grass was one of those rare individuals.","A Level 100.","Its golden compound eyes remained fixed on the distant darkness spreading across the meadow.","This was the fourth time it had come across something like this. More importantly:","Why does this group also look different from the previous three? Don’t tell me this Michael Norman has two hundred Rank Four undead with him? Isn’t he a realm at this point?!","The information he purchased from the Shadow Pavilion didn’t include this at all!","Sure, granted he only bought the lowest tier on this fellow, but with how expensive it was, surely they could have been more generous to include something like this, no?!","In fact, this was how most supernaturals that didn’t have the resources or guts to approach Aurora got more information about the matter.","It was how it knew that this fellow was nineteen years old, a Rank Three Awakener at Level 75, had at least one undead who could match three Level 100 Awakeners without losing, proven by evidence gathered from his last Origin Battlefield visit, and also had at least two battlefield treasures with him.","This was what the basic information contained. Oh, and an insignificant part about some family members.","The Lumin Mothkin’s wings trembled slightly.","For the first time since accepting Michael’s challenge, a thought appeared in its mind.","Had it made the correct decision?","It knew someone becoming known across multiple realms couldn’t possibly be ordinary. The Lumin Mothkin had understood that before accepting. It had simply ignored the warning since its greed had been stronger.","It had thought that as a Level 100, it should be able to handle a Level 75, even if he was guarded, right?","The creature repeated that thought to itself as it watched Beginning’s enormous silhouette rise above the golden grass in the distance.","The Lumin Mothkin swallowed.","\"...should I still continue this?\"","It had only just finished that thought when the sunlight above it suddenly disappeared.","The Lumin Mothkin froze.","A shadow swallowed the grass around it. Its head snapped upward.","A massive hand was descending from the sky.","\"What?!\"","There was no time to think.","The creature’s wings erupted with golden light as it shot sideways, its body becoming almost transparent beneath the sunlight.","The sixty-metre giant that had just passed it had somehow found it.","The Lumin Mothkin’s heart immediately sank. The information from Shadow Pavilion had mentioned the dark drake, but nothing about this one, which was why it had hidden itself even more upon sensing it at first.","\"Those bastards!\"","After this, it was never buying the lowest information tier again.","The creature had no intention of fighting Beginning directly. It needed time to make a decision after seeing what this Michael Norman had to offer. Right now, it had already lost the will to fight and was just being stubborn.","Fortunately, Beginning was enormous. Something that large should be slow if it didn’t use the Void, and even if it did, with how limited the use of the Void was in the Origin Battlefield arena, a good part of chasing depended on flight.","The Lumin Mothkin accelerated. It didn’t use the Void, as there was no need. The moment the giant attacked, it had used its power to make the surrounding void chaotic, creating a sort of space lock.","In any case, speed was one of the greatest advantages of its race, especially beneath sunlight this dense.","It believed it could escape."]},{"number":1231,"title":"Chapter 1231: We’ll See Again","paragraphs":["Beginning’s arm moved.","\"So fast?!\" the Lumin Mothkin’s eyes widened.","The enormous palm changed direction in midair with a speed completely incompatible with Beginning’s size.","\"No!\"","Bang!","The hand struck it directly.","The Lumin Mothkin became a golden blur as it was slapped across the meadow. Its tiny body tore through the grass, bounced once, then again, before finally smashing into the ground hard enough to create a long trench.","For several seconds, it didn’t move.","Then one trembling wing slowly rose from the crater.","\"...What kind of giant moves like that?\"","It had only just forced itself upright when the air beside it shifted.","A fair hand emerged from seemingly nowhere and closed around empty space where its neck had been a fraction of a second earlier.","The Lumin Mothkin’s wings exploded with golden light. Its body blurred. By the time the hand closed, it had already escaped several metres away.","The creature twisted in midair, staring back.","A young man stood where it had been. Long black hair moved gently behind him in the wind. His expression was calm, almost curious.","The Lumin Mothkin recognized him immediately.","Michael Norman.","The portrait provided by Shadow Pavilion had been accurate.","Michael, meanwhile, was surprised at the creature’s movement.","\"It’s so fast?\"","One should know, he was already in Wisdom State. His perception, reactions, control, and movement were all operating at their highest level.","Yet the creature had still escaped his grasp. Its speed was no joke. Looking at the creature’s appearance, Michael was curious what race it was from.","Unfortunately for the Lumin Mothkin, there was no time for either of them to think further.","Beginning arrived.","The giant’s enormous foot came crashing down. The creature vanished in a burst of golden light before impact.","Boom!","The meadow exploded.","Michael moved at the same time.","For the next several minutes, the battlefield became something resembling a hunt.","The Lumin Mothkin never stayed in one place for more than a second. It darted across the golden plains, using sunlight to constantly erase its presence and change direction without warning.","Michael followed tightly. Sometimes he appeared behind it. Sometimes above it. Other times, a hand would suddenly reach from a blind spot the creature had been certain was empty moments earlier.","Each time, it barely escaped. But that was all it could do. Michael was still able to land a few solid hits when it was distracted.","At this point, the Lumin Mothkin wanted to escape. It no longer had any real opportunity to attack Michael.","The other undead were considerably less troublesome. They simply couldn’t keep up. Even when they surrounded areas in groups, the Lumin Mothkin could slip through gaps before they reacted.","That should have reassured it, if Michael hadn’t also been able to keep up. Instead, it terrified it.","The Rank Three human could actually chase it.","Worse, Michael wasn’t recklessly throwing attacks around, the way it had expected from a human youth trying to teach it a lesson. He was like a slippery snake, only daring to attack when it was distracted by the giant.","The Lumin Mothkin’s heart beat faster.","Another shadow appeared overhead.","It was Beginning.","\"Again?! Just leave me alone!\"","It shot sideways. Michael appeared directly in its escape path.","The creature immediately twisted downward, wings nearly folding against its back as it dropped toward the grass.","Michael’s fingers passed just above its head.","The creature disappeared into the sunlight again.","Michael stopped in the air and watched it flee.","\"This one’s troublesome.\"","It was not powerful enough to threaten him as long as he was careful, but if it wanted nothing except to run, catching it cleanly would take time.","Michael didn’t particularly feel like wasting that time.","So he summoned another five hundred undead.","The Lumin Mothkin stared in shock. Its wings stopped moving for half a second. Its eyes slowly moved toward the undead already scattered across the meadow.","Something inside it finally broke.","A panel appeared.","[Would you like to forfeit the Ranking Challenge?]","The creature selected yes immediately.","[Forfeit Confirmed.]","Michael had only just begun directing the newly summoned undead when the entire battlefield froze.","[Opponent Has Forfeited.]","[Challenge Victory Confirmed.]","[Ranking Positions Will Be Exchanged.]","Michael stared at the panel. Then toward the distant golden blur that was already beginning to dissolve into light.","\"...Seriously?\"","Michael watched the Lumin Mothkin disappear without feeling much disappointment. If anything, he was amused.","\"We’ll meet again.\"","During the few solid hits he had managed to land, Michael hadn’t only been trying to injure it. He had also left something behind.","A spatial mark.","Michael couldn’t sense it in the arena, but when he went outside, the story would change. As long as the mark remained, Michael had a reference. Eventually, regardless of where the creature went within the Origin Battlefield or the universe, he would have a much easier time finding it again if they ever crossed paths.","Michael wasn’t particularly angry.","The Lumin Mothkin had simply accepted a ranking challenge, but the chosen battlefield implied it might have had some other intentions.","Michael didn’t feel comfortable dwelling on whether that was true or whether it had simply been a coincidence, since the creature was aligned with the light element and might have simply wanted a home-ground advantage.","Was it petty?","Probably.","Michael smiled as the golden meadow vanished around him.","\"But it is what it is. When we meet in the future, we’ll naturally talk over any issue of mutual interest, I guess.\"","Still, just like Varek, this creature also made Michael aware of the power difference of those ranked in the Top 200. No one of them was truly ordinary.","He wondered just how strong those in the Top 100 were.","Or even the Top 10.","Surely those people had Demigod-rank prowess, right?","Aside from wanting some peace by proving to others that they needed to think twice before crossing him, Michael felt a rare trace of battle intent.","The Origin Battlefield was truly interesting."]},{"number":1232,"title":"Chapter 1232: Suitable Location","paragraphs":["After a match ended, the participants were given three hours before the battlefield forcibly removed them.","Michael had no intention of using that time.","The moment the notifications settled, he recalled Beginning and the rest of his undead.","After he was done, Michael selected the option to leave.","Light surrounded him. A moment later, he returned to the Fourth Layer.","His ranking had already changed.","Michael barely glanced at it before opening the leaderboard again. There was no reason to stop now.","He selected another name ten ranks above his own and immediately issued the next challenge.","While Michael continued climbing and making changes to the leaderboard, his repeated victories were already beginning to attract another wave of attention among the countless Awakeners scattered across the Origin Battlefield.","On the other hand, far away in the Land of Origin, another Michael sat inside a grand office.","He wore a dark ceremonial robe embroidered with subtle golden patterns, while his long black hair had been left loose. Sunlight entered through the tall open windows beside him, falling across the room and catching against the edges of his hair.","Before him rested an enormous map covering nearly the entire table.","Michael leaned over it silently, one hand resting against the wood while his eyes moved across the marked territories.","For several moments, he didn’t speak. The scene was peaceful.","*Image*","The reason Michael had returned to the Land of Origin wasn’t only because he wanted to see Arianne again after being away for so long.","There was something else he had wanted to test for quite some time.","One of the functions connected to the Universal Cornerstone.","For a while now, Michael had carried several suspicions regarding what the cornerstone could really do and how deeply its influence extended beyond the Origin Battlefield. Unfortunately, there had never been a convenient opportunity to test those ideas properly.","Now there was. Since this body had already returned to the Land of Origin, he could test the cornerstone and spend some time with Arianne.","In fact, Arianne had been the first person Michael wanted to see after arriving.","Unfortunately, she wasn’t currently inside the palace.","After a bit of investigation, he saw she had gone into the imperial city earlier this morning with several palace maids and guards, bringing food and supplies to children in poorer districts.","One of Michael’s Rank Four undead accompanied her as always.","Since he felt there was no need to interrupt whatever she was doing simply because he had returned, he had the undead accompanying her inform her of his return.","It definitely wasn’t because he was trying to prolong whatever misgivings she would have at him upon seeing him.","Michael smiled faintly at the thought before returning his attention to the map.","The enormous map spread across the table represented the imperial capital and the surrounding territories extending hundreds of kilometres outward.","Whether roads, villages, forests, rivers, mountains, military outposts, or resource zones, everything had been marked in considerable detail.","Michael’s eyes moved slowly across it.","He needed somewhere suitable for the experiment. Preferably not too far from the capital.","If his suspicion was correct, whatever appeared might become extremely useful to the empire in the future. Keeping it close would make managing and protecting it much easier.","More importantly, since Michael wasn’t certain whether whatever was created could be moved afterward, choosing carelessly could become a problem.","Just as Michael was considering whether the location beneath his finger was suitable, his perception caught something moving rapidly through the palace.","His eyes shifted toward the office doors.","The presence was familiar enough that the tension in his expression disappeared almost immediately.","Arianne.","She was already back.","Michael smiled.","Judging by how quickly she was moving through the corridors, the undead he had contacted must have delivered his message not long after he sent it.","Michael straightened slightly and waited.","The familiar presence approached the office, then suddenly stopped right outside the door.","\"...?\"","Michael tilted his head in confusion.","For some reason, Arianne seemed to be hesitating to enter his office.","What exactly is she doing? Did I do something wrong?","Wait, why am I immediately thinking I’m at fault?","Michael thought for a moment before looking toward the open space beside the desk.","A second later, a small rabbit taken from the Mausoleum appeared.","The animal landed lightly on the carpet and immediately looked around in confusion, its ears twitching.","Michael raised a hand.","\"Sorry about this.\"","Snap. His fingers clicked.","[Swap]","The rabbit vanished.","At the exact same moment, something much heavier appeared in its place.","\"Ah?!\"","Arianne dropped directly out of empty space.","Michael’s arms caught her, one beneath her back and the other around her waist, as her legs fell across his lap.","Outside the office, the unfortunate rabbit appeared where Arianne had been standing. It barely had time to understand what was happening before another small portal opened beneath it. The rabbit dropped straight through.","A second later, it was back inside the Mausoleum, landing harmlessly among the wilderness before immediately hopping away in fear.","Its brief service to the empire had ended.","Back inside the office, Michael looked down at Arianne still sitting across his arms and legs.","Michael’s smile returned.","\"Hi.\"","For a moment, Arianne’s expression softened. The corners of her lips almost rose. Then, as though suddenly remembering something, she squeezed her face into what was probably supposed to be a serious expression and deliberately turned her head away from him.","\"...?\"","Her reaction caught him off guard.","He lifted one hand and gently tried to turn her face back toward him.","Arianne calmly pushed his hand aside.","\"What happened?\" Michael inquired but got no answer.","\"Did something happen while I was gone?\"","Silence.","\"Did someone bother you?\"","She still didn’t say anything.","Michael’s confusion gradually deepened.","\"Arianne?\"","She continued looking away.","Michael hesitated before finally asking the question that had first crossed his mind outside the door.","\"Did I do something wrong?\"","Arianne immediately turned toward him. Her green eyes locked onto his.","The serious expression on her face would have been far more intimidating if Michael hadn’t noticed how much effort she seemed to be putting into maintaining it.","\"Do you think disappearing for almost an entire week is something your partner is supposed to be fine with?\""]},{"number":1233,"title":"Chapter 1233: I’m Sorry","paragraphs":["Michael froze.","\"...Ah.\"","That was what this was about. A small trace of panic entered his expression.","\"No, wait. That’s not exactly what happened.\"","Arianne raised an eyebrow.","Michael quickly continued.","\"I told you before I left that I might not be around for a while, remember?\"","She said nothing.","\"And I had Jester send you a message three days ago saying I’d be back soon, no?\"","Arianne’s expression remained unchanged.","Michael felt slightly more confident.","Exactly. I communicated with her after returning from Aurora. I didn’t simply vanish without saying anything.","Amidst his thoughts, Arianne asked calmly, \"Were you really so busy that you couldn’t come and tell me yourself?\"","\"...\"","Michael’s mouth opened. Then closed.","Arianne stared at him.","Michael looked away for half a second.","For someone capable of processing countless thoughts simultaneously, he suddenly found himself without a single useful response that wouldn’t sound like a lame excuse.","Technically...","He could have. Finding a few minutes wouldn’t have been impossible. Jester had simply been more convenient to pass a message for him before he entered the Netherworld.","However, saying that aloud seemed like a terrible idea.","Michael looked back at Arianne. She was still sitting comfortably across his lap despite supposedly being angry with him.","Michael thought for several seconds. Then he gave up trying to find an excuse.","His shoulders relaxed.","\"...I’m really sorry. I could have done better.\"","Michael lowered his head slightly.","\"I should have come myself. It’s not a lie that I was indeed occupied, but it’s true I could have come to see you at least.\"","There was silence.","Michael didn’t try to explain further. He had genuinely been busy. There had been the Netherworld, the resurrection ritual, Lunara, Aurora, the assassins, the Origin Battlefield reopening, and far too many other things competing for his attention.","But none of that really changed her point.","So he remained quiet.","A few seconds passed.","Then Michael felt a touch beneath his chin.","Arianne gently raised his face.","Before he could say anything, she leaned forward and kissed him.","Michael’s eyes widened.","Arianne kissed him with the same boldness she seemed to approach almost everything involving their relationship after her resurrection. Arianne was strangely aggressive whenever it came to affection.","Even now, he wasn’t completely used to this side of her.","Not that he disliked it, though. Quite the opposite.","Michael remained frozen for the first second, caught completely off guard by how quickly her anger had transformed into this. Then he slowly relaxed. His arm tightened naturally around her waist.","Arianne eventually pulled back just enough for their faces to separate.","Michael stared at her.","\"...You were angry just a while ago.\"","\"I still am.\"","Michael almost laughed.","Perhaps noticing that he was still being a little too passive, Arianne frowned faintly. Then, without warning, she caught his wrist.","\"What are you...\"","She pulled his hand toward herself and placed it against her chest.","Michael froze again. His eyes immediately returned to her face.","Arianne stared back at him, the faint redness appearing around her ears completely ruining the confident expression she was trying to maintain.","Michael’s mind briefly went blank. For someone who had faced Demigods and commanded thousands of undead while ruling over millions of people, he suddenly had absolutely no idea what he was supposed to say.","Arianne narrowed her eyes.","\"Are you always going to make me do everything?\"","\"...\"","Michael finally understood.","A slow smile appeared on his face.","\"Probably not.\"","This time, when he leaned toward her, Arianne didn’t need to take the initiative. Michael closed the remaining distance between them.","This time, the kiss was slower.","Arianne’s earlier aggression softened as Michael finally began matching her properly, one arm remaining securely around her waist while the other rested against her back.","Arianne’s fingers slipped into his long hair, pulling him slightly closer.","Michael smiled against her lips.","Minutes passed quietly.","Eventually, however, Arianne’s movements slowed. Her expression changed.","Michael noticed.","\"What is it?\"","Arianne didn’t answer immediately. She shifted slightly on his lap then froze.","\"...\"","Her face gradually became red.","Michael followed her gaze downward and immediately understood.","Ah.","Arianne stood up almost instantly.","Michael blinked as the warmth disappeared from his lap.","She straightened her clothes before turning toward him with a glare.","Michael raised both hands innocently.","\"What?\"","Arianne’s eyes narrowed even further.","\"You know exactly what.\"","Michael’s expression became awkward.","\"That’s not exactly something I consciously control.\"","Arianne stared at him for another second before turning away, though the redness on her ears made the entire attempt at looking angry considerably less convincing.","Under Michael’s amused gaze, Arianne remained standing for only a few seconds before turning around to sit back down on his lap.","Arianne ignored the look on her partner’s face and settled comfortably against him, though she made a very deliberate effort to sit slightly differently this time.","Michael almost laughed but wisely kept that to himself.","Arianne leaned back against his chest.","\"How long are you staying this time?\"","Michael’s expression softened slightly. He rested one arm around her waist and thought about it honestly.","\"I can’t promise anything.\"","Arianne turned her head enough to look at him.","Michael continued before she could complain.","\"But unless something drastic happens again, I should be around much more.\"","There were still too many things demanding his attention. The Origin Battlefield had reopened. Aurora remained unstable. Lucky and several other undead were evolving. His Rank Advancement Quest was finally showing real progress.","Promising Arianne that he wouldn’t disappear again would simply be dishonest.","\"But I’ll do better about actually telling you when I need to leave.\"","Arianne studied his face for several seconds.","\"Personally?\"","Michael smiled helplessly.","\"Personally.\"","That seemed to satisfy her.","\"Good.\"","She relaxed properly against him.","For a short while, neither of them spoke.","Then Arianne’s eyes wandered toward the enormous table. More specifically, the map covering almost its entire surface.","She tilted her head.","\"Why do you have the capital’s regional map open?\"","Michael followed her gaze. His attention, which had completely abandoned the reason he’d been sitting here in the first place, finally returned to the marked territory beneath the sunlight."]},{"number":1234,"title":"Chapter 1234: Selected Location","paragraphs":["With his attention brought back to the map, Michael returned to the task he had abandoned earlier.","Arianne remained beside him, and with her familiarity with the imperial capital and the surrounding areas, narrowing down a suitable location became considerably easier.","Before long, the two settled on a region northeast of the capital.","It was relatively open, sparsely populated, and close to one of the empire’s military training zones.","The empire currently maintained three major categories of armed forces.","The largest was the Imperial Regular Army. It consisted mostly of ordinary knights, soldiers, cavalry, archers, engineers, and other conventional military personnel. Individually, most of them were nothing remarkable by supernatural standards, but their numbers were enormous.","They formed the backbone of the empire.","Because of their size, it was impossible to gather all of their training grounds in a single location. Barracks, forts, and training camps belonging to the Imperial Regular Army were scattered throughout the empire, particularly around major cities, trade routes, agricultural regions, and populated territories.","Very few of their main bases were built close to the imperial capital itself. Concentrating hundreds of thousands of ordinary troops around one city was not practical.","Above them stood the Silver Guard Army. Every proper combatant within the Silver Guard possessed strength roughly equivalent to a Rank One existence. Their commanders were considerably stronger, with some reaching Rank Two while many stood just beneath that threshold.","Compared to the Imperial Regular Army, their numbers were dramatically smaller, but they were still large enough to be divided into numerous posts throughout the empire. These soldiers were often responsible for dealing with supernatural threats that ordinary knights couldn’t reasonably handle.","The final and strongest force was known as the Crown Legion. It was also the smallest. Even the weakest proper member possessed strength equivalent to Rank Two. Its officers and commanders naturally stood much higher.","Such people couldn’t be wasted guarding ordinary roads or maintaining public order. Crown Legion units were stationed around important resource zones, dangerous borders, strategic fortresses, ancient ruins or secret realms, and other locations whose value justified placing powerful individuals there.","For that reason, most of the Crown Legion wasn’t normally gathered near the capital either.","During periods of peace, however, many of its senior commanders spent roughly half of each year rotating through the imperial capital. It could either be on a week-on, week-off basis, or a month or two on and off.","It was partly ceremonial, partly administrative, and partly defensive.","The empire Michael had fought during his takeover hadn’t represented its complete military strength. Had the entire empire somehow been gathered against him from the beginning, Michael’s losses would undoubtedly have been greater. The final outcome, however, wouldn’t have changed.","That difference mattered far less now.","These people were no longer enemies. They were his subjects.","The location Arianne eventually recommended was positioned close to one of the Silver Guard Army’s divided training posts. That made it particularly convenient.","The arrangement itself wasn’t something Michael had created after taking over. The previous rulers had deliberately positioned several Silver Guard posts within reasonable distance of the capital so that powerful troops could reinforce the city quickly during emergencies without permanently concentrating the entire force there.","Michael and Jester had seen no reason to change that structure. If anything, it remained useful.","Michael personally didn’t require thousands of Silver Guards rushing to protect him. But the imperial capital contained far more than Michael. Officials, civilians, merchants, craftsmen, noble families, administrative facilities, storage depots, and countless other important parts of the empire existed there. Millions of lives ultimately depended on the city remaining stable.","Now that Michael ruled those lives, even if the previous him had been partly unserious about it, there was no reason to dismantle an effective military arrangement simply because he himself had little need for it.","More importantly, placing his experiment near a Silver Guard post solved several potential problems at once. If whatever the Universal Cornerstone created couldn’t be moved afterward, the location would already possess a military presence. Additional defenses could be constructed easily. The nearby soldiers could guard it, maintain the surrounding region, and respond immediately if anything unexpected occurred.","Michael’s attention settled on the selected location. For the experiment he intended to conduct, it was about as suitable as he could reasonably ask for.","As for why Michael had not chosen this location immediately, it was simply because it was not the only suitable option. There were several other areas around the capital that could also work, each with its own advantages. Some were more isolated, others had better terrain, while a few were even easier to defend.","Michael had been comparing them without much urgency.","Arianne’s suggestion changed that. There was genuinely nothing wrong with the location she had chosen, and when Michael noticed the expectation in her expression after pointing it out, the decision became much easier.","She clearly wanted to be useful. There was no reason to overcomplicate the decision.","The site would do.","Michael glanced at the marked location one final time before straightening.","\"Let’s go check it out.\"","Arianne barely had time to respond before Michael stood. One arm naturally circled her waist, pulling her close against him.","The next instant, space folded. Both of them disappeared from the office.","When the distortion cleared, they were standing several dozen metres above a vast plain.","The land beneath them was mostly covered in short green grass, trimmed naturally low enough that almost nothing obstructed the view. The terrain was relatively flat, with only a few gentle slopes stretching toward the horizon.","Far in the distance, however, two enormous figures towered into the sky.","They weren’t real creatures but projections. One resembled an enormous armored humanoid holding a spear, while the other looked like some kind of four-legged beast covered in scales.","Both were over a hundred metres tall.","Michael immediately recognized what was happening.","The nearby Silver Guard post was conducting formation training. Unlike ordinary military drills, units at this level often practiced fighting through large-scale arrays."]},{"number":1235,"title":"Chapter 1235: New Title","paragraphs":["Dozens or even hundreds of soldiers could pour their energy into a shared formation while designated individuals acted as the core, allowing them to create enormous projected constructs capable of fighting opponents far beyond the strength of any single participant.","The soldiers themselves effectively became part of the formation materials.","It was one of the methods the empire used to allow weaker soldiers to challenge considerably stronger enemies.","Michael had already asked Jester to research something similar for him. Unfortunately, doing it with undead was far more complicated. His legion wasn’t composed of a single race or even a consistent form of energy.","Some possessed darkness. Others used fire, poison, blood, plants, physical force, or stranger energies like Shojo’s blood energy. Their bodies also differed tremendously and couldn’t simply be placed into one standardized military array and expected to cooperate perfectly.","Layering a shared formation over creatures whose very foundations contradicted one another risked instability rather than synergy, and instability inside a formation meant collapse at best, backlash at worst.","The Silver Guard had it easy by comparison. Every soldier in their formations was, at the core, still human, still built from the same basic template the empire had spent generations refining arrays around.","Michael’s legion had no such luxury. Whatever system eventually emerged would need to account for wildly different bodies, energies, and instincts all at once, which meant it couldn’t simply be borrowed. It would have to be built from scratch.","Theoretically, if Michael could overcome those issues, the final result might be far more powerful than anything the Silver Guard currently used.","But that was for later.","Neither Michael nor Arianne paid much more attention to the distant training.","Michael lowered them toward the plain. Once his feet touched the ground, he opened the relevant interface.","A familiar translucent panel appeared.","[Universal Cornerstone]","[Subsidiary Territorial Anchor]","[You are preparing to establish a Subsidiary Territorial Anchor connected to your Universal Cornerstone.]","[Once established, the Anchor will form a permanent territorial connection with the primary Universal Cornerstone.]","[Confirm suitable placement before proceeding.]","Another projection appeared immediately afterward.","Blue light spread across the ground in front of Michael. It rapidly expanded. Soon, an enormous translucent outline covered a huge section of the plain.","Michael’s eyes narrowed slightly.","The projection showed the exact area the structure would occupy after establishment. It was considerably larger than an ordinary building. Several additional blue lines extended underground as well, showing that whatever was being constructed would affect more than just the visible surface.","Fortunately, there was still more than enough open land.","Michael moved the projected location several times. The blue image followed his will, shifting across the plains while continuously displaying its boundaries. He could place it almost anywhere within the suitable area.","After several adjustments, Michael settled on a position. The projection stabilized.","[Placement Selected.]","[Establish Subsidiary Territorial Anchor?]","Michael glanced toward Arianne and wrapped an arm around her waist again. Both rose into the air.","Once they were several hundred metres above the plain, Michael looked down at the enormous blue outline.","He had come all this way specifically to test this. There was no reason to hesitate now.","Michael selected the option.","[Confirmed.]","[Beginning Subsidiary Territorial Anchor Establishment.]","The moment Michael confirmed his choice, the enormous blue projection beneath them changed.","Light erupted from every line at once.","At first, Michael thought it would simply condense into a structure directly, but the phenomenon was far more familiar than expected.","It reminded him of evolution. Whenever one of his undead underwent a major evolution, its body would usually be swallowed by a brilliant cocoon of light while the surrounding energy gathered toward it.","This looked strangely similar.","Except the light was not white.","A myriad of colours surged across the plain.","Red.","Blue.","Gold.","Green.","Purple.","Black.","Silver.","Countless shades intertwined with one another, forming an enormous radiant cocoon that covered the entire projected area.","The surrounding mana immediately reacted. Streams of energy were dragged from every direction, entering the cocoon continuously. Even the distant projections created by the Silver Guard flickered slightly as some of the surrounding ambient mana was pulled away.","Michael watched carefully.","Fortunately, unlike the evolution of some of his higher-grade undead, the process did not last long.","Within less than a minute, the countless colours suddenly contracted. The light collapsed inward. Then vanished.","What remained beneath them made Michael pause.","A large section of the grassland had completely transformed. Smooth grey stone now covered the ground, polished so perfectly that it almost looked artificial.","At the center of the platform was an enormous magic circle. Its lines were incredibly complicated, extending across almost the entire stone surface in several concentric layers. Strange symbols moved slowly along the engraved pathways, occasionally flashing with faint multicoloured light.","However, neither Michael nor Arianne paid much attention to the formation at first.","Their attention was drawn elsewhere.","A statue stood beyond it. No, calling it merely a statue did not properly describe its scale.","It towered high above the stone platform, easily visible even from hundreds of metres in the air.","And the person depicted was unmistakable.","Michael.","The statue possessed his face, his long hair, his build, and even the ceremonial clothing style he often wore in the Land of Origin.","Its posture, however, was what made Michael’s expression become strange.","The enormous stone Michael stood with his face raised toward the heavens. Both arms were spread wide to either side. It looked almost as though the figure were welcoming the entire sky into its embrace.","Arianne slowly turned her head toward the real Michael. The corner of her lips lifted.","\"Well, it certainly captured your modesty.\"","Michael’s eyebrow twitched.","Arianne’s smile widened.","\"And the likeness is impressive. Very heroic. Very grand.\"","Arianne continued examining it with exaggerated seriousness.","\"I think the people will like it.\"","Michael turned toward her.","\"You’re enjoying this too much.\"","\"Maybe. But while I know you’re very amazing, isn’t this too much? Creating something out of nothing?\"","Before Michael could reply, a translucent panel suddenly appeared directly in front of him.","His expression immediately changed.","The words at the top were different from any normal notification.","[Universal Milestone Achieved]","Michael’s attention locked onto it.","[Congratulations, Michael Norman for accomplishing an unprecedented feat by successfully breaking all universal borders!]","[Title Acquired.]","[Universal Pioneer]"]},{"number":1236,"title":"Chapter 1236: Rank 108","paragraphs":["\"Fuck.\"","The word escaped Michael almost immediately.","At nearly the exact same moment, somewhere unimaginably far away within the Origin Battlefield, the same word left another mouth.","\"Fuck.\"","The second Michael was currently standing inside a completely different arena.","One hand was wrapped around the throat of a strange humanoid creature with smooth pink skin, a narrow waist, and delicate features feminine enough that Michael had initially struggled to determine its gender.","The creature’s feet hung several centimetres above the ground. Its hands were gripping Michael’s wrist, desperately attempting to pull his fingers apart.","Michael had been moments away from ending the fight when the announcement appeared.","[Universal Milestone Announcement]","[Congratulations, Michael Norman, for accomplishing an unprecedented feat by successfully breaking all universal borders!]","[Title Acquired: Universal Pioneer]","Michael stopped moving.","The pink-skinned man hanging from his hand stopped struggling for half a second as well, apparently equally shocked by the sudden universal announcement.","Michael stared at the panel with a darkened expression.","Another announcement? Again?","For a moment, he forgot he was even fighting.","If there was anyone in the universe who wanted less attention than Michael currently did, he genuinely wanted to meet them. Because this was getting ridiculous.","His activities during his previous entry into the Origin Battlefield had already spread across multiple realms. And now this.","The Origin Will had apparently decided that every mildly important thing Michael accomplished needed to be announced to the entire universe. At this point, it was beginning to feel less like an impartial universal existence and more like an enthusiastic gossip who couldn’t keep his name out of its mouth.","Michael’s grip unconsciously tightened.","The pink-skinned man immediately began struggling again.","Only then did Michael remember the creature was still there. He loosened his fingers slightly but didn’t release it. His attention remained fixed on the announcement.","Had he known establishing a subsidiary territory would trigger something like this, Michael genuinely would have reconsidered his approach and waited to allow someone else to discover the function first.","Let another Awakener connect two worlds. Let that person receive the grand universal announcement and all the attention that came with becoming the first. Then Michael could have quietly established his own immediately afterward.","Same result. Far less trouble.","Instead, he had somehow managed to become first again.","The Michael floating above the newly created anchor in the Land of Origin wore almost exactly the same irritated expression.","Michael’s attention finally returned to the creature struggling in his hand.","This was his ninth opponent since beginning his climb.","Rank 108.","More importantly, this was the first opponent Michael had encountered before any of his undead had even appeared.","Normally, Michael wouldn’t have approached someone ranked this high alone. The people within this range of the leaderboard were simply too unpredictable and too strong. Even if Michael was confident in himself, there was no reason to abandon one of his greatest advantages by refusing to summon his legion.","This time, however, circumstances had been different.","The pink-skinned man had clearly only recently finished another battle before accepting Michael’s challenge. Even now, faint injuries remained across his body. His aura was unstable, his breathing uneven, and several parts of the priestly garments covering him had already been torn.","The strangest part was that he was apparently a priest.","Michael still didn’t fully understand how a priest had climbed all the way to Rank 108. But after everything he had seen from Awakeners and being one himself, he also wasn’t particularly surprised.","That was one of the biggest differences between Awakeners and more traditional supernatural systems.","Traditional paths usually had clearer limits. A knight fought like a knight. A mage fought like a mage. A priest supported, healed, purified, or relied on divine arts.","Awakeners were far less restrictive. With Classes, Skills, Attributes, Titles, equipment, racial traits, Talents, and countless other factors layered together, someone could effectively build themselves however they wanted. Two people with the exact same Class could end up fighting completely differently. It was closer to constructing a game build than following a fixed supernatural path.","Apparently, this priest had built himself well enough to enter the Top 110.","There was a reason Michael hadn’t killed him but wanted the other party to surrender instead.","The first was the battlefield.","The arena the priest had selected was almost entirely saturated with darkness. Dark clouds covered the sky, the earth was black and cracked, and streams of dark elemental energy constantly drifted through the air like mist.","For the priest, it was a bizarre choice, since this was only beneficial for his opponent.","The second problem was the priest’s behavior.","Michael had caught him off guard almost immediately after the match began. Yet even after Michael’s hand closed around his throat, the man had focused entirely on trying to break free. He hadn’t attacked. Even now, his hands were only wrapped around Michael’s wrist as he struggled to loosen the grip.","The third clue was the most obvious.","He had accepted Michael’s challenge despite clearly being injured from his previous match.","Taken together, the situation wasn’t difficult to understand.","This man hadn’t accepted because he wanted to fight. He wanted something else. A conversation, perhaps. Maybe a deal. Or maybe some kind of cooperation.","Michael didn’t particularly care which. He had entered the ranking battles for one purpose. To climb as high as possible while he still had challenges available. Stopping in the middle of that to discuss business with a stranger wasn’t part of the plan.","Still, since the priest had shown no intention of killing him, Michael had no reason to respond with unnecessary brutality either. He only needed him to surrender.","Michael’s fingers tightened slightly again.","The pink-skinned priest’s expression immediately became strained.","Michael watched him calmly. He had already made his intentions clear enough through his actions. This wasn’t going to become a negotiation. One of them was leaving the arena with a higher rank. And Michael had no intention of being the one who forfeited."]},{"number":1237,"title":"Chapter 1237: Title Effect","paragraphs":["The priest seemed to notice that Michael’s patience was beginning to disappear. His struggling became more frantic for a moment, but instead of trying to break Michael’s grip again, one of his hands hurriedly rose and made several gestures toward his mouth.","Michael hesitated. Then his fingers loosened slightly.","The priest immediately sucked in a breath. Normally, supernaturals at his level wouldn’t be affected by something as simple as a lack of air, but this bastard had done more than just strangle him. His fingers had been coated in mana, digging into his skin and causing damage.","\"I only wanted to talk.\" The man’s voice was hoarse and shaky, like speaking caused him pain.","Michael said nothing.","The priest glanced at his expression before continuing quickly.","\"I had no intention of fighting you. But... it seems you’re not in the mood for a conversation right now.\"","That was an understatement. Even saying those words made the priest nervous.","His name was Selar, and he came from the small Verith Realm.","Compared to many of the realms represented within the Origin Battlefield, Verith was insignificant. It possessed no Demigod, so it was no great civilization whose influence stretched across entire realms.","At present, Selar himself was the strongest existence within the realm. That technically placed him in a position somewhat similar to a Realm Master.","But only superficially.","A true Realm Master possessed more than raw strength. There was normally some deeper relationship between such an existence and the realm itself, whether through recognition, authority, inheritance, law, or another form of symbolic connection. Selar had none of that. He was simply the strongest person Verith currently possessed.","That was precisely why he had accepted Michael’s challenge. He had only just completed a ranking battle of his own and climbed by a single position. His injuries had not yet recovered, but the moment Michael Norman’s challenge appeared, Selar accepted almost immediately.","Michael’s name had already become too prominent to ignore. Though he didn’t have the resources other civilizations had to know more about this figure, he was still able to learn something after forking out money to obtain information from the Shadow Pavilion, even if it was only superficial knowledge.","Selar had never believed someone attracting that much attention could be ordinary. For a small realm like Verith, meeting such a person wasn’t necessarily a threat. It could be an opportunity.","Selar had hoped to see Michael personally, judge his temperament, and perhaps establish some kind of connection that might benefit Verith in the future. Even something as simple as being remembered favorably by someone with seemingly enormous potential could prove valuable.","He had deliberately selected a battlefield saturated with darkness partly to show that he hadn’t entered with hostile intentions.","He simply hadn’t expected Michael to appear beside him almost immediately after the battle began and seize him by the throat.","Worse, Michael’s reaction had been so fast that Selar hadn’t even finished deciding how he wanted to introduce himself.","Then the universal announcement appeared.","The same man currently holding him in the air had apparently just become the first person to do something again.","Was this truly the Origin Battlefield, or was this Michael Norman’s personal playground?","Selar’s original assessment of Michael rose considerably.","So did his fear.","Fortunately, Michael didn’t seem interested in killing him.","Selar quickly continued.","\"I only wanted to make a friend.\" Selar continued. \"I’ll forfeit, seeing it looks like you have somewhere else to be. If there’s an opportunity in the future, perhaps we can have a more pleasant conversation.\"","Michael studied him for several seconds. That was considerably better than whatever complicated proposal he had expected. Michael’s impression of him improved slightly.","His hand finally left Selar’s throat.","The priest landed lightly on the black ground beneath them, one hand immediately rising to rub his neck.","Michael looked at him.","\"Next time, if you still want to talk, you can challenge me.\"","Selar blinked. Then his expression brightened considerably.","Ranking challenges guaranteed both parties would enter the same arena. More importantly, if Michael was willing to accept one specifically for a conversation, it meant he hadn’t completely rejected the possibility of future contact.","Selar nodded quickly.","\"Of course.\"","A panel appeared in front of him almost immediately.","[Would you like to forfeit the Ranking Challenge?]","Selar selected the option without hesitation.","[Forfeit Confirmed.]","[Opponent Has Forfeited.]","[Challenge Victory Confirmed.]","[Ranking Positions Will Be Exchanged.]","The priest gave him one final respectful nod before disappearing completely.","Michael watched as Selar’s body gradually became surrounded by light.","A moment later, Michael was left alone beneath the dark sky.","His ranking had changed again.","Rank 108.","He only had one challenge left.","At this point, most of Michael’s earlier anger had already faded.","His expression became complicated as he called out a panel of the title he had received.","Even now, when his body in the Land of Origin was checking the same thing, Michael was shocked in both realms.","[Universal Pioneer]","[You have drawn the attention of the Universal Will.]","[Your achievement has been recorded as one beneficial to countless worlds and future civilizations.]","[For successfully opening a path beyond ordinary universal boundaries, you have received its blessing.]","[Effect 1: Universal Law Resonance]","[The effectiveness of your Law is increased by 250% anywhere within the universe.]","[Effect 2: Pioneer’s Choice]","[Whenever you advance through a Major Rank from this point onward, three Traits will be generated from which you may select one to keep]","Silence.","Michael stared at the panel.","The irritation he had felt only a short while ago disappeared almost immediately.","A two-hundred-and-fifty-percent increase to the effectiveness of his Law.","This reminded him of another gift of his that gave a similar effect.","[Gift]: Aurora’s Child","[Description]: Ever since Aurora awakened, she has been searching for a partner to her will. Unfortunately, she has yet to find one. Still, Aurora has not given up. At certain points, she chooses individuals born within her realm as candidates to inherit her will.","[Effect]: Law effectiveness is increased by 200% within Aurora."]},{"number":1238,"title":"Chapter 1238: Transit","paragraphs":["Unlike the gift, which could only be used when he was in Aurora, this title not only provided extra effectiveness but could be used anywhere in the universe.","If he were to use them together in Aurora, while without his enchanter treasure the effect wouldn’t be as monstrous as before, wouldn’t he still be able to boost his Undead High Drake and Undead High Dragon to Demigod for as long as he could manage?","If he included Lunara and Valeria, wouldn’t he have four Demigods he could control at any time?","Even if Aurora as a whole might have more Demigods than him, surely this would make any faction think twice before crossing him, right? In fact, this might even be a universal statement.","However, this was only one benefit, and it wasn’t even the best!","The second effect was even stranger.","From now onward, every time he crossed a Major Rank, the Origin Will would generate three Traits specifically for him and allow him to choose one.","Traits were the closest thing most people could have to Talents. In some cases, depending on their origin and quality, a Trait could even become more useful than a Talent.","Michael didn’t believe that would necessarily be the case for him. Infinite Evolution was already absurd enough. But that didn’t mean he would ever reject more Talent-like abilities.","Certainly not.","Traits could grant entirely new functions, strengthen existing paths, improve affinities, or provide passive effects that remained useful regardless of what Class someone possessed. Some of the better ones could even grow alongside their owner.","That was the part Michael cared about most.","A weak Trait obtained now might not remain weak forever. As his strength increased, some Traits could evolve, deepen, or reveal stronger effects. And if he was going to receive another choice every time he crossed a Major Rank from now onward, then his collection would only continue to grow.","More abilities.","More options.","Michael’s expression gradually changed.","The Universal Will had certainly made a lot of noise when granting him this reward. Far too much noise for his liking. His name had once again been thrown across the universe, and countless people who might never have cared about him before would now know that Michael Norman had accomplished something important enough to continuously receive universal recognition.","But looking at the effects of Universal Pioneer, Michael couldn’t deny one thing.","The reward was really good. Very, very good.","So good, in fact, that the thoughts he’d had only minutes ago about happily giving this achievement to someone else had quietly disappeared.","Michael exhaled slowly and closed the title panel.","As tempting as it was to just not do anything for now, one challenge remained. He had already used nine of his ten monthly ranking challenges. Once the last one was consumed, he would no longer be able to initiate another ranking battle until the next month.","There was no reason to stop now.","Michael turned his attention toward the scattered undead waiting throughout the dark battlefield and began recalling them one after another.","Meanwhile, in the Land of Origin, Arianne was looking at Michael with obvious concern.","His earlier outburst had caught her completely off guard. Michael wasn’t someone who normally cursed so openly, or at all. At least not around her.","Seeing him suddenly curse had been unusual enough to worry her. Most of the time, he carried himself with a grace that made it easy to forget how young he actually was. To be honest, she believed it was mostly because he had a bit of a loner personality and was surrounded by undead all the time.","Arianne lightly touched his arm.","\"Are you alright?\"","Her voice finally pulled Michael’s attention completely away from the title.","He looked toward her before giving a small smile.","\"I’m fine.\"","If anything, after seeing the rewards attached to Universal Pioneer, he was considerably better than he had been a while earlier.","Arianne studied him for another moment before accepting the answer.","Michael then turned his attention elsewhere.","By now, both Michael and Arianne had already descended to the ground beside the newly created Subsidiary Territorial Anchor.","At some point while he had been distracted, a group of soldiers had gathered not far from them. He had sensed them well before they arrived and didn’t consider them a threat, so they hadn’t broken him out of his thoughts.","Several dozen Silver Guard soldiers stood near the edge of the enormous stone platform.","Their presence wasn’t surprising. The creation of the anchor had been anything but subtle. Even the military formations they had been training with had briefly flickered because of it. If the nearby soldiers hadn’t noticed something of that scale, Michael would have seriously questioned what exactly they were being trained for.","In truth, they had noticed almost immediately. The reason they hadn’t rushed over sooner was simply because their commanding officer wasn’t currently at the post. He had traveled into the imperial city earlier that day.","The soldiers left behind had initially maintained their distance while sending word to their commander and organizing themselves in case the phenomenon turned out to be dangerous. Only after determining that whatever had appeared wasn’t immediately attacking the surrounding area had they begun approaching.","The soldiers stopped at a respectful distance.","Their attention moved repeatedly between Michael, Arianne, the enormous magic circle carved into the ground, and finally the gigantic statue towering above everything.","The last one received considerably more looks than the others.","Michael noticed, his eyes slowly moving toward the statue as well.","The stone version of himself was still gazing proudly toward the heavens with both arms spread wide.","A panel appeared before him.","[Subsidiary Territorial Anchor]","[Grade: Legendary]","[Function: Universal Transit]","[The Subsidiary Territorial Anchor may establish direct transportation to the primary Universal Cornerstone or any other Subsidiary Territorial Anchor connected to it.]","[Transportation Cost: Variable]","[Energy Requirement may be fulfilled through any energy source.]","*","A/N: Thank you for the continued support!!"]},{"number":1239,"title":"Chapter 1239: Energy","paragraphs":["The Legendary grade itself didn’t surprise Michael much.","There were no stars attached to it, but this wasn’t the first time he had encountered something like that. The Universal Cornerstone itself was also listed as Legendary without possessing any stars.","And if Michael had to judge purely from what it had already demonstrated, calling the cornerstone merely Legendary ★★★ would almost feel insulting. Its functions had probably already gone far beyond what he normally associated with treasures of that grade.","He might not have enough experience to say this, but he did have a Legendary treasure that contained a whole world, and he still didn’t think it could be compared to the Universal Cornerstone.","Perhaps that was simply because it had not crossed whatever invisible threshold separated Legendary from Mythical. If so, then the system could only classify it as Legendary regardless of how absurdly close it stood to the next grade.","That explanation made enough sense to Michael, especially when he considered what the Universal Cornerstone could actually do.","Now this Subsidiary Territorial Anchor had inherited the same strange starless Legendary classification.","Putting aside the obviously ridiculous cornerstone for a moment, wasn’t this thing essentially a teleportation port? A teleportation port capable of crossing worlds.","Michael reopened the Universal Cornerstone’s status and focused on one section.","[Universal Cornerstone]","[Territory Level: 1]","[Available Subsidiary Territorial Anchors: 3]","Michael’s eyes lingered on the number.","Three more.","So even at Level One, the cornerstone allowed him to establish four subsidiary territories in total. One had already been used here in the Land of Origin. That left three.","If each one functioned exactly like this, then Michael could establish three additional universal transit points in completely different worlds and connect all of them together through the same network.","Aurora was the obvious candidate for one. That alone would mean direct transportation between Aurora, the Land of Origin, and the Origin Battlefield without relying on Michael personally opening a path.","And he would still have two anchors remaining.","The possibilities immediately expanded.","Another allied realm. A strategically important world. A resource-rich location. Even some distant territory he hadn’t discovered yet.","As long as a Subsidiary Territorial Anchor could be established there, all of those places could effectively become neighbors. Distance across the universe would stop mattering in the conventional sense.","The only real cost was energy, but according to the panel, it didn’t even demand one specific type. As long as the anchor recognized it as usable energy, the formation could consume it to power transportation.","Michael looked down at the enormous magic circle again. He wanted to see with his own eyes exactly how the thing worked.","With that thought, Michael turned toward the Silver Guard soldiers waiting nearby. His gaze settled on the strongest among them.","The man immediately stepped forward. Michael gave a slight gesture, prompting him to introduce himself.","The commander straightened before speaking.","\"Commander Aldric Thorne, Your Majesty. Acting head of the Third Silver Guard Training Post.\"","He then turned to Arianne and added, \"Greetings to you, Highness,\" to which Arianne happily waved at him with a little anxiousness.","Being with Michael had exposed her to many things, but when it came to facing powerful people, she still preferred communicating with Michael’s undead over real people.","This man should not be weaker than Princess Priscilla, who she looked up to. Seeing him greet her with respect made her nerves crack.","Michael nodded.","\"Please head to the palace and ask the stewards to prepare ten crates of high-quality mana crystals and another ten crates of high-quality elemental crystals. Bring them here.\"","Aldric immediately bowed.","\"At once, Your Majesty.\"","Space distorted around him. A second later, he disappeared.","Michael watched the place where the commander had been standing before returning his attention to the Subsidiary Territorial Anchor.","That was precisely why he had sent Aldric himself despite the man being the highest-ranking officer currently present.","The commander possessed spatial abilities as a Rank Three existence. For running an urgent errand between this location and the imperial capital, it made him far more useful than anyone else here.","There was little reason to send several soldiers riding or flying back when Aldric could simply cross the distance almost immediately.","The remaining Silver Guards stayed where they were.","Michael stepped closer to the enormous magic circle. The smooth stone beneath his feet looked almost mundane despite the absurd function hidden within it.","Arianne followed beside him.","Michael wanted to test several things before deciding exactly how important these anchors would become to him.","First was the actual energy consumption.","The panel had only described the transportation cost as variable. That could mean almost anything.","Transporting one ordinary person might require a handful of mana crystals.","Transporting Michael himself could require considerably more.","Rank, distance, quantity, mass, and even the difference between worlds could potentially influence the cost.","Then there was the question of elemental energy. The description specifically stated that any energy source could be used.","Michael intended to confirm how literal that was.","If ordinary mana crystals worked, that was already useful. If elemental crystals worked just as easily, then the empire wouldn’t need to create some specialized fuel purely for the anchor. And if other forms of stored energy could be substituted later, the structure would become even easier to maintain.","At that point, what would matter most was cost effectiveness.","More importantly, Michael wanted to know what happened on the other side. Could the destination reject a transfer? Could someone use one anchor to reach another without Michael being present? Those questions mattered considerably more than simply proving that teleportation was possible.","It didn’t take long for Commander Aldric to return.","Space rippled a short distance from the gathered soldiers before his figure stepped out, followed almost immediately by twenty large reinforced crates that appeared across the grass.","Ten contained mana crystals. The moment their lids were opened, dense light spilled out, red in some crystals and blue in others.","Each crystal was roughly the size of a thumb or larger, translucent and almost perfectly clear, with concentrated mana flowing through the interior like mist trapped inside glass.","Even from several metres away, the surrounding mana became noticeably denser."]},{"number":1240,"title":"Chapter 1240: Points","paragraphs":["The other ten crates contained elemental crystals. Their appearance was far more varied. Some burned with faint red light without producing heat.","Others were deep blue, with tiny traces of frost gathering against the wooden crates around them.","There were green crystals carrying dense wind energy, golden ones that released a faint warmth, earthy brown crystals, and several darker varieties whose exact affinities were harder to determine at a glance.","The Silver Guard soldiers visibly reacted. Several swallowed unconsciously.","Resources of this quality were not something ordinary soldiers could casually obtain in large amounts.","For those below Rank Three, crystals like these still possessed considerable value for cultivation. They could accelerate mana accumulation, help recover depleted reserves, and support breakthroughs.","Even among the Silver Guard, most wouldn’t casually waste such materials.","Only Aldric appeared completely composed. At this stage, all he needed to concern himself with was compressing his Law to completion.","Michael approached the crates and casually picked up one of the mana crystals. He rolled it between his fingers.","The crystal was dense, clean, and contained very little impurity.","Good quality.","He picked up two elemental crystals as well, briefly examining their energy before nodding.","Michael then turned toward the gathered soldiers. His eyes moved across them one by one. The Silver Guards immediately straightened.","Michael pointed toward one of the weakest soldiers present.","\"You.\"","The man stepped forward.","Then Michael selected another. This time, one of the strongest people present aside from Aldric.","After that, he chose three of the weaker Silver Guards and had them stand together. Then another group of three, this time made up of some of the strongest soldiers currently present.","Finally, Michael gestured toward Aldric and had him stand alone in a separate position.","The arrangement quickly became clear.","One weak individual. One strong individual. Three weak individuals. Three strong individuals. And finally the Rank Three commander.","Michael wanted comparison points. If the transportation cost really changed depending on strength, quantity, or both, this would give him enough information to begin understanding the pattern.","The selected soldiers were confused. None of them knew exactly what Michael intended to do with them, especially with twenty crates of valuable crystals sitting beside a gigantic unfamiliar formation.","But beneath that confusion was an obvious trace of excitement.","It had only been a few months since the empire changed rulers. At first, uncertainty had naturally spread throughout the military. They had served one royal family for generations, only to watch that family fall and an outsider seize the throne with frightening ease.","There had been fear. Suspicion. Resentment from some. Caution from almost everyone.","But once the fighting ended and normal life resumed, the reality had been far less terrible than many expected. Michael had not stripped the empire apart simply because he possessed the power to do so.","For most ordinary soldiers, life had continued. Training continued. Pay continued. Their families remained untouched. The empire remained stable.","That alone had softened many initial fears.","More importantly, there was one fact nobody within the military or common populace could ignore. Their new ruler was vastly more powerful than the previous royal family.","That didn’t automatically create loyalty. People didn’t abandon generations of attachment simply because someone stronger appeared. Especially not soldiers.","But strength still mattered. A strong ruler inspired confidence. And when the difference became large enough, confidence could gradually turn into awe.","Michael had already approached that point.","Several of the soldiers had heard rumors of what he could do. Some had personally witnessed his \"undead,\" which many still didn’t know the true nature of, during the takeover.","Now they had just watched him create an enormous unknown structure out of nothing while a statue of him appeared beside it.","Being personally selected by such a ruler, even if only for an experiment they didn’t understand, was enough to make several of them visibly excited.","Michael paid little attention to that reaction. His focus remained on the test.","After a moment of thought, Michael pointed toward the weakest soldier he had selected.","\"Get on the platform.\"","The man immediately obeyed. He stepped onto the enormous stone surface and stopped near the center of the magic circle.","Michael’s attention shifted inward. Almost immediately, the Subsidiary Territorial Anchor responded.","[Target Detected.]","[Permission Requirement Satisfied.]","[Select Destination.]","Another panel unfolded beneath it. There was only one option.","[The Eternal Crown]","Michael’s eyes paused on the name. That was the territory surrounding his main Universal Cornerstone in the Origin Battlefield.","Before Michael could select it, another notification appeared.","[Current Subsidiary Territory Has Not Been Named.]","[Please Assign A Territory Name.]","Michael stared at it briefly. After only a moment of consideration, he entered a name.","[Territory Name Confirmed.]","[The Eternal Crown Empire]","Simple. Perhaps a little too simple. But Michael didn’t care. It clearly distinguished this subsidiary territory from the Eternal Crown itself, and that was all he needed.","He returned to the previous interface.","[Available Destination]","[The Eternal Crown]","Michael selected it. The response came immediately.","[Insufficient Energy Points.]","[Please Recharge Subsidiary Territorial Anchor.]","Michael’s expression shifted.","Another smaller notice appeared beneath the warning.","[To Convert External Energy Into Energy Points, Present A Compatible Energy Source To The Dominion Conduit.]","Michael looked toward the enormous statue. A faint symbol had appeared at its base.","So that was the Dominion Conduit.","Michael raised one hand. A high-grade mana crystal floated from the nearby crate and flew toward the statue. The moment it crossed the invisible boundary surrounding the base, the crystal crumbled completely.","A new number appeared on the panel.","[Energy Points: 1]","Michael stared.","\"...\"","One point?","He looked back toward the crate. That had been a high-grade mana crystal.","Mana crystals generally fell into several accepted quality levels. Low Grade. Mid Grade. High Grade. And above them were even more valuable varieties.","There was technically another category beneath Low Grade, but most supernaturals barely bothered calling those proper mana crystals. Their purity was so poor that they were usually referred to as defective crystals instead.","Yet a high-grade mana crystal had provided exactly one Energy Point. From what he could tell, to trade for anything, he’d need these Energy Points."]},{"number":1241,"title":"Chapter 1241: Demonic Exchange Vaule","paragraphs":["Michael’s expectations immediately changed.","He pulled an elemental crystal from another crate. This one contained concentrated fire energy. It floated toward the Dominion Conduit.","The result was noticeably better.","[Energy Points Gained: 3]","Michael’s eyes narrowed. He tried another elemental crystal.","Again.","[Energy Points Gained: 3]","So ordinary elemental crystals of this quality were worth roughly three times as much as pure mana crystals.","That at least made some sense. Elemental crystals contained not merely energy but a more concentrated and specialized form of it.","Michael decided to test with an even rarer element. Unfortunately, the only one available in sufficient quality for immediate testing was a dark-element crystal.","Michael fed it into the Dominion Conduit. The crystal vanished.","[Energy Points Gained: 4]","Michael stared at the number.","Though it was higher, it still wasn’t particularly impressive.","He looked toward the soldier standing nervously on the formation. At this point, Michael had already realized something.","Universal transportation was expensive. Potentially very expensive.","Even if transporting a weak individual ultimately cost relatively few Energy Points, the resources being converted into those points were not cheap.","And if stronger individuals required substantially more, then moving Rank Three or Rank Four existences across worlds could easily become a luxury.","Michael nevertheless continued and attempted the transfer again.","[Insufficient Energy Points.]","He added another. Then another. Still insufficient.","Eventually, after consuming enough crystals to bring the stored amount to a hundred, the interface finally changed.","[Required Energy Available.]","[Target: 1]","[Destination: The Eternal Crown]","[Energy Cost: 100]","[Initiate Transfer?]","Michael’s heart ached slightly at the number.","One hundred Energy Points.","One had to understand just how ridiculous the value of those crystals actually was. The normal exchange between grades was roughly one hundred to one.","A single High-Grade Mana Crystal could be exchanged for around one hundred Mid-Grade Mana Crystals. And a single Mid-Grade Mana Crystal could, in turn, be exchanged for around one hundred Low-Grade Mana Crystals.","The difference was enormous. One High-Grade Mana Crystal represented a truly significant amount of lower-grade resources.","Michael’s expression became complicated.","Expensive. Very expensive.","But after thinking about it from another angle, it suddenly stopped feeling quite as outrageous.","This was not ordinary teleportation. It was not even long-distance teleportation across a continent. It was dimensional transportation across entirely separate worlds.","The destination was the Origin Battlefield. A place that normally couldn’t simply be entered through conventional spatial methods.","From that perspective, one hundred Energy Points no longer sounded completely unreasonable. If anything, the fact that such a transfer could be performed at all using ordinary energy resources was already absurd.","Michael glanced at the open crates. There was little point being conservative now. He needed proper testing data.","Michael raised his hand. Hundreds of crystals began floating out of the crates at once.","The soldiers nearby watched in stunned silence as streams of blue, red, green, gold, black, and countless other lights rose into the air.","The crystals formed several rotating rivers of energy before surging toward the Dominion Conduit. The moment they entered its range, they began disintegrating one after another.","Crack.","Crack.","Crack.","The sounds overlapped continuously.","The number on the panel began rising rapidly.","[Energy Points: 127]","[Energy Points: 241]","[Energy Points: 468]","[Energy Points: 903]","[Energy Points: 1,537]","Putting Michael’s expression aside, even the Silver Guard soldiers and Arianne, who couldn’t see the panel and had been excited earlier, now looked pained. They knew exactly how much wealth was disappearing before their eyes.","Michael felt it too. But he didn’t stop.","Soon, the final crystals disappeared into the Dominion Conduit. The twenty crates were empty.","Michael looked at the panel again.","[Energy Points: 8,720]","At least now, he had enough Energy Points to properly see what the Universal Cornerstone’s transport network could really do.","Michael did not initiate the transfer immediately. Instead, he turned toward the other soldiers he had selected. The first test had already established the minimum cost for a single weaker individual. Now he wanted to know how much personal strength actually mattered.","He gestured for the stronger Silver Guard to step onto the formation beside the first. The man obeyed.","Michael mentally adjusted the transfer target.","[Targets: 2]","[Destination: The Eternal Crown]","[Energy Cost: 200]","Michael paused.","Exactly one hundred more.","His eyes moved toward the first group of three weaker soldiers. They stepped onto the platform.","[Targets: 5]","[Destination: The Eternal Crown]","[Energy Cost: 500]","Still one hundred per person.","Michael’s interest grew. He immediately added the three strongest Silver Guards he had selected. These soldiers were considerably stronger than the first group, yet the moment all three entered the formation, the result remained strangely simple.","[Targets: 8]","[Destination: The Eternal Crown]","[Energy Cost: 800]","\"It’s uniform?\"","So at least among everyone currently standing on the platform, personal strength made absolutely no difference.","The weakest soldier required one hundred Energy Points. The strongest soldier required one hundred. Adding weaker soldiers cost another hundred each. Adding stronger soldiers also cost another hundred each.","Michael’s gaze finally moved toward Commander Aldric.","The Rank Three existence had been waiting beside the platform. Michael gestured. Aldric stepped forward.","The moment his feet touched the enormous magic circle, the panel changed.","[Targets: 9]","[Destination: The Eternal Crown]","[Energy Cost: 1,800]","Michael’s eyelid twitched.","The commander had added one thousand Energy Points by himself.","There it was.","So strength did matter. It simply didn’t matter by individuals, but by rank. Everyone beneath whatever threshold Aldric had crossed cost one hundred Energy Points each. A Rank Three individual, however, immediately required one thousand.","Ten times more.","Would a Rank Four cost 10,000 Energy Points?","Michael looked at the remaining balance.","[Energy Points: 8,720]","[Energy Cost: 1,800]","His heart hurt again. Nearly one fifth of everything he had just poured into the structure was about to disappear in a single experiment.","But Michael had already gone this far. Stopping because the test was expensive would make sacrificing twenty crates of crystals in the first place rather pointless."]},{"number":1242,"title":"Chapter 1242: Another Beginning","paragraphs":["There was also something else he had learned while manipulating the formation. Not everyone could simply walk onto the platform and decide to activate it.","The moment Michael interacted with the Subsidiary Territorial Anchor, he could clearly sense the authority structure built into it.","Permission was required. Michael, as the owner of the Universal Cornerstone, possessed absolute authority over the entire network.","At present, only two people possessed authority directly below his own. Their permissions were still considerably more limited than Michael’s, but they could operate important functions of the territory in his absence.","This discovery immediately removed one of Michael’s earlier concerns. An enemy couldn’t simply capture this place, step onto the formation, and casually teleport straight into the Eternal Crown. At least not through ordinary means.","Michael looked toward the soldiers standing across the enormous formation. Most were visibly curious now. They still had no idea where Michael intended to send them.","Michael finally selected the destination.","[The Eternal Crown]","A second confirmation appeared.","[Targets: 9]","[Transfer Cost: 1,800 Energy Points]","[Current Energy Points: 8,720]","[Initiate Universal Transfer?]","Michael accepted.","[Confirmed.]","The change was immediate.","The countless markings covering the enormous magic circle lit up simultaneously. Multicoloured light raced through the engraved lines, starting from the outermost ring before rapidly converging toward the center.","The soldiers looked down in surprise. Aldric’s expression became considerably more serious.","Space around the platform began to distort. There was no tearing sensation or unstable spatial crack. Instead, the entire area containing the nine soldiers seemed to become increasingly unreal.","Their figures blurred, becoming translucent.","Michael watched closely. Arianne stepped slightly nearer to him as the light intensified.","The formation flashed and nine figures disappeared. One moment they had been standing on the platform. The next, the entire formation was empty.","Michael immediately looked at the panel.","[Universal Transfer Successful.]","[Destination: The Eternal Crown]","[Energy Points Consumed: 1,800]","[Remaining Energy Points: 6,920]","At the same time, he opened the territorial panel for his territory in the Origin Battlefield and saw nine unregistered life forms had immediately been registered.","It was without a doubt. Michael had once again succeeded in bringing people out of the Land of Origin to another realm, but this time the will of the world acknowledged it.","For the nine soldiers, the experience was completely different from what the ones outside saw.","The moment the formation activated, the world around them vanished. One instant, they were standing beneath the enormous statue in the Land of Origin. The next, they were somewhere else.","Or perhaps nowhere at all.","Surrounding them was complete darkness.","Eight of the nine soldiers immediately tensed. There was no sky above them. No earth beneath them. No horizon. Nothing.","They were suspended inside what appeared to be a transparent spherical bubble drifting through an endless black space.","Several soldiers instinctively reached for their weapons. One of the weaker men took a step backward, only to immediately stop when he realized there was nowhere to step toward.","Fortunately, the transparent barrier beneath his feet still gave him something solid to stand on.","The soldiers quickly gathered closer together.","Only Commander Aldric remained relatively calm. His expression had changed, however.","He recognized this place. Or at least, he believed he did.","The void.","Aldric raised one hand and tried to gather energy, but nothing happened. His eyebrows slowly drew together. He could still sense his own power perfectly. The problem was the bubble.","His perception also couldn’t penetrate it. Every attempt to extend his senses beyond the transparent barrier was immediately blocked, as though the sphere existed completely independently from whatever surrounded it.","Aldric had entered the second layer of the void many times. For someone who cultivated spatial abilities, it was unavoidable. The void known to most people within the Land of Origin was divided into two accessible layers.","Aldric had entered the Inner Void countless times. That was why he had assumed this darkness belonged to it.","But something was wrong. The scale felt different. The emptiness felt deeper. Even with his senses blocked, the instinct he had developed through years of manipulating space told him that this was not quite the Inner Void he knew.","What Aldric didn’t know was that his confusion came from a simple limitation.","The people of the Land of Origin only knew of two layers. Those from civilizations outside understood that the void was generally divided into three.","The Surface Layer. The Inner Layer. And beyond both of them, the Deep Layer.","The third was fundamentally different. It was the layer through which the boundaries separating worlds and realms could truly be crossed. Ordinary spatial teleportation could move someone across a city. To cross from one independent realm into another required reaching the third layer.","And that was something the natives of the Land of Origin simply could not do.","Their civilization possessed spatial cultivators. They possessed secret realms, spatial treasures, and countless methods involving space. Yet there was an invisible ceiling above all of them.","To most inhabitants, there was nothing unusual about their world. The Land of Origin was enormous. Its territories seemed almost endless. Its resources were abundant. Why would they ever think of themselves as trapped?","Only those with knowledge of the greater universe could understand the truth.","The Land of Origin was miraculous. But for those born within it, it was also something resembling a cage. Its natives could explore its vast lands. They could grow stronger. But reaching beyond the world itself was another matter entirely.","Until Michael.","The nine soldiers standing inside the transparent bubble had no idea that they were currently experiencing something almost no native of their world had ever experienced before.","They didn’t know that the darkness outside the bubble was carrying them through boundaries their strongest spatial experts couldn’t cross.","They didn’t know that the place waiting for them ahead wasn’t another region of their empire.","It wasn’t another continent. It wasn’t even another hidden world attached to their own.","For the first time in their lives, all nine of them were leaving the Land of Origin.","They were about to see a wider universe.","This was only the beginning."]},{"number":1243,"title":"Chapter 1243: Awakening [1]","paragraphs":["Soon, the darkness around them began to change.","At first, it was subtle. A faint distortion appeared beyond the transparent bubble, like ripples spreading through ink. Then light appeared.","The soldiers barely had time to react before the black void surrounding them folded inward, and the bubble vanished.","Their surroundings changed completely.","For several seconds, none of the nine moved.","The first thing they saw was a massive black pillar rising into the sky. It stood not far from them, tall and unnaturally smooth, its dark surface carrying faint patterns that seemed to shift whenever they looked at them too closely.","Beyond it, further into the territory, stood an enormous temple. Calling it magnificent almost felt insufficient. Its architecture was unlike anything the soldiers had seen in the empire.","The structure towered over the surrounding land, ancient and imposing, with countless intricate designs covering its walls and pillars.","Several of the soldiers instinctively stared. Then something else hit them.","Mana. Dense mana flooded into their bodies the moment they appeared.","The reaction among the eight weaker soldiers was immediate. Several staggered, with one dropping to a knee. Another inhaled sharply as though he had suddenly been submerged underwater. Their bodies greedily absorbed the surrounding energy without permission. For a few seconds, they almost looked drunk.","The mana density here was simply too high compared to what they were accustomed to. Their circulation immediately became chaotic as their bodies attempted to adapt to an environment where every breath contained far more energy than what they normally experienced.","Commander Aldric reacted much faster. Even then, his expression changed.","The mana here was very dense. Far denser than most regions he had visited within the empire. Even certain high-level cultivation grounds didn’t maintain this kind of concentration across such a wide open area.","His first thought was that this was a secret realm. Their lord must have somehow transported them into some exceptionally high-grade secret realm.","It made sense, given how this place seemed to be like some ruins. At least, that was the only explanation Aldric could currently think of.","He turned slowly.","That was when he noticed the wall.","Far in the distance, an enormous structure cut across the landscape. It rose more than a hundred metres into the air. From this distance alone, Aldric could already tell that it was absurdly thick.","His expression became increasingly serious.","Aldric was just about to spread his senses again when space shifted in front of him.","Two figures appeared. Michael stood before them. Beside him was Arianne.","\"I can understand if there’s a uniform price below Rank Three, but why was I priced at 10,000 points? What’s this nonsensical discrimination?!\"","The nine soldiers could not understand what their lord was talking about.","Points? Ten thousand? Discrimination?","Still, confusion did not stop discipline. Aldric straightened first and brought a fist to his chest. The other eight followed almost immediately.","\"Your Majesty.\"","At this point, even Aldric was looking at Michael differently.","Before today, he had already understood that Michael was powerful. Everyone in the military did. Even Rank Three existences treated his name carefully.","But this was different.","This looked like something only gods could do.","Arianne found herself looking at Michael with even more admiration as well.","She had already seen many ridiculous things since becoming involved with him. The Mausoleum. His undead. His abilities. Yet somehow, he kept revealing something new.","She had several questions she desperately wanted to ask. Where exactly were they? What had that strange dark space been? Could anyone use the structure?","But with the soldiers still present, she kept everything to herself.","Michael, meanwhile, looked around.","Nothing had changed. Everything was normal.","Except for one problem.","There was no option to send the nine soldiers back to the Land of Origin. The Eternal Crown Empire appeared within the territorial network, but there was no usable departure point here corresponding to the Subsidiary Territorial Anchor he had created there.","Michael finally understood. He had misunderstood the structure slightly.","The Universal Cornerstone itself was the heart of the network, but it was not meant to act as a normal transit platform.","To send people from one territory to another, both sides required an actual Subsidiary Territorial Anchor. The cornerstone established and governed the connection. The anchors handled transportation.","Fortunately, the solution was simple.","Michael turned toward the nine soldiers and Arianne. Space folded around all of them. The next moment, they disappeared from the central region.","When their surroundings stabilized again, they stood within the Outer Area of the Eternal Crown.","Michael deliberately chose a central location.","[Establish Subsidiary Territorial Anchor?]","[Confirmed.]","The soldiers barely had enough time to recover from yet another instantaneous relocation before light began spreading across the ground.","Aldric’s eyes widened at the phenomenon appearing before him.","When the light disappeared, a smooth stone platform occupied the land. A vast magic circle covered its surface. And behind it stood another gigantic statue of Michael with his face raised toward the sky and both arms spread apart.","Several soldiers looked from the statue to Michael.","Michael ignored them. He immediately opened its interface.","[Subsidiary Territorial Anchor]","[Connected Territories: 2]","[The Eternal Crown Empire]","[Energy Points: 2,930]","Michael’s eyes sharpened.","The Energy Points were still there.","He had half expected this newly constructed anchor to possess an empty reserve and require another twenty crates of crystals before he could do anything. Instead, the remaining 6,920 Energy Points had carried over.","It seems the energy reserve wasn’t local but belonged to the entire territorial network.","Michael’s earlier pain over the crystals faded slightly.","Michael turned toward the nine soldiers. They had already served their purpose. He selected all nine.","[Targets: 9]","[Destination: The Eternal Crown Empire]","[Transfer Cost: 1,800 Energy Points]","The formation activated.","This time, none of the soldiers panicked when light surrounded them, although several still looked visibly tense.","Their bodies became translucent. Then disappeared.","Back in the Land of Origin, the first Subsidiary Territorial Anchor lit up. Several moments later, nine figures appeared across the magic circle.","Aldric immediately spread his senses.","It was a familiar land.","They were back."]},{"number":1244,"title":"Chapter 1244: Awakening [2]","paragraphs":["Aldric remained still for a moment after confirming they had truly returned.","The nearby soldiers, however, were far less composed. All of them were staring openly at the nine who had just appeared from the enormous formation.","Aldric finally recovered. His expression became stern as he turned toward the gathered Silver Guards.","\"Enough staring.\"","The soldiers immediately straightened.","Aldric pointed toward the surrounding area.","\"Establish a temporary camp around this location. I want a wall posted immediately, and no one approaches the structure without permission.\"","The soldiers responded at once. The earlier curiosity disappeared beneath military discipline.","Groups quickly separated and got to work. To create a wall quickly, it was better to have a mage, so a group headed off to call some from the capital. Mages were rare in the military, so they could only ask for external help.","A few remained close to the platform itself, though none dared step onto it.","All of this was Michael’s instruction to Aldric before sending him and the others back. Further instructions would come after Michael returned.","Aldric took the order to heart, though most of his seriousness was still rooted in the thought that the place he had gone to was some extraordinarily powerful secret realm, and the strange structure acted as an entrance that his emperor’s mysterious abilities allowed him to open and close wherever he wanted.","Far away from him, inside the Eternal Crown, Arianne had finally stopped holding back.","\"Is this a secret realm?\"","Her eyes continued moving across the surrounding territory.","\"If someone cultivated here, wouldn’t it be like getting twice the result for half the work?\"","Michael’s expression became slightly strange. He looked at her for a moment before activating Detect.","A familiar panel appeared.","[Beast Tamer Level 19]","Only a few months had passed since Arianne’s death and resurrection, yet she had already climbed back to around the level she possessed before.","Choosing to continue her previous profession wasn’t particularly surprising, as it was familiar and easier to get back into.","Michael didn’t stop her, as there was no reason to.","Before the Origin Battlefield, Michael’s intention for Arianne was relatively simple. He wanted her to become stronger eventually. Not because he expected her to fight beside him, but because a higher strength meant a longer lifespan.","It was the same plan Michael had for Aunt Mia as well. Lily would have been included if she failed to awaken after eighteen.","Before the revelation of the Origin Battlefield, there hadn’t been a better plan. But now, whenever he thought back to it after claiming the Universal Cornerstone, a feeling of conflict came to him.","Michael’s expression softened slightly before he answered Arianne.","\"You can call it a secret realm, but it’s far more mysterious than one.\"","He gestured toward the surrounding territory.","\"This is the Origin Battlefield. Normally, only Awakeners can enter.\"","The term Awakeners made Arianne pause.","She was already familiar with the word. When Michael had first confessed everything to her, Awakeners had been among the many truths he revealed.","They were people who, after reaching a certain age, possessed a small chance of awakening something called a class and other abilities that did not exist naturally within the Land of Origin.","At the time, finding out that her place of birth was somewhat seen as a sort of false, game-like world had been one of the hardest things for Arianne to accept. But after enough repeated proof of being able to leave her world, disbelief had eventually become pointless.","Arianne understood what Awakeners were. What confused her now was this: if the Origin Battlefield was supposedly a place only Awakeners could enter, why was she standing here?","Arianne’s gaze slowly shifted toward the enormous statue of Michael behind them.","Michael noticed immediately.","\"Yes. With this structure, I can indeed bring ordinary people to this place. But to be honest, I still don’t know exactly what I’m supposed to do with it.\"","Michael looked at Arianne for a moment before suddenly asking,","\"What do you think about Awakeners?\"","Arianne was startled, clearly not expecting the question. She then thought about it seriously.","\"You’re the only one I’ve actually met, so I can’t say I understand them very well.\"","Michael waited.","Arianne looked toward the distant walls.","\"But from everything you’ve told me, they’re amazing. They can become stronger faster. They have those things called Classes, Skills, and access to places like this and beyond.\"","\"I’d be lying if I said there wasn’t a little bitterness in me when I think of them. It’s enviable.\"","Arianne smiled faintly.","\"They really are chosen ones, aren’t they? Favored by the world.\"","Michael didn’t immediately respond.","From the perspective of someone born in the Land of Origin, or in the universe in general, that description was not entirely wrong. Awakeners received opportunities most ordinary supernaturals could only dream of. Even though the gap lessened drastically at Rank Three, Awakeners still possessed a great advantage, especially in terms of advancement.","After a few seconds of silence, Arianne turned back toward Michael. Her smile grew.","\"But even among them I somehow feel none of them can really compare to you.\"","Michael laughed softly.","\"That’s not true.\"","Arianne only smiled back. She didn’t argue and continued admiring the scenery around them.","After a while, Michael suddenly asked,","\"What if you could become an Awakener?\"","Michael continued before she could answer.","\"If there was actually a way for you to awaken, would you take it?\"","Arianne stared at him with an odd expression.","\"Of course. Who would say no to such a thing?\"","Michael had expected that answer so he wasn’t surprised.","Arianne studied him for another moment before looking away.","\"I’m already older than eighteen, and I wasn’t even born in your world, so I never got the chance naturally. Having a chance to be like you sounds really nice.\"","**","A/N: Sorry for the late update dear readers and happy next month to everyone! Plesss vote to support this poor starving author!!!?"]},{"number":1245,"title":"Chapter 1245: Awakening [3]","paragraphs":["\"Still, it’s not that bad. Thanks to you, I have another life.\"","Arianne’s fingers brushed lightly against her chest.","\"This body is much better than my old one. Even without this level-up ability you gave me, just with meditation I think I might be able to break Princess Priscilla’s record and become the youngest great mage back in Lionheart.\"","Thanks to being something akin to a tamed existence, Arianne, just like any of Michael’s undead, was able to level up through experience points.","In fact, there was actually no difference between her and an Awakener on paper, if one considered her ability to level up and learn skills quickly.","Michael remained silent for a moment before looking directly at her.","\"What if I told you I could actually make you an Awakener?\"","Arianne froze. Her hand, which had still been resting lightly against her chest, stopped moving.","\"You can?\"","Michael didn’t answer straight away.","Ever since he obtained the Awakening Temple, a question had been bothering him.","Before then, his plans for Arianne and Aunt Mia had been simple enough. If they couldn’t naturally follow the same path as Awakeners, then Michael would simply help them grow through his talent.","Even now, if Michael truly wanted to, he could force Arianne’s strength to Rank Three right now. There was nothing inherently wrong with this path. But it carried a certain dependency on him.","Michael had also never minded that part. If anything, a selfish corner of his heart almost preferred it.","But when he saw the effect of his Awakening Temple, a conflict grew in him.","Arianne and Aunt Mia could also be Awakeners! This way, they’d grow their own Classes, gain the Skills they wanted, and develop their own foundations.","The two paths had their pros and cons. But even if Michael could artificially raise someone’s strength, becoming an Awakener meant becoming part of something much larger.","His logic had been telling him that ever since the Awakening Temple appeared. Awakening was better.","Yet his emotions had kept resisting that conclusion.","It was fine to be selfish, wasn’t it? Did these two really need to involve themselves in the world of the supernatural? Wouldn’t it just be better if they simply had strength for the sake of a longer lifespan?","*If he could personally guarantee their safety and future, why did it matter how they reached that point?*","But after listening to Arianne just now, Michael finally realized what was wrong with that reasoning.","Arianne wasn’t one of his undead. Aunt Mia wasn’t some creature waiting for him to decide the optimal evolutionary route.","They were people. Human beings with their own desires and their own choices. They weren’t his belongings.","If Michael genuinely saw them as family, as people he loved, then wanting the absolute best for them should matter more than his own selfish desires if they conflicted with it.","His gaze returned to Arianne.","Michael’s expression gradually relaxed.","\"Yes.\"","Arianne’s eyes widened dramatically in shock. Then her expression slowly became suspicious.","\"Wait. I know you’re impressive, but you’re not that impressive, right?\"","Michael’s mouth twitched.","Arianne raised a hand before he could respond.","\"I mean, there’s still a lot I don’t know about Awakeners, but even I understand awakening isn’t something people can just do whenever they want.\"","\"It happens naturally, doesn’t it? At a certain age, and even then only to some people.\"","Her eyes moved over Michael’s face.","\"So what are you saying? That you can just... go against nature?\"","Michael rubbed his forehead.","\"Of course I’m not that impressive. It’s complicated to explain. But yes. I really do have a way to make you awaken.\"","Arianne’s expression shifted again, but she said nothing, seemingly deep in thought.","Michael looked toward the distant Awakening Temple. All he had to do was simply take her there.","But if he was really going to let Arianne choose for herself, then he needed to tell her everything first.","Michael turned back toward her.","\"However, there’s something else you should know before deciding.\"","Arianne immediately became serious.","Michael pointed at her.","\"I can also make you much stronger without awakening at any time.\"","\"How much stronger?\"","Michael thought briefly.","\"Instantly around Princess Priscilla’s level.\"","Her eyes widened.","\"Right now?\"","\"Yes.\"","Arianne stared.","\"You mean eventually?\"","\"No. I mean I could start pushing you toward that level immediately.\"","Her expression became blank.","Michael continued before she could react too much.","\"But there’s a problem. If you take that path, you’d have to give up becoming an Awakener.\"","Arianne’s surprise slowly settled into confusion.","Michael understood this was a serious decision, so he didn’t attempt to rush her.","His expression softened.","\"I won’t choose for you, so decide. Both options are good, though if you become an Awakener, you’ll have to face some hardships I can’t help you with.\"","However, Michael’s words seemed to trigger something inside Arianne. The hesitation in her eyes disappeared. Her green eyes seemed to burn as she looked at him.","\"I want to become an Awakener!\"","Michael was startled by the sudden change in aura.","\"Arianne, you don’t have to decide that fast.\"","\"I’ve already decided. I think this is best for me.\"","\"You should at least consider the other option properly. Becoming that strong immediately isn’t something small.\"","\"I know.\"","\"As an Awakener, you’d have to start from the beginning and face unknown obstacles that you might not even know how to break through.\"","\"I know.\"","Michael frowned slightly.","Arianne turned toward him fully and took in a deep breath.","\"Michael.\"","Her expression softened, but the determination in her eyes didn’t weaken.","\"I appreciate everything you do for me. Really. I do.\"","Arianne looked down at her hands for a moment.","\"You gave me another life. You protect me. You keep giving me things I don’t even know how to repay.\"","Michael was about to speak, but she shook her head.","\"But this is also for me.\"","Arianne’s fingers slowly curled into a fist.","\"I want to feel like I did something.\"","She paused, as if trying to put the feeling into words.","\"Like I’m doing something.\"","A solemn expression appeared on her face as she continued.","\"Like whatever I become, at least part of it came from me.\""]},{"number":1246,"title":"Chapter 1246: Awakening [4]","paragraphs":["Arianne gave a small laugh.","\"Instant power sounds amazing. Seriously, it does. Becoming as strong as Princess Priscilla right now? That’s no small temptation.\"","For most of her life, Priscilla had represented a level of talent and power that seemed almost unreachable. To be told she could stand near that level almost immediately was something she didn’t even know was possible until she met Michael.","Yes, everything started changing after she met him.","Arianne’s expression became more determined.","\"I want something more, Michael. Something truly more solid and deserving.\"","\"I want to prove something.\"","\"To who?\" Michael interrupted.","Arianne smiled at him.","\"Me. I want to prove something to me.\" Then, after a short pause, she added, \"And you too.\"","Michael’s expression became strange.","\"Why me?\"","\"Because you’re ridiculous.\"","Arianne continued before he could interrupt.","\"Everything about you is ridiculous. Every time I think I understand how strong you are or what you’re capable of, you show me something else.\"","She gestured around them.","\"Like this.\"","Michael glanced at the territory.","Arianne’s smile became slightly embarrassed.","\"I know I’m probably never going to catch up to you.\"","\"You don’t know that.\"","\"I do.\"","\"You really don’t.\"","Arianne ignored him.","\"But I don’t want to just stand beside you because you made me strong enough to.\"","That made Michael quiet.","\"I want to know I can grow too.\"","Her hand moved to her chest.","\"I want something that’s mine.\"","\"Isn’t your awakening still going to come from me?\"","Arianne gave him an annoyed look.","\"You know what I mean.\"","Michael did. At least, somewhat. He still didn’t fully understand why the distinction mattered so much to her. From his perspective, power was power. If he could give someone a better body, evolve them, improve their race, or increase their strength, he didn’t see why accepting it made what they achieved afterward any less meaningful.","Or was it that he did understand, but because it was Arianne, his selfishness made him stubborn about accepting it?","In the end, Michael nodded helplessly, knowing he couldn’t change Arianne’s choice.","\"Alright.\"","Arianne’s eyes brightened.","\"Really?\"","\"As long as it’s what you want, I’ll respect it. Regardless, I’m always here.\"","Arianne smiled widely.","Michael sighed and shook his head.","\"But don’t complain to me later when you’re Level One and getting beaten up by things you could have crushed if you picked the other option.\"","Her smile immediately became smug.","\"Then I’ll just come to you for help, no? What? Why are you looking at me like that? I’m stubborn, not stupid.\"","After several seconds of speechlessness, Michael shook his head.","Michael reached out and pulled her against him, one arm settling firmly around her waist. Before Arianne could react, the world blurred, and a moment later they were standing before the temple’s entrance instead.","Arianne stumbled slightly against him, blinking up at the structure towering overhead. She had seen this place earlier but hadn’t had the opportunity to observe it fully.","The staircase alone stretched wide enough to fit a large group of people, each step carved from flawless white crystal. The massive crystal gates stood open at the top, runes shifting endlessly across their surface, and above the entrance hung a circular golden emblem the size of a small house, an eye ringed by countless concentric circles.","\"...What is this place?\"","\"The Awakening Temple.\" Michael guided her up the stairs without slowing. \"This is where it happens, if you’re serious.\"","The moment they crossed the threshold, Arianne froze entirely.","What had looked like a modest chapel from outside opened into something closer to a palace hall. No, it was even bigger. The space inside the temple looked nothing like what the outside would suggest at all!","\"Michael,\" Arianne whispered, \"this is...\"","\"Don’t pay too much attention to these things. They’re hard to explain.\" Michael kept walking.","At the far end of the hall stood two enormous statues, facing each other across the empty floor. On the left, a warrior wrapped in layered armor, weapons strapped across every inch of him: sword, spear, axe, daggers lining his belt, as if he’d been built to wield anything put in his hands. On the right, a mage draped in long robes, a wand resting in one palm, an ancient scroll held in the other.","Both faces remained blurred. Beneath each statue, a circular blue vortex turned in complete silence.","Michael stopped a short distance from both portals and finally released her.","\"These are the two paths,\" he said. \"The Physical Path, under the warrior. The Magical Path, under the mage.\"","Arianne studied them both, uncertain.","\"Whichever one you enter, you’ll go through a trial,\" Michael continued. \"If you succeed in the physical path, you will awaken a physical-type class. Knight, Warrior, Assassin, Guardian, Hunter, there’s no fixed outcome. It depends entirely on how well you perform during the trial itself.\"","He gestured toward the mage statue.","\"The Magical Path works the same way. Succeed, and you awaken a mage-type class.\"","\"Outstanding performance in either path can earn you something extra, on top of the class itself. So you need to do your best. But don’t worry. It’s totally safe.\"","At least for the first time, Michael thought.","Arianne’s gaze moved between the two portals, weighing them.","\"There’s no favoritism here,\" Michael added quietly. \"What you walk out with depends entirely on you.\"","He stepped back, giving her room.","\"So. Which one calls to you, Arianne?\"","\"What path do you think would give me something related to taming?\"","Michael thought for a moment and replied honestly.","\"I don’t know.\"","Arianne looked mildly disappointed.","Michael smiled and continued.","\"If I had to guess, Mage is probably your best chance. Taming isn’t limited to one type of Class.\"","There were Awakeners with physical Classes who could tame creatures too. There were even stranger physical Classes that mixed martial combat with animal bonds.","So taming itself clearly wasn’t something that belonged exclusively to magic, but if he had to choose one, if the trial allowed one to choose a class, a Beast Tamer was more of a magic-type class than physical."]},{"number":1247,"title":"Chapter 1247: Awakening [5]","paragraphs":["Arianne considered her choice for a moment, then nodded to herself, decision made.","\"Mage, then.\"","She stepped toward the vortex beneath the mage statue, but Michael’s hand caught her shoulder before she got too close.","Arianne glanced back at him.","\"You don’t need to be too worried about all this,\" Michael said. \"Just try your best. That’s all that actually matters here. A good performance shapes your class and whatever extra reward comes with it, but even a mediocre one still gets you a class.\"","\"And you’re safe,\" he added. \"Whatever the trial throws at you, it won’t actually be able to kill you. So you can go in with a little more confidence than you’re probably feeling right now.\"","Arianne managed a small, nervous smile.","\"That obvious?\"","\"A bit.\"","She exhaled, some of the tension easing out of her shoulders.","Michael continued, tone softening further. \"And if something does go wrong, if you go in and come out with a class you hate, or nothing usable at all, it’s not the end of it. If you still want to be an Awakener afterward, I have other ways to make that happen. This isn’t your only chance.\"","Arianne opened her mouth in surprise, clearly not having considered that possibility.","\"...Okay.\" The nervousness in her expression settled into something steadier. \"Okay. Good to know.\"","She turned back toward the swirling blue vortex, squared her shoulders, and took a slow breath.","\"Wish me luck.\"","\"You don’t need it,\" Michael said. \"But good luck anyway.\"","Arianne smiled at him, then stepped forward into the portal.","The vortex swallowed her whole without a sound, and a heartbeat later, she was gone.","* * *","Arianne found herself standing in an endless white space.","There was no ground beneath her feet that she could see, no walls, no ceiling, just an all-consuming white that stretched in every direction, swallowing any sense of scale or distance.","It was disorienting. Her heart began beating a little faster.","Arianne took a slow breath, forcing her shoulders to relax.","lMichael said it’s safe. It’s fine. Whatever this is, it’s fine.","She held onto that thought and let it settle, the initial nervousness gradually smoothing out into focus.","Just as she began studying the nothingness around her, searching for any detail at all to anchor herself to, a panel materialized in front of her.","[Awakening Trial Participant Discovered]","[Please state your desired Class direction.]","She wasn’t unfamiliar with panels, but this was the first time one had interacted with her instead of her interacting with it.","Arianne hesitated only a moment before answering aloud.","\"Beast Taming.\"","[Choice Considered.]","The panel shifted, and a new one unfolded beneath it.","[Please select your Trial Difficulty.]","[Normal] | [Hard] | [Extreme] | [Hell]","Beneath the four options, additional text scrolled into view, explaining what each level meant for her outcome.","[Normal]: Guarantees successful class awakening upon completion. No additional rewards beyond the base class.","[Hard]: Increased trial difficulty. Small chance of bonus Trait upon exceptional performance.","[Extreme]: Further increased difficulty. Strong chance of bonus Trait. Possibility of other rewards and advanced class variant based on performance.","[Hell]: Maximum difficulty. Possibility of advanced Class increases significantly. Participants who perform sufficiently well may be granted a choice in their final Class rather than having one assigned. Protection towards death removed.","[Trial Performance Rating]","[Average] | [Excellent] | [Exceptional] | [Perfect]","[Note: Trial Performance Rating affects the quality of your reward.]","Arianne read through it twice, her eyes lingering longest on the final line as her breath caught in shock.","Just as she was wondering what to choose, another panel appeared in front of her.","[Please make your selection.]","Arianne stared at the four difficulty options, running through them methodically.","Normal guaranteed her a class with no failure possible. If one had no ambition and just wanted a class to become an Awakener, this was the easiest method available to them.","Hard, on the other hand, offered a real shot at something called a Trait without much added danger. Safety still seemed to be guaranteed, but the class wasn’t a given.","Extreme pushed further still, but still within safety’s reach: a strong chance at something extra, maybe even an advanced variant of her choice, all at the cost of a much higher chance of failing.","Hell, on the other hand, removed the safety net entirely. On paper, it seemed like an unnecessary risk.","There was no logical reason to choose it. If something went wrong in there, actual death was on the table. Yet Arianne’s eyes kept drifting back to it anyway.","Michael.","Every time she thought of him she understood the size of the gap between them.","She wasn’t joking when she’d told him she knew she’d probably never catch up to him. She’d meant it, mostly.","Inside, though, some small, stubborn part of her had never quite let go of the idea that maybe, someday, if she pushed hard enough at the right moments, the distance between them might actually close. Even if only a little.","Choosing Hell wouldn’t close that gap today, and her life would even be at risk. She knew that too. But it was the only option in front of her that seemed to challenge whether she truly had the ambition to match Michael.","Arianne’s palms were sweating.","[Protection towards death removed.]","The words sat there, unmoving. Two minutes passed in silence while she wavered, caught directly between wanting to prove something to herself and the fear of regretting it later if she didn’t brave through this.","Amidst her internal struggle, a small timer flickered into existence at the corner of her vision.","[00:30]","[If no selection is made, a difficulty will be randomly assigned.]","Arianne’s breath caught.","The timer kept counting down, unbothered by her indecision.","[00:25]","[00:20]","Arianne’s eyes darted between Hell and Extreme, then back again, her heart hammering loud enough she was almost certain it echoed through the empty white space around her.","[00:15]","Just choose. Just pick one.","*","A/N: Please vote to support!!!!"]},{"number":1248,"title":"Chapter 1248: Spirit World [1]","paragraphs":["Arianne choice twitched toward Extreme, the safe answer, the sensible one, the one that let her walk out of here with something to be proud of even if she failed, but she could also die.","[00:10]","Arianne didn’t move.","[00:05]","Sweat rolled down the side of her face. Her fingers curled at her sides, frozen.","[00:03]","[00:02]","[00:01]","[Time Expired.]","[No selection detected. Difficulty randomly assigned.]","Arianne’s stomach dropped.","The panel flickered once, then settled.","[Selected Difficulty: Hell]","For a moment, she simply stared at the word. Then, slowly, something in her chest loosened.","A long breath escaped her, shoulders sagging as the tension she’d been holding for the last two minutes finally broke.","It wasn’t relief at the danger. The Protection towards death removed line was still sitting right there beneath it, still just as real. But somehow, not having to be the one who chose it made it easier to breathe.","She hadn’t backed down. She hadn’t picked the safe option either.","Arianne wiped her palm against her sleeve, steadying herself.","Well. Guess that settles that.","A new panel flickered into existence.","[Generating Trial...]","Arianne braced herself, though she wasn’t entirely sure what to expect. The white space around her stayed exactly as empty and formless as before, giving nothing away.","Seconds passed.","[Trial Generated.]","Her vision darkened all at once, swallowing the endless white without warning.","The next thing Arianne saw was a foot.","It filled her entire field of vision. She barely had time to register the shape. She tried to dodge, but her body didn’t respond as she would have liked.","The kick landed.","The first kick was followed almost immediately by a second, then a third, blows landing from different directions before Arianne could even orient herself.","Her body moved sluggishly, nowhere near the speed or strength she’d grown used to since her resurrection. Every attempt to raise an arm or twist away arrived a half-second too late, as though she were fighting through water.","Through the haze of pain, she made out shapes. Three of them.","Their clothes were fine, well-tailored and clean.","They were shouting at her. Cursing, from the tone of it, sharp and mocking.","The language wasn’t one she recognized. And yet, somehow, she understood every word anyway.","\"Filthy little rat, watch where you’re going...\"","\"Doesn’t even know how to bow properly...\"","\"Someone should really teach her some manners already...\"","Arianne gave up trying to block and curled in on herself instead, arms wrapping over her head, knees drawn toward her chest, making herself as small a target as she could manage. Every kick that landed against her back or ribs sent a fresh burst of pain through her, but curling up at least kept the worst of it away from anywhere that mattered.","It felt like it went on forever.","Eventually, though, the blows slowed. Then stopped altogether, the three of them apparently growing bored, or tired, or simply satisfied.","\"Tch. Waste of time,\" one of them muttered.","Another crouched slightly, voice dropping into something almost lazy with contempt. It was a female voice.","\"Next time, watch where you’re going. You don’t get to just bump into people you can’t afford to mess with.\"","A third laughed, short and cold.","\"She’s just some vagrant orphan after all, we can’t expect her to have common sense.\"","Soon their footsteps retreated, unhurried.","Arianne stayed curled where she was for a long moment after they’d gone, breath ragged, every part of her body throbbing in overlapping waves of pain.","Arianne pushed herself upright, wincing at the fresh protest from her bruised body, and forced her eyes open properly for the first time since the beating had started.","She was in an alley.","Narrow walls of dark stone rose on either side of her. Trash was piled in uneven heaps against one wall, and a thin trickle of water ran down a crack in the stone somewhere behind her, the only sound besides her own ragged breathing.","Above, a strip of grey sky was visible between the buildings, dim and overcast, giving no real sense of what time it was.","Arianne looked down at herself.","She was wearing a uniform.","The same style as the three who’d just left, but where theirs had been crisp and clean, hers was worn threadbare, the fabric faded and stained, one sleeve torn at the seam like it had been mended and re-torn more than once.","Her hands were trembling.","Where... where am I?","She tried to stand, using the wall for support, and her legs shook under even that small effort. She also realized her body simply didn’t have the strength it should have.","This isn’t me. This isn’t my body’s strength.","Arianne pressed a hand against the cold stone, steadying herself, mind racing.","Why am I so weak?","A panel finally flickered into view in front of her, hovering just above the cracked stone of the alley.","[Trial Generated.]","[World: Ashveil Continent]","[Description: A world of Spirit Tamers, where the strength of a nation is measured by the beasts its people can summon and bond with. For three hundred years, the continent has stood against the encroaching Demon Army, a force that grows more relentless with each passing decade. Spirit Tamers are the last true line of defense; without them, humanity’s cities would have fallen long ago.]","[Setting: Silverleaf Academy, a prestigious institution training the next generation of Spirit Tamers.]","Arianne read through it as memories that weren’t quite hers, and yet were, surfaced alongside the panel. A name. An age. A place in this world she apparently already occupied.","I’m sixteen. I’m a student at Silverleaf Academy. I’m a Spirit Tamer.","Or she was supposed to be, anyway.","The other students summoned Spirit Beasts: wolves wreathed in lightning, hawks made of living flame, serpents that moved like flowing water. Powerful things. Beautiful things.","Arianne’s spirit had come out humanoid.","The weakest tier of them all, according to everything her borrowed memories told her, barely above uselessness in the eyes of this world.","Others summon beasts, I summon humans?"]},{"number":1249,"title":"Chapter 1249: Spirit World [2]","paragraphs":["In this world, spirits were generally divided into several broad types.","Beast Spirits were the most common. Wolves, serpents, birds, and countless other creatures fell beneath this category.","There were also Plant Spirits, Elemental Spirits, Construct Spirits, Undead Spirits, and several rarer classifications that Arianne’s memories only contained limited information about.","Then there were Humanoid Spirits.","And among all the commonly recognized classifications, Humanoid Spirits had one of the worst reputations.","Most were weak. Painfully weak.","That didn’t mean every Humanoid Spirit was useless. There were powerful ones. Giants, elves, ancient blood races, strange humanoid demons, and countless other creatures that resembled humans while possessing bodies and abilities far beyond them.","Some were even considered extremely desirable summons.","The problem was humans themselves.","Ordinary humans were widely regarded as the weakest Humanoid Spirits a Spirit Tamer could summon.","And unfortunately, Arianne seemed to possess the rare talent of summoning only humans.","Her expression gradually stiffened as more memories surfaced.","She hadn’t merely summoned a human once and been unfortunate. This body had been enrolled at Silverleaf Academy for three years. Spirit Tamers here were allowed to perform a formal taming ritual once every year under the academy’s guidance.","She had attempted it three times.","All three had produced humans.","The first had been an ordinary middle-aged man. He wasn’t a warrior. He wasn’t a mage. He wasn’t even particularly strong. He had been a farmer.","Arianne’s lips parted slightly.","The second attempt had produced a young man who at least knew how to use a sword. Unfortunately, that description made him sound considerably more impressive than he actually was. He had been nothing more than an ordinary guard.","Her third and most recent attempt had been the reason her reputation at Silverleaf Academy had completely collapsed.","A set of twin children.","Three years. Three opportunities. All humans.","Arianne slowly leaned back against the alley wall.","\"Oh.\"","For several seconds, she said nothing else.","She finally understood what Hell meant.","This was the Hell difficulty. This was a terrible starting point.","She was an orphan with practically nothing to her name, studying at an academy filled with people who already considered her worthless. Her body was weak. Her resources were nearly nonexistent.","She had no powerful family supporting her. And in a world where someone’s future was determined almost entirely by the spirits they could summon and tame, she possessed an ability that had seemingly decided to give her the weakest possible result every single time.","Arianne closed her eyes.","She suddenly remembered Michael’s words before she entered.","The better your performance, the more influence it’ll have on the Class you awaken and whatever additional rewards you receive.","Her eyelids opened again.","\"This is a joke.\"","Arianne looked toward the mouth of the alley.","For the first time, the true weight of the difficulty she had randomly received settled over her.","Arianne pushed herself away from the wall.","Pain immediately spread through her ribs.","She grimaced but remained standing.","Fine.","She had already chosen this path because she wanted something she could call her own. It would be rather embarrassing if the first thing she did after entering was complain because the starting point was terrible.","Just as Arianne took another step, a familiar blue light flickered before her.","She stopped immediately.","[Trial Tasks Generated.]","[Completing any one Trial Task will grant you the freedom to leave the trial at any time.]","[Death will also terminate the trial.]","[The greater the number of Trial Tasks completed before departure, the greater your final evaluation and rewards.]","[Trial Task 1: First of Silverleaf]","[Graduate from Silverleaf Academy as the highest-ranked student one year from now.]","Arianne’s expression stiffened.","\"...What?\"","Highest-ranked? Her? The girl who had spent three years summoning humans?","Before she could properly process it, the second task appeared.","[Trial Task 2: Break the Verdict]","[Defeat three students whose Spirit Tamer ranking currently exceeds yours by at least two major tiers in officially recognized combat.]","Her lips twitched.","Then came the final task.","[Trial Task 3: Humanity’s Answer]","[Using Human Spirits as the core of your force, make a contribution significant enough to alter the outcome of a battle against the Demon Army.]","The alley became very quiet.","Arianne read all three again.","Her gaze eventually returned to the first.","\"Graduate first in the academy.\"","She slowly looked down at her bruised body as she recalled every spirit she had summoned until now.","\"...Hell.\"","This time, she said it with considerably more understanding.","The first task alone was ridiculous. The second task wasn’t much kinder.","Arianne pressed two fingers against her forehead as she thought of the third task.","The Demon Army.","That was no school competition. The memories this body possessed about them were fragmented, mostly lessons and news brought into the academy, but even that was enough.","Cities had disappeared beneath Demon invasions. Veteran Spirit Tamers died every year holding defensive lines.","And the task wasn’t merely asking her to participate. She had to change the outcome of a battle. With Human Spirits forming the core of whatever force she used.","Arianne stared blankly at the panel.","\"So the first one is somehow the easiest.\"","That realization wasn’t particularly comforting.","All three tasks revolved around the same thing.","Her humans.","Arianne stared at the three tasks for another long moment before finally sighing.","She looked down at herself again. Her uniform was dirty, one sleeve torn, and she could still feel dried blood at the corner of her mouth.","\"...I should probably take a bath first.\"","There was no point trying to overturn her fate while looking like she’d been dragged through a ditch.","With that thought, Arianne began making her way toward the dormitory room belonging to this body, still sorting through the unfamiliar memories as she walked.","Meanwhile, outside the trial...","Michael had barely finished watching Arianne disappear into the blue vortex when several panels appeared in front of him.","His expression immediately became serious.","[Awakening Temple]","[Participant Registered.]","[Participant: Arianne Evermoon]"]},{"number":1250,"title":"Chapter 1250: GateKeeper [1]","paragraphs":["[Awakening Temple]","[Participant Registered.]","[Participant: Arianne Evermoon]","[Trial Path: Magical]","[Selected Difficulty: Hell]","Michael froze.","\"...Hell? What’s that?\"","All he knew was it probably wasn’t a good thing.","Michael’s expression darkened almost immediately.","The next lines appeared before he could react further.","[Hell Difficulty]","[The highest standard trial available to an Awakening Candidate.]","[Hell Difficulty grants the greatest potential evaluation and rewards, but provides no protection from death once the trial begins.]","[Trial conditions, identity, environment, and objectives are generated according to the participant.]","[External interference is prohibited.]","Michael’s face became increasingly ugly as he read.","She picked Hell?","He knew Arianne was ambitious and stubborn. But Michael didn’t believe she’d casually gamble her life after he’d explicitly told her the first trial was safe.","Alongside worry, immense anger surged through him.","\"I should have just sold a few things and gotten her an awakening scroll instead!\"","Michael couldn’t even imagine how he’d feel if she died. All he knew was that it would be his fault. He should have tested it on someone else first!","However, if there was a possibility of death, why had the temple description told him the first trial was safe?!","Unfortunately, the panel offered no explanation for how Hell had been selected.","It simply continued.","[Participant Status: Trial In Progress.]","[Trial information is inaccessible. Please raise the level of the temple for more functions.]","Michael frowned.","So he couldn’t see what she was doing.","The whole situation irritated him.","However, the temple didn’t care for his feelings and sent out more information.","[Trial Time Dilation Active.]","[Time Ratio: 365 Trial Days : 1 External Hour.]","Michael’s expression changed.","\"Three hundred and sixty-five days?\"","One year inside the trial was only one hour outside. That was far more extreme than he’d expected.","Michael’s gaze returned to the blue vortex.","To him, Arianne had entered only moments ago. But depending on the exact speed of the dilation, days could already have passed for her.","Weeks, even.","Michael folded his arms.","\"Wonderful.\"","He had told her she was safe. Then she somehow ended up in the one difficulty that explicitly removed protection from death.","His fingers tapped slowly against his arm.","Still, there was nothing he could do now. External interference was prohibited. Forcing his way into the trial would probably be either impossible or dangerously stupid. No, given the description he saw in the temple, it would just be plain stupid.","Michael looked at the portal in silence.","Then sighed.","\"Arianne...\"","His expression softened slightly.","\"Please don’t do anything too ridiculous.\"","It wasn’t only this Michael who was in a bad mood.","Far away, within the Origin Battlefield, the other Michael was equally displeased.","Although the two bodies shared the same mind and soul, things weren’t quite as simple as saying they were one person moving two bodies at the same time. There were subtle differences.","Through the strange and wonderful means of the Origin Will, both bodies possessed a certain degree of individuality. Their memories were shared. Their thoughts could overlap. Their intentions were ultimately the same. But their immediate emotions didn’t necessarily mirror one another perfectly.","One Michael could be irritated while the other remained calm. One could be amused by something while the other barely cared.","So when both bodies were affected by the same emotion at nearly the same time, it usually meant the matter had cut deep enough. And right now, both Michaels were in a terrible mood.","The Michael within the Origin Battlefield stood silently in the middle of a ruined landscape.","The battlefield around him had clearly been devastated. The earth was split apart in multiple directions, huge cracks running through the ground like scars.","Entire sections had been blown into craters, while chunks of stone and broken terrain were scattered across the surroundings.","Yet the arena was already beginning to repair itself. Cracks slowly closed. Broken ground shifted. Loose stone dissolved into particles before reforming where it belonged.","The Origin Battlefield was restoring the environment piece by piece.","Michael barely paid attention to it. His gaze remained fixed thousands of meters ahead.","There, inside an enormous pit, lay a ten-meter-tall white humanoid figure.","Its body looked almost sculpted rather than living, pale and smooth with barely any recognizable features left after the battle. Large portions of its torso had already collapsed. One arm was missing entirely. Its lower body had been crushed into the earth.","And now the rest of it was slowly fading. White particles peeled away from its body one after another, drifting upward before disappearing.","Michael watched without much emotion.","This was the gatekeeper of the Top 100.","After winning his previous battle and reaching Rank 108, Michael had immediately used his final challenge for the month on the person occupying Rank 98.","He had expected the familiar challenge notification. Instead, something different appeared.","[You are attempting to enter the Top 100 of the Fourth Layer Battlefield Ranking.]","[Special Ranking Mechanism Available.]","[Choose your advancement method.]","[Option 1: Top 100 Gatekeeper Trial]","[Challenge a combat construct generated according to the average combat standards of ranks 51-100.]","[Your final performance will be evaluated.]","[Upon completion, you may be assigned an appropriate ranking between Rank 51 and Rank 100.]","[Failure or voluntary withdrawal will not reduce your current ranking.]","[Option 2: Direct Ranking Challenge]","[Continue with your challenge against Rank 98.]","[Standard Battlefield Ranking rules will apply.]","At the time, Michael’s first instinct had been to choose the second.","The first sounded suspiciously convenient. Instead of defeating one person and taking Rank 98, the Origin Battlefield was offering to judge his strength directly and potentially place him considerably higher.","Anything that convenient naturally made Michael wonder what the catch was.","He almost selected the direct challenge. But after thinking about it properly, he changed his mind.","The current Battlefield Ranking wasn’t perfectly accurate. Far from it.","When the Origin Battlefield had opened previously, its initial ranking evaluation had been based largely on the strength participants displayed during their activities within the Fourth Layer, combined with the amount of time and accomplishments they accumulated there.","That system worked well enough to create an initial ranking. But it naturally produced problems."]},{"number":1251,"title":"Chapter 1251: GateKeeper [2]","paragraphs":["Someone could have hidden most of their strength. Someone else might have displayed an unusually powerful trump card during the evaluation period and received a ranking above what they could normally maintain.","Others might have improved tremendously since then. Some could have stagnated.","The result was that even among the Top 1000, there were plenty of people occupying what Michael considered false rankings.","A person ranked 300 could potentially possess enough strength to defeat someone ranked 180. Likewise, someone ranked 90 might not actually deserve to remain anywhere near that position.","That uncertainty became considerably more dangerous the closer one moved toward the Top 100.","Michael had already suspected that the monsters there were on an entirely different level. The Fourth Layer gathered countless extraordinary Rank Four existences from different civilizations, realms, races.","Among that many geniuses, it would be stupid to assume nobody had crossed the normal boundary of Rank Four combat power.","Some of them almost certainly possessed Demigod-level strength.","Michael himself already had Demigods.","Lunara. Valeria.","But owning Demigod-level subordinates and personally possessing Demigod-level combat ability inside the Fourth Layer were two very different things.","Michael couldn’t simply bring Lunara or Valeria into the Fourth Layer unrestricted. The Origin Battlefield had already made that painfully clear. A true Rank Five existence had to be suppressed before entering.","Even worse, not only was the cost expensive, Michael wasn’t convinced a suppressed Rank Five would necessarily be superior to an exceptional Peak Rank Four Awakener.","Suppression didn’t merely hide someone’s rank. It restricted the power they were allowed to express.","A Rank Four genius who naturally possessed Demigod-level combat prowess wouldn’t have that problem.","Michael had no idea what Rank 98 actually was. Perhaps they were simply just another powerful Peak Rank Four.","Or perhaps they were one of those ridiculous existences who had already reached the combat threshold of a Demigod while technically remaining Rank Four. After all, except for him, everyone in the Top 200 was at Level 100.","Choosing Option Two meant gambling his final challenge on an opponent whose true strength he knew almost nothing about for this month.","Option One was different.","The Gatekeeper was generated from the average combat standard of people ranked between 51 and 100. That gave Michael a much clearer benchmark.","Even better, failure carried almost no meaningful punishment. If the trial became too dangerous, he could simply withdraw and remain Rank 108. And if he performed reasonably well without completely defeating it, there was still a chance his evaluation would place him somewhere inside the Top 100.","Though this looked like it was more dangerous, Michael, who believed his Law meant he shouldn’t be that pathetic even in the Top 100, felt it was a good deal.","The only difference between choosing Option One and Option Two, at the end of the day, was that Option Two gave less reward.","So he had picked the first.","Michael stared at the fading white humanoid.","The fight hadn’t been easy. That alone told him quite a lot. This thing represented an average drawn from Rank 51 through Rank 100.","In the fight, it had also been growing stronger as they fought. It was only now, after so many deaths, that it was finally destroyed and didn’t revive.","\"So this is the gatekeeper of the Top 100...\"","Michael exhaled slowly as he watched the last pieces of the white humanoid dissolve into light.","Now there was only one question left.","How had the Origin Battlefield judged his performance?","As if responding to the thought, a blue panel appeared before him.","[Top 100 Gatekeeper Trial Completed.]","Michael’s attention immediately shifted toward it.","[Evaluation Complete.]","[Your demonstrated combat strength has exceeded the theoretical upper peak calculated for Awakeners ranked between 51 and 100.]","[Your performance cannot be accurately represented by the average combat standards of this ranking interval.]","[Final Placement Assigned.]","[Fourth Layer Battlefield Ranking: 51]","Michael stared at the number for several seconds.","\"Fifty-one?\"","He had expected to enter the Top 100. He had even considered the possibility of being placed somewhere around Rank 70 or 60 if the Origin Battlefield judged his performance highly enough.","But Rank 51 was literally the highest position the Gatekeeper Trial was capable of assigning. Though it was true he had ganged up on the Gatekeeper, this was still a very high placement.","The panel continued before he could think too deeply about it.","[Excellent Performance Detected.]","[Your combat performance substantially exceeded the qualification requirements of the Top 100 Gatekeeper Trial.]","[Special Reward Granted.]","[Ranking Challenge Quota Refunded: +1]","Michael’s expression brightened slightly.","His final challenge for the month had been returned. He had originally entered this trial believing he was spending his last opportunity to climb until the following month. Instead, he had jumped directly from Rank 108 to Rank 51 and still retained one challenge.","Michael looked at the recovering battlefield around him. The enormous crater where the Gatekeeper had fallen was already shrinking as shattered earth pulled itself back together.","\"Not bad.\"","That was putting it mildly.","Rank 51. He had crossed fifty-seven positions in a single challenge.","More importantly, the evaluation itself confirmed something Michael had been wondering about. His current combat strength wasn’t merely somewhere within the standards of the lower Top 100. According to the Origin Battlefield, he had actually broken the theoretical upper peak calculated for ranks 51 through 100.","Of course, Michael didn’t misunderstand what that meant. It didn’t mean he was stronger than every person between Rank 51 and Rank 100.","The current rankings were still imperfect, and the Gatekeeper itself had been formed using accumulated combat data and theoretical standards. There could absolutely be monsters hidden among those ranks who exceeded the model.","Michael himself was living proof that such people existed.","Still, the result was valuable. At the very least, he now had a proper estimate of where his current strength stood.","Michael opened the ranking list.","His name had moved dramatically upward.","[51. Michael Norman]","He stared at it for a moment. Then his gaze naturally moved higher.","Rank 50. Rank 40. Rank 30.","Eventually, the Top 10.","Michael’s eyes lingered there.","The lower half of the Top 100 was already this strong.","Then what exactly were the people above Rank 50 like? And more importantly... what kind of monsters were occupying the first ten positions?","Michael’s bad mood finally improved slightly.","The worry over Arianne was still there, buried beneath everything else, but a faint battle intent began rising in its place.","He still had one challenge.","*","A/N: Please vote to support! More Chapters coming!"]},{"number":1252,"title":"Chapter 1252: Real Vs Copy [1]","paragraphs":["Since he had already decided to use every challenge available to him this month, there was no reason to stop simply because the Origin Battlefield had unexpectedly returned one.","Michael’s gaze moved away from the Top 10 and settled much closer.","[41. Kaelith Vorn]","Ten ranks above his. The maximum jump he could make through an ordinary ranking challenge.","Michael selected the name.","[Ranking Challenge Issued.]","[You have entered a new ranking threshold.]","[Special Ranking Mechanism Available.]","\"Again?\" Michael’s eyes narrowed.","The panel expanded.","[You are attempting to advance within the upper rankings of the Fourth Layer Battlefield Ranking.]","[Choose your advancement method.]","[Option 1: Top 50 Gatekeeper Trial]","[Challenge a combat construct generated according to the average combat standards of Awakeners ranked between 11 and 50.]","[Your final performance will be evaluated.]","[Upon completion, you may be assigned an appropriate ranking between Rank 11 and Rank 50.]","[Failure or voluntary withdrawal will not reduce your current ranking.]","[Option 2: Direct Ranking Challenge]","[Continue through the standard Battlefield Ranking challenge system.]","[Standard Battlefield Ranking rules will apply.]","Michael stared at the panel.","It seemed the Origin Battlefield had divided the upper rankings into another bracket. Ranks 51 through 100 had one Gatekeeper. Ranks 11 through 50 had another.","Which naturally meant...","Michael’s gaze shifted toward the first ten names on the ranking list.","There was probably another threshold waiting there. Perhaps a Gatekeeper specifically for entering the Top 10.","Michael’s attention returned to Option One.","This time, there was no hesitation caused by suspicion. He already understood what the system was doing. The Gatekeeper wasn’t merely an obstacle. It was a way for the Origin Battlefield to correct the inaccuracies in its ranking without forcing an obviously misplaced Awakener to spend several months challenging upward ten positions at a time.","If his strength belonged somewhere higher, it would put him there. If it didn’t, he would remain Rank 51.","What Michael was unsure of was whether this special mechanism only applied to the Top 100 and Top 50, or if there was now one for the Top 200, 300, 500, or even Top 1000.","[Top 50 Gatekeeper Trial Selected.]","[Generating Gatekeeper.]","[Since you’re challenging a high rank, the difficulty of this match is at its highest difficulty.]","[Death and damages done in this match will be void after it ends. Please battle to your heart’s content, dear Awakener.]","\"Hmmm? Why does it sound more \"real\"?\"","Reading the last message on the panel again Michael’s eyes slowly brightened.","\"So I really can go all out?!\"","This was much more interesting than all his other matches.","For once, he could actually test everything without calculating the cost of failure afterward.","The scenery around him changed.","Michael immediately an enormous pressure gathering around him. Far heavier than the presence of the previous Gatekeeper.","Michael’s casual expression disappeared.","\"Yeah...\"","Darkness rolled from his body as one undead presence after another began appearing around him.","Beginning.","The High Drake.","Then hundreds more. Thousands.","Michael stared ahead as the pressure continued rising.","\"This one definitely isn’t going to be easy.\"","The world around Michael finally settled.","The first thing he noticed was the body of water surrounding him.","An endless expanse of black, perfectly still water stretched in every direction, reflecting almost nothing from the equally dark sky above. There was no horizon to speak of, water and darkness simply bled into each other, and the silence felt just as absolute above as below.","Michael stood on the surface as though it were solid ground, his undead spread behind him in a vast formation.","Michael looked ahead.","Several hundred meters away, the black water moved.","Something began rising from beneath the surface.","A head appeared.","Michael’s eyes narrowed.","The figure continued emerging until it stood completely above the water.","\"W-what is this?!\" Michael was shocked by the sight ahead of him, because the person standing across from him was... him.","Long black hair. Green eyes.","Same face. Same height. Same body.","Even the expression was disturbingly familiar.","The figure across from him stared back with the exact same cold focus.","Michael’s gaze moved over it more carefully.","The resemblance wasn’t merely superficial. Even the pressure it gave off.","It was all his.","Just as he got ready to act, the water around the replica moved again.","Hundreds of disturbances appeared across the black surface as bodies began rising from the water one after another.","A massive figure emerged behind the false Michael.","It was Beginning in its human form.","Another shape followed.","The High Drake in its human form as well, just like it was beside him.","Undead after undead rose from beneath the black water, each one taking the exact shape of something standing behind Michael.","The same bodies. The same sizes. The same appearances. The same formations.","Within moments, an entire army stood opposite him.","Michael looked behind himself. Then back ahead.","The two forces mirrored one another across the endless black ocean. Even the smallest details were there. The undead he had summoned only moments earlier were now reproduced across from him.","Michael’s eyes narrowed.","\"So that’s what highest difficulty means?\"","A panel appeared.","[Top 50 Gatekeeper Trial]","[Highest Difficulty Active.]","[Gatekeeper Form Generated.]","[Combat Model: Challenger Reflection.]","Michael stared at the last line for a few seconds longer as more information appeared.","[The Gatekeeper will reproduce the combat force, abilities, combat habits, and demonstrated capabilities of the challenger.]","[The reflected force will scale according to the combat standards required for ranks 11-50.]","Michael’s expression became strange, and he looked toward the false version of himself.","Though the current situation was very eerie, he felt a faint chill of excitement run through him. This was different from fighting some strange race with abilities he had never encountered.","Michael slowly smiled.","\"Interesting.\"","The copied Michael smiled too. Exactly the same way.","For a brief moment, neither side moved as battle intent continued to rise on both sides, thickening the still air over the black water until it felt almost solid enough to cut."]},{"number":1253,"title":"Chapter 1253: Real Vs Copy [2]","paragraphs":["Michael turned his head slightly.","Of all the undead standing beside him, Beginning was the one whose battle intent was the most obvious. The giant was still in his human form for now, looking almost calm on the surface, but Michael could feel the violent \"excitement\" rolling beneath it.","Beginning had always been like this. The stronger the opponent, the \"happier\" he became.","Michael’s lips curled upward.","\"Go at it, boy.\"","Beginning looked toward him.","\"Let’s try that method.\"","Beginning nodded, then moved.","The first step sent ripples racing across the black water. The second shattered the stillness entirely.","Beginning accelerated straight toward the mirrored army. For the first few hundred meters, he remained in his smaller form.","Then his body burst apart.","His flesh and bones exploded outward in a violent spray, as though some invisible force had torn him apart from the inside.","And almost immediately, everything returned.","His bones reformed along with his flesh. But Beginning didn’t return at the same size. His body expanded rapidly. By the time the regeneration finished, Beginning had become a fifty-meter giant. His aura rose with him.","The pressure around Beginning had become much heavier. But he didn’t stop running.","Another stretch of distance disappeared beneath his feet.","Then his body burst apart again.","Boom!","This time, the explosion was even more violent. Chunks of flesh and bone scattered across the black water before being dragged back together almost instantly.","Beginning regenerated again, becoming larger and stronger. His body climbed to a hundred meters.","The pressure rolling from him became oppressive enough that several weaker undead behind Michael instinctively shifted.","At this stage, Beginning’s aura had already reached a ridiculous level. It reminded Michael of Lucky when he had evolved to Epic ★★★. One had to know that Beginning was still only Extraordinary ★★★. A complete major grade below Epic.","Yet through his Law and this method of self-destruction, repeatedly destroying and rebuilding himself instead of accumulating injuries, his aura had climbed, at the cost of a ridiculous amount of energy, until it could already rival Michael’s strongest Epic undead.","Beginning continued running. The distance between both armies had already been cut in half.","When he reached the midpoint, his body exploded for the third time.","The black ocean beneath him collapsed downward from the force. For hundreds of meters around, water was blasted away, exposing a hollow abyss before the surrounding ocean rushed back inward.","Beginning’s enormous form vanished completely inside the explosion. When he appeared again, Beginning rose above the black ocean like a moving mountain, his current height at two hundred meters.","His aura erupted alongside a roar.","Michael’s expression changed as a chill ran through his body.","\"This pressure...\"","It couldn’t compare to the female Demigod before her death. But the current Beginning had gone far beyond normal Rank Four.","\"Demigod...\"","At this moment, Beginning possessed Demigod-level battle prowess.","However, there was no joy on Michael’s face.","Across the battlefield...","The other Beginning had done the exact same thing.","First destruction. Fifty meters.","Second destruction. A hundred.","Third destruction. Two hundred.","Every stage. Every burst of regeneration. Every increase in aura.","Perfectly mirrored.","The reflected Beginning now stood opposite the real one at the exact same height.","Two hundred meters.","Its aura was equally terrifying. Equally violent. Equally far beyond Rank Four.","The two giants reached each other. Neither slowed or dodged. Both drew back one arm at exactly the same moment.","Michael felt the pressure from their fists before they even collided.","BOOOOOOM!","The black ocean detonated.","For several kilometers around the point of impact, the water was blown away completely. A massive wall of black liquid rose toward the dark sky. The shockwave tore across the battlefield. Undead on both sides were thrown backward. The air itself seemed to compress and burst.","Michael raised one arm instinctively as the force reached him. Even from hundreds of meters away, his clothes snapped violently against his body. His hair whipped backward.","And in the center of it all, the two Beginnings remained locked fist against fist, both refusing to move back.","Michael stared at them. Then at the mirrored version of himself standing far beyond them.","The fake Michael stared back.","Michael’s battle intent surged. The sight of Beginning matching his reflection head-on, both sides already displaying power beyond normal Rank Four, only made the excitement inside him burn hotter.","His eyes sharpened.","\"Go!\"","The order rang across the black ocean.","The undead army behind him moved instantly. Thousands charged forward at once. The still water beneath them erupted into countless waves as heavy footsteps, claws, wings, and bursts of mana shattered the silence.","At the front of the aerial forces, the Undead High Drake’s human form shot into the sky like an arrow. Halfway upward, its body began transforming. Within moments, the humanoid silhouette was gone, replaced by an enormous crimson draconic body. Two massive wings snapped open. The force sent a storm sweeping across the battlefield.","The reflected High Drake did the same.","Two gigantic crimson figures climbed into the dark sky from opposite sides, then collided.","BOOM!","Their claws slammed together. The shockwave rippled through the sky.","Neither stopped. Their jaws opened almost simultaneously. Two torrents of destructive fire energy met at point-blank range. The explosion lit the black sky red.","Behind them, the Undead Bone Dragon and Bone Wyvern had joined the battlefield to fight their reflections. They all crashed into one another. Claws scraped against reinforced bone. Tails whipped through the air. Their collision produced a sound like mountains grinding together.","Within seconds, the sky had become another battlefield entirely.","Dragon against dragon. Wyvern against wyvern. Undead against undead.","And below...","The rest of the army collided. The black ocean disappeared beneath them. Thousands of bodies slammed into their reflections. Magic erupted in every direction.","The battlefield became chaos almost instantly.","Michael watched from behind as he retreated. The energy surrounding him was becoming increasingly violent. Mana gathered around his body in thick waves. The black water beneath his feet began trembling before he even moved.","Michael took several steps backward, increasing the distance between himself and the main clash.","His gaze remained fixed on the reflected Michael.","The other Michael was doing the same retreating as they both gathered energy.","Michael’s smile widened.","\"Of course you are.\"","The mana around him surged harder."]},{"number":1254,"title":"Chapter 1254: Real Vs Copy [3]","paragraphs":["At almost the exact same moment, both Michaels stopped retreating.","Their hands lowered and struck the surface of the black water.","\"Death Ground.\"","Both voices seemed to overlap across the battlefield as dark mist exploded outward from their bodies and poured across the battlefield like a flood.","Within seconds, the black water around Michael had disappeared beneath rolling layers of dark energy. It swallowed the battlefield beneath a dark haze, winding around the bodies of the undead.","The moment Michael’s undead came under its influence, their auras changed.","Unfortunately, just as Michael’s undead were benefiting from his Death Ground, across the battlefield the same thing was happening.","Just like that, the advantage Michael had hoped to create vanished before it could even exist.","Instead, the battlefield simply became more violent.","BOOM!","Beginning and his reflection collided again. This time, the impact was even worse. A circular depression hundreds of meters wide appeared beneath them as the water was blasted away.","One Beginning grabbed the other’s shoulder. The other caught his arm. Then both drove their knees forward at once.","The collision produced another deafening explosion.","Above them, the two High Drakes tore into one another with renewed ferocity. One ripped several crimson scales from the other’s neck. The wound began closing swiftly under the influence of Death Ground. The injured Drake responded by biting into its counterpart’s wing.","Michael watched the battlefield become steadily more ridiculous.","Every enhancement he applied was copied. Every increase in recovery only prolonged the battles. Every boost in power increased the destruction on both sides without breaking the balance.","The black ocean could barely remain still for even a fraction of a second anymore. Waves several hundred meters high rose and collapsed. Columns of water were blasted into the sky.","The entire battlefield looked less like an arena now and more like a small apocalypse.","Michael’s eyes narrowed.","\"This is troublesome.\"","Michael’s gaze shifted toward the fake Michael in the distance and sent a command to all his undead.","\"Slow Curse.\"","It had been many months since Michael had gotten the skill [Memory Infusion]. Aside from using it to boost his knowledge by leaps and bounds, having his undead work as knowledge banks to feed information back to him, he had also fed back skills that many of them could use. Examples included, but were not limited to, Fireball, Mana Ball, Mana Arrow, and so on.","The undead legion responded at once. A wave of murky energy spread from several sections of his army. Dark curse marks appeared on the reflected undead, causing their movements to slow.","It might have only been a fraction of a second, a small delay in reaction. But in a battle where both sides were almost perfectly equal, even a tiny difference should have mattered.","However, just as Michael’s side was about to make a big move, the reflected Michael bit back.","Several reflected undead suddenly stopped moving, their bodies swelling into a disgusting form.","Michael’s pupils contracted.","\"Corpse Explosion?\"","BOOOOOOM!","The first undead detonated. It was a Rank Three.","The explosion was nothing like the Corpse Explosion Michael had been accustomed to using in his earlier days. The difference was absurd. The Rank Three undead’s entire existence seemed to collapse inward for a split second before releasing everything at once.","Several of Michael’s undead caught within the blast were torn apart in a single instant.","Before the first explosion had even finished expanding, another reflected undead swelled. Then another. And another.","BOOM!","BOOOOOOM!","The battlefield lit up with consecutive explosions.","Michael’s expression stiffened.","Several of them were also Rank Four.","An Awakener’s skill set differed from other supernaturals, who needed to upgrade their abilities to match their rank for any major promotion in power. Aside from gaining new skills as they advanced in rank, or after every twenty points in their main stat, and occasionally in other stats if lucky, old skills, even without modification, could still remain strong, since they too scaled with rank and stats.","A skill that had a range limit of ten metres while the Awakener was unranked could increase to twenty-five metres at Rank One, and seventy at Rank Two. As for getting a skill every twenty points of increase in a stat, this chance got increasingly rarer as the stat rose, but the trade-off was that if one did get it, the skill would automatically match their current rank.","It was only now that Michael truly understood how ridiculous Corpse Explosion had become at his current stage.","The destructive power was horrifying. One Rank Four undead detonated near the center of the clash. The blast swallowed dozens of figures from both sides. Even Beginning and his reflection were forced apart by the shockwave, though they closed the distance again a moment later, never truly breaking from their clash.","Michael’s eyes widened.","The copied Michael had sacrificed some of its own army, and the exchange wasn’t bad, as every detonation took out enemies standing nearby.","And while the reflected side lost the undead used as explosives, Michael’s side suffered enormous casualties from the blast itself.","Within moments, a noticeable section of his army disappeared. Some were killed outright. Others survived with missing limbs, shattered torsos, broken wings, or heavily damaged shells.","Michael stared at the destruction.","\"...That’s nasty.\"","He couldn’t even complain. It was his own skill.","Michael’s expression hardened.","If the other side was willing to sacrifice its forces...","Why wouldn’t he?","Michael’s gaze swept across the battlefield. He quickly identified the undead already too badly damaged to contribute properly.","Michael hesitated for a moment.","Normally, he would never casually sacrifice his undead like this. Especially Rank Four undead, as every one of them represented enormous resources. And more importantly, they belonged to him.","Even if many weren’t individually important to him, simply destroying them unnecessarily had never been his preferred style.","But his current situation was also a bit special.","Michael had noticed something strange from the moment he entered this arena.","*","A/N: Please vote to support!"]},{"number":1255,"title":"Chapter 1255: Real VS Copy [4]","paragraphs":["His soul felt covered. Protected, like there was an additional layer surrounding the connections between himself and his undead.","Michael couldn’t properly identify what it was, but it was probably the special protection of this trial.","After all, when the explosions killed his undead, he didn’t receive a soul backlash.","Normally, the sudden destruction of multiple powerful undead should have produced at least some disturbance through their connection. Here, there was none.","Combined with the Origin Battlefield’s earlier message...","[Death and damages done in this match will be void after it ends.]","Michael understood. His undead weren’t truly being permanently destroyed. At least, their loss here wouldn’t follow him outside.","Michael’s eyes became cold.","\"Fine.\"","His hesitation disappeared.","He pointed toward the center of the battlefield. The wounded undead reacted at once.","Michael’s voice dropped.","\"Explode.\"","Across the battlefield, the reflected Michael’s expression changed for the first time.","Michael saw it and smiled.","\"Your turn.\"","BOOOOOOOOOOM!","The first wave detonated. Several Rank Three undead exploded simultaneously. The combined blast tore open the battlefield.","Then a wounded Rank Four joined them. The resulting explosion was so violent that the black mist of Death Ground was temporarily blown apart over an enormous area. Water rose into the sky like an inverted ocean. Several reflected undead vanished inside the destruction.","Michael felt no backlash, and his smile widened even more.","\"So I was right.\"","Another group detonated.","BOOM!","BOOOOOOM!","The nature of the battle changed.","It was no longer simply undead trading blows against identical opponents. Now both sides were turning their own losses into weapons. An undead that lost an arm wasn’t merely weakened. It had become potential ammunition.","Michael watched several of his injured undead rush toward their reflections. One grabbed its counterpart around the waist. The reflected undead tried to pull away, but it was too late.","The real undead’s body expanded.","BOOOOOOM!","Michael’s eyes flickered.","\"This skill...\"","Though he admitted he had underestimated it, he felt it was a pity this skill couldn’t be used in real life, since sacrificing his own undead like this would cost him far more than it could ever be worth here.","\"Wait! Why do I need to use my own undead? Didn’t I just transport a whole group of undead from the Netherworld?\"","An idea sprouted in Michael’s mind. Though those creatures were currently weak, their existence gave him an idea for the future.","At this point, even after all the destruction both sides had caused, neither Michael held any meaningful advantage. The battlefield had only become even more devastated. Several powerful undead on both sides had been completely destroyed, while many others were injured to varying degrees.","But the balance remained. If Michael destroyed ten undead, his reflection usually destroyed around the same number. If one of his stronger undead managed to push ahead, the copied version would eventually answer with something equally troublesome. In terms of raw force, they were still nearly identical.","However, Michael had noticed one difference.","When it came to command, the reflected side was good. Its coordination was frighteningly accurate, making Michael picture an image of his future self, given enough time to learn.","The other side’s command wasn’t enough to create a decisive advantage. But it existed.","At this point, Michael knew he had to bring out the big guns.","The dark mist spreading from Death Ground began retreating rapidly. Within seconds, the entire field of death energy collapsed back toward Michael before disappearing completely.","The reflected Michael did the same.","Michael wasn’t surprised, as he had already expected that. Based on his experience with this copy, it wasn’t like it was reading his mind. It was more like it responded to whatever he did, matching him move for move. This reminded him of a saying: that we are our own worst enemy.","Michael’s expression became serious.","The air around him changed as he drew upon his Law. This was part of why he had withdrawn Death Ground, since he couldn’t sustain two such massive drains of energy simultaneously.","Michael’s eyes glowed faintly as his attention locked onto two targets.","The Undead High Drake and the Bone Dragon.","The same two undead he had once used together during his battle against the female Demigod. That battle had taught him something extremely important. There were certain combinations of traits that didn’t merely make an undead stronger but caused a qualitative change.","When he had layered those particular traits during that fight, the result had gone far beyond what Michael originally expected. Putting together the temporary external enhancement Michael possessed at the time, the two undead had been able to toy with a dignified Demigod.","Michael had never forgotten that scene. He wanted to reproduce it ever since.","The situation now was different, as he no longer had that temporary external support. But he did have something he hadn’t possessed back then.","[Universal Pioneer.]","Its passive effect increased the effectiveness of his Law by two hundred and fifty percent anywhere within the universe.","If he were in Aurora, this would have been a four-hundred-and-fifty-percent boost.","Michael’s eyes brightened.","Though lower, a two-hundred-and-fifty-percent boost, alongside the qualitative change from his Law, should still be powerful, right?","That removed one of the biggest uncertainties.","Michael didn’t hesitate. His first target was the Undead High Drake, as he once again applied the traits of Beginning and Lucky onto it.","Michael didn’t stop. His attention moved to the Bone Dragon. The enormous skeletal dragon was currently locked against its copied counterpart, claws and jaws crashing repeatedly. Michael’s Law wrapped around it and gave it the traits of the Undead High Drake and Beginning.","The changes came at once.","Midair, both the Undead High Drake and the Bone Dragon suddenly swelled. Their sizes exploded upward alongside their auras. The overwhelming pressure they released rolled across the battlefield in waves, forcing even nearby Rank Four undead to stagger away.","Michael’s eyes widened even more, a wide smile spreading across his face.","Beginning had already reached Demigod-level battle prowess through his repeated destruction and rebirth. Yet the pressure now coming from the High Drake and Bone Dragon... was stronger.","Far stronger."]},{"number":1256,"title":"Chapter 1256: Real Vs Copy [5]","paragraphs":["The two enormous undead dominated the sky, their presence pressing down over the battlefield like a pair of calamities.","Michael felt his heartbeat quicken.","Without borrowing any actual Rank Five existence, Michael knew at this point he could already create three Demigod-level combatants whenever he wanted.","He had always known his Law was powerful. But the Universal Pioneer title had pushed it even further. And this was with only a two-hundred-and-fifty-percent boost.","Michael was still thinking about it when a strange thought suddenly passed through his mind.","It was a fleeting thought that he might now be the best among all classes, like Beast Tamers and necromancers, below Rank Five in the universe.","His brows furrowed.","\"Wait. If a Beast Tamer possessed a Rank Five beast, would the Fourth Layer really prevent them from using it entirely?\"","That seemed... wrong, as it would effectively cripple an entire class of Awakeners whose strength came from their contracted creatures.","A frown tugged at the corner of Michael’s mouth.","\"Wait.\"","He froze, eyes widening.","Because of what happened with Lunara, he had automatically assumed he couldn’t bring his Demigod undead into the Fourth Layer.","However, Lunara wasn’t actually the same as his undead. She was connected to his soul, yes. He could even use Infinite Evolution on her. But their relationship was still fundamentally different from his other undead, since Lunara was an independent entity. She had never truly become one of his undead in the same sense as the others.","The more he thought about it, the more ridiculous it seemed. He hadn’t even tested the difference.","Michael reached through his soul connection at once and tried to summon Valeria from his Mausoleum.","Space beside him distorted and a figure appeared.","Michael stared at Valeria in shock. He had actually summoned her.","His senses swept over her at once, and he noticed her Rank Five aura was gone.","Or rather...","Suppressed.","Michael laughed.","\"I really was an idiot.\"","He had completely misread the situation because of Lunara. The restriction placed on an independent Rank Five spirit was not the same as the restriction placed on his own contracted undead. The female Demigod was still being suppressed, but she could enter without extra cost.","Perhaps it was the obedience, and the close feeling of kinship he felt with Lunara, that had clouded his judgment.","Unfortunately, Michael’s happiness lasted less than a second.","Across the battlefield, the reflected Michael had summoned its own copy of the female Demigod undead.","\"Of course.\"","He should have expected it. The copy had mirrored everything else.","Why would this be different?","Michael clicked his tongue, and his attention shifted upward to the two dragons above. Or rather, four.","The two reflected dragons had transformed too. Their appearances were nearly identical to his own, proving the copied Michael had reproduced the same Law combinations.","But... something was visibly wrong.","Michael tilted his head slightly, studying them.","\"They’re smaller.\"","Not by a tiny amount either. The difference was obvious. Though their auras had similarly crossed into Demigod-level power, compared to Michael’s real High Drake and Bone Dragon, their presence was much weaker.","As they clashed, the difference became even more obvious. What had previously been an equal fight turned completely one-sided.","Michael quickly understood what had gone wrong.","Though the other side had copied his move, it could not replicate the effectiveness his title gave.","Michael felt it wasn’t that the copy couldn’t replicate the effect of a title at all. It seemed titles like the one he had recently obtained were simply outside its bracket.","Michael’s attention shifted away from the dragons to his own copy.","Across the battlefield, the copied Valeria was staring at him.","Michael sighed and turned to Valeria beside him.","\"Go greet your sister.\"","Valeria nodded and moved without hesitation, shooting across the battlefield. The copied Valeria reacted just as fast.","BOOM!","A violent blood-colored explosion tore through the dark sky.","Michael barely looked at it, his gaze fixed on the copy standing across from him.","The advantage had finally begun tilting in his favor. Except for Jester and a few others whom Michael had kept out, he had nearly gone all out.","Still, the battle hadn’t ended. There was one thing left.","Michael himself. The reflected Michael seemed to reach the same conclusion.","A spear appeared in Michael’s hand.","[Item Name]: Venomflare Lance","[Grade]: Epic Grade ★★","At nearly the same moment, another spear appeared in the copy’s grip.","Michael smiled.","\"Since we can’t die here, let’s fight to our death. Please show me what I can do.\"","The reflected Michael didn’t answer.","Both lowered their bodies slightly.","Then vanished.","BOOM!","The water beneath their feet exploded at the same instant. They shot toward each other. Hundreds of meters disappeared in a blink.","Michael tightened his grip around the spear, preparing for their collision, when the reflected Michael suddenly threw his spear.","Something flickered across Michael’s face.","The weapon tore through the air toward his head. Michael tilted his body and easily avoided it. His instincts screamed a moment later as the Michael in front of him suddenly disappeared.","Swap?!","Amidst his shock, Michael sensed the copied Michael appear directly behind him. Its fist was already moving toward his head.","Michael twisted hard.","BOOM!","The attack passed beside his head and smashed into the air, producing a violent shockwave.","Michael swung his spear backward at once, but the reflected Michael avoided it.","Michael tensed again as his attention shifted back to the same spear he had dodged earlier, now flying toward him from the opposite direction.","When the copy swapped positions with it, the spear had inherited the location the copy had occupied, maintaining the speed at which it was thrown.","Michael leaned backward. The spear passed inches over his chest.","At the same moment, the reflected Michael reached toward it, and the weapon curved, landing neatly back in its hand.","Michael put some distance between them at once and stared speechlessly at his copy.","\"...You can do that? Can I really play like this?\" Michael couldn’t help but ask.","The reflected Michael lunged.","CLANG!","Michael blocked as their spears collided, both of them sliding backward across the water.","The copy attacked again. Michael didn’t back down and attacked just as aggressively.","Their spears clashed, with Michael managing to knock the weapon away.","The reflected Michael hurriedly retreated when Michael suddenly threw his own spear and disappeared.","\"Swap.\"","Michael appeared behind the copy.","The reflected Michael reacted without delay and twisted away from his strike.","*","A/N: Multiple Chapters coming in batches before reset! Still editing some at the moment! Also! Last day of the month! Please vote to support the novel and motivate the author! Let the novel explode with your golden tickets! Thank you for the continued support!","Hopefully, one of your favorite authors, _Drakon, wishes you a happy last day of the month!"]},{"number":1257,"title":"Chapter 1257: Bomber [1]","paragraphs":["Michael’s spear returned to his hand almost at once.","This time, neither side rushed blindly. For half a second, both Michaels simply stared at each other.","Then black flames erupted around both spears.","The fire wasn’t ordinary. It clung tightly to the shaft and spearhead, moving like liquid darkness rather than flame. That was one of the functions of the Venomflare Lance. The black fire itself was already destructive, but its true annoyance came from how difficult it was to remove once it touched something.","Unless one had a suitable means of cleansing it, putting the flame out through brute force was troublesome.","Michael tightened his grip and the two dashed at each other again.","CLANG!","Black fire exploded outward as both spears collided. With the two of them coating their bodies with mana as a protective layer, this bit of unintentional flame was harmless to them.","Michael twisted his spear at once and stabbed toward the copy’s chest.","The reflected Michael redirected the spearhead with the smallest possible movement, then stepped forward and thrust.","Michael shifted aside. The spear passed his ribs by barely a finger’s width.","With neither able to land a meaningful hit, the two didn’t hesitate to charge madly at each other.","As they continued fighting, the playful edge slowly drained from Michael’s face.","At first, he had thought the difference between them would be small. It wasn’t.","When it came to pure spear technique and close combat efficiency, the reflected Michael was suppressing him. Michael could tell the other party had reached the same advanced mastery as him, but the other party was simply more efficient at utilizing that advantage than he was.","This couldn’t be helped. As his power grew stronger, with his undead once again taking the lead in combat and him no longer needing to hide his power the way he had when he first started, Michael’s role on the frontlines had gradually been reduced to support.","However, he didn’t think this was a bad change, as it was normal for necromancers to stay behind their undead in the first place. He was only an anomaly, since even his physical strength surpassed his peers at the same level.","It was still fine for him to fight personally when he could still match his undead and his enemies were people he could personally touch, but this was the first time in a long while that Michael had to face someone in this kind of intense one-on-one battle, outside of when he battled his other body as a form of training.","But this time was different from his training with his other body since here his opponent wasn’t holding back.","Michael swung his spear at the copy, who stepped half a pace to the side to dodge.","Not willing to let the other side settle, Michael thrust at its torso, to which it responded with a small movement, dodging once again by tilting its torso.","Michael feinted high before changing direction toward the waist.","The reflected Michael barely moved its spear, yet somehow intercepted the attack with the exact angle needed to push it away.","Michael clicked his tongue.","\"Annoying.\"","The two had another clash.","CLANG!","Black flames scattered everywhere as Michael retreated three steps, while the copy only took one.","This confirmed it again: compared to the other party, his movements were wasteful.","Michael was far beyond an ordinary fighter. He had accumulated enormous amounts of combat experience, absorbed memories through Memory Infusion, fought powerful enemies, and possessed excellent comprehension. But there was still a difference between knowing how to fight and having every movement refined until almost nothing was wasted.","The reflection was showing him exactly where those gaps were.","Michael stepped forward again. The copy stabbed at him.","Michael dodged, twisting just enough to let the spearhead pass a hair’s width from his side.","A second attack followed right after, aimed lower this time, angled toward his hip. Michael managed to block, the shaft of his own spear catching the strike with a jarring clack.","A third came right after, faster than the first two, testing. Michael barely deflected it, the tip skating off the edge of his weapon before the butt of the spear whipped around and slammed toward his ribs.","He twisted away, throwing his whole upper body out of range to avoid it.","Too much.","Michael noticed it right away. The motion had carried him farther than necessary, opening a gap the copy hadn’t given him. The reflected Michael had only needed to shift slightly to avoid the same kind of follow-up. He had overreacted, wasting distance he’d now have to close again.","Michael’s eyes sharpened.","Again.","They exchanged another ten moves. Then twenty. Then thirty, the spears a blur of silver and black between them, each clash sending small shocks up through Michael’s arms.","His breathing grew heavier. Not because he was exhausted. His body could sustain this pace for hours if it had to. It was something else.","He was learning.","Every exchange exposed something new about himself, things he had never consciously noticed because there had never been anyone capable of showing them to him this clearly. If anything, it was only now that he realized his training with his other body, while helpful, had also reinforced some of his bad habits. There were simply some things training couldn’t fix, things only real experience could correct.","Michael began correcting them in real time, adjusting with every exchange.","The next thrust came, aimed for his throat.","This time, Michael moved only enough to avoid it, no wasted distance, no overcorrection. The spearhead passed beside his cheek, close enough that he felt the displaced air against his skin.","Michael countered without hesitation, driving his own spear forward in the same breath.","The reflected Michael blocked, weapon snapping up just in time.","Michael smiled.","\"Better.\"","The copy attacked again, faster now, as if acknowledging the improvement and refusing to let it stand unanswered.","Michael shifted his weight, blocked the incoming strike, and returned a thrust of his own in one fluid motion. Their spearheads clashed, sparks of light scattering across the black water beneath them."]},{"number":1258,"title":"Chapter 1258: Bomber [2]","paragraphs":["The difference was shrinking.","Slowly. But it was shrinking.","Michael’s comprehension had always been monstrous, and after everything that had happened to him recently, it had only become more ridiculous. Watching himself fight was almost like having the perfect instructor standing across the battlefield, one who couldn’t lie, couldn’t hide anything.","There was no need to wonder what he had done wrong. The answer was standing directly in front of him, spear in hand, waiting to punish him if he failed to fix it fast enough.","But comprehension didn’t mean instant perfection. Knowing what to change and actually forcing the body to abandon ingrained habits were two very different things. Even Michael needed time to rebuild more than a year of accumulated instinct into something cleaner. And the reflected Michael wasn’t going to give him that time for free.","The copy suddenly stepped in, closing the distance faster than the rhythm of the exchange between them.","Michael reacted. Too late.","The Venomflare Lance grazed across his forearm, the edge barely catching skin.","It wasn’t a deep wound. Barely a cut, the kind he would have shrugged off without a second thought under any other circumstances.","But the moment the spearhead touched him...","FWOOSH!","Black fire erupted across his arm.","Michael’s jaw clenched.","\"Shit.\"","The flames spread fast. From the cut, they crawled across his forearm toward his hand, clinging to flesh and clothing alike.","Michael hurriedly poured mana into the area. It was only after a sizable chunk of his reserves had been spent that he was able to put out the fire and let his body’s regenerative ability take over. Still, the sensation of his own poisonous fire biting into him wasn’t something he’d forget any time soon.","Michael quickly retreated.","The reflected Michael didn’t allow him the chance and gave chase.","The spear came again.","CLANG!","The impact forced him backward.","Michael’s jaw tightened further.","\"You’re really irritating.\"","The copy said nothing and then stabbed again.","Michael avoided the strike by a hair.","Then another.","And another.","Black flames streaked through the air with every movement.","Michael continued adapting. His steps became smaller. His turns cleaner. His spear recovered faster after every attack.","But the reflection remained ahead.","Michael glanced at his burning hand. Then back at the other Michael.","A strange smile slowly appeared on his face.","Painful as this was...","This fight might actually be one of the best things the Origin Battlefield had ever given him.","Without warning, the reflected Michael suddenly discarded the Venomflare Lance.","Michael tensed.","\"What are you...\"","The copy lunged at him. Its hand reached directly toward Michael’s arm.","Michael reacted at once, twisting away, but his movements, even refined by his heightened comprehension, were still too slow to keep the copy from exploiting the opening.","Michael’s stomach dropped the moment the reflected Michael’s palm touched the back of his hand.","The copy’s skin darkened, and its flesh shriveled. Its arm had abruptly decayed.","\"What the hell?\"","Michael tried to pull away, but the copy held on.","A deep sense of unease suddenly surged through him.","\"No way...\"","The copied Michael’s arm swelled.","BOOOOOOM!","Its arm exploded.","Michael’s hand detonated with it.","The blast tore them apart in an instant. Both bodies were thrown in opposite directions. Michael spun through the air before forcing himself upright.","His feet struck the surface of the still water, sliding backward for hundreds of meters before finally stopping.","Pain shot through his head, and he quickly turned to check the arm the copy had touched.","His hand was gone.","Destroyed from just above the wrist.","Blood poured from the stump before his regeneration swiftly began closing the wound, and a second later, a new hand could be seen. This was an automatic action, without Michael’s intentional control. This was also the first time he had seen the full effect of his body’s healing factor.","It was indeed fast, not any weaker than using his Law to copy Beginning’s Law of brutal rebirth to heal.","Michael looked up. Across from him, the reflected Michael’s arm had regenerated.","\"...Corpse Explosion?\"","That was definitely Corpse Explosion.","But this time... it hadn’t been used on a corpse.","Or rather...","Realization struck him.","\"So that’s possible?\"","The logic clicked into place almost at once.","Corpse Explosion didn’t care about the original identity of what it detonated. It needed dead matter that could carry death energy and be recognized as a corpse or corpse fragment. That was all.","If he could force a part of the body into a sufficiently dead state...","Then technically, that body part became usable.","\"What the fuck? Are you a suicide bomber?!\"","Fear took hold in Michael’s heart. At the same time, his excitement didn’t disappear. If anything, it became sharper.","He was learning. Really learning.","So one could really play like this?","Not just refining what he already knew, but discovering applications he had never even considered before.","Unfortunately, the reflected Michael had no intention of giving him time to appreciate that. Its regenerated arm moved.","Michael’s breath caught.","\"Don’t tell me...\"","The copy grabbed its own forearm. Decay spread across the limb at once.","Michael’s face twisted.","\"No.\"","The arm swelled. Michael turned around and ran.","BOOOOOOM!","The reflected Michael’s forearm exploded behind him. The blast tore across the water. Michael accelerated harder, letting the shockwave push him forward instead of trying to resist it.","Behind him, the copy’s arm had already regenerated. Michael glanced back and saw this.","\"You’ve got to be kidding me.\"","Another hand decayed. Another explosion followed.","BOOM!","The reflected Michael chased. Michael’s instincts screamed and he changed direction.","BOOOOOOM!","The blast caught Michael from the side and sent him tumbling across the water. He recovered almost at once and pushed himself upright.","The copy started approaching him. Michael stared at it.","\"This is insane.\"","The reflected Michael decayed part of its thigh. Michael’s mouth twitched.","\"You’re seriously using your leg now?\"","BOOM!","The explosion launched the copy forward. Understanding hit Michael a heartbeat too late: it hadn’t merely used the blast as an attack, it had used it for movement.","The reflected Michael shot through the air at terrifying speed, propelled by the detonation of its own leg. Michael barely raised an arm before the copy appeared in front of him. Its fist slammed into his chest.","BOOM!","Michael was thrown backward. His body skipped across the black water several times before he twisted and landed on his feet. Pain spread through his chest, but what bothered him more was the realization.","\"...You can use Corpse Explosion for propulsion too?\""]},{"number":1259,"title":"Chapter 1259: Top 11","paragraphs":["Disbelief gave way to concentration on Michael’s face. If the copy could do it, then he could too.","The logic was already clear. Decay a body part, letting it cross the threshold into dead tissue, then use Corpse Explosion. Simple. At least in theory.","Michael looked down at his left hand.","\"This is going to hurt.\"","He placed his right palm over his forearm and forcefully infused it with dark energy while actively limiting his regeneration. His skin darkened and his muscle withered as sensation in the arm began disappearing.","\"...Huh.\"","He had expected a bit of pain. Instead, the pain weakened the further the decay progressed. That made sense. The tissue was dying. By the time his forearm had fully crossed that line, he could barely feel it at all.","The discomfort came more from knowing it was his own arm than from the dead flesh itself.","Michael stared at it for half a second. Then he activated Corpse Explosion at the approaching copy.","BOOM!","The forearm detonated. Michael’s entire body jerked from the force as a shockwave tore outward, blasting water away beneath him.","Michael staggered but didn’t scream. Though the proximity of the explosion brought him pain, it wasn’t above his pain threshold.","Michael stared at the stump as regeneration began right away.","\"Oh.\"","Surprise flickered across his face.","\"That’s much better than I thought.\"","The hand reformed. Michael flexed it as his gaze returned to the fight. The reflected Michael had already begun moving again.","This time Michael didn’t retreat. He decayed part of his leg and used Corpse Explosion.","BOOM!","The blast launched him sideways. Michael nearly lost control and spun through the air.","\"Too much.\"","He landed hard, recovered, then laughed.","The copy appeared in front of him. Michael detonated part of his shoulder.","BOOM!","The force twisted his body away from the incoming strike, causing the attack to miss.","Michael’s grin widened. The two Michaels moved again. This time, both were using it.","BOOM!","One exploded a leg and shot forward.","BOOM!","The other detonated an arm to twist around a strike.","BOOM!","Another burst changed direction in midair.","Their bodies became weapons in the most literal sense. Every few seconds, flesh died, exploded, regenerated, and was sacrificed again just as quickly. Michael could hardly believe this was how his own skill could be used.","The reflected Michael rushed him. Michael detonated part of his thigh and accelerated forward instead of away.","Michael caught the copy’s wrist, and the copy caught his. Both understood at once what the other intended as they stared at each other from point-blank range, their expressions becoming almost identical as every limb darkened.","BOOOOOOOOOOOOOOM!","The explosion swallowed both Michaels completely. For a moment, there was nothing but light, pressure, and violently displaced black water. The blast was far larger than any of their previous exchanges, and the resulting shockwave tore outward across the battlefield, forcing several distant undead to pause or stagger.","When the light finally faded, two mutilated bodies could be seen lying far apart on the surface of the water. Neither moved. Michael’s torso was badly damaged, and the copy wasn’t in any better condition.","For several seconds, the battlefield remained strangely still around them compared to the chaos raging elsewhere.","A moment later, Michael’s lips curled upward. He smiled.","\"I won.\"","And he had.","Truthfully, the outcome had already been decided long before this final exchange. The moment Michael used Echoed Bestowal on the Undead High Drake and Bone Dragon, the balance had broken. From that moment onward, the two enhanced undead had begun tearing through their counterparts.","By the time Michael and his copy had reached the stage of blowing apart their own limbs, the battle around them was effectively over.","Right now, only one enemy remained.","The reflected Michael.","Michael’s regeneration began working as bone extended from his shoulders and hips. Within moments, Michael’s body was whole again. He sat upright slowly. Across from him, the reflected Michael still hadn’t regenerated.","Michael looked at it for a moment. Perhaps the Gatekeeper had already recognized that the battle was over.","Michael turned his head to his undead. Beginning stood not far away. The giant was still enormous, his body covered in damage but his aura remaining monstrous.","Michael pointed toward the fallen copy.","\"End it.\"","Beginning moved without hesitation. Each step shook the black water. The reflected Michael finally twitched, but there was no time left.","Beginning raised one massive foot. For a moment, the shadow of it completely swallowed the copy. Then it came down.","BOOOOOOM!","The black ocean exploded upward. The reflected Michael disappeared beneath the impact.","Before Michael could admonish Beginning for the lack of respect shown toward its master, a blue panel appeared in front of him.","[Top 50 Gatekeeper Trial Completed.]","The panel remained for only a moment before more lines appeared beneath it.","[Evaluation Complete.]","[Your demonstrated combat strength has exceeded the theoretical combat strength calculated for Awakeners ranked between 11 and 50.]","[Your performance cannot be accurately represented by the average combat standards of this ranking interval.]","[Final Placement Assigned.]","[Fourth Layer Battlefield Ranking: 11]","For several seconds, Michael simply stared at the number before he slowly exhaled.","\"That’s a huge jump.\"","Michael’s lips slowly curved upward as he continued reading the messages that appeared on the panel before him.","[Excellent Performance Detected.]","[Special Reward Granted.]","[Ranking Challenge Quota Refunded: +1]","Michael laughed.","\"Again?\"","His final challenge had been returned to him once more. At this point, the Origin Battlefield almost seemed determined to keep him climbing.","Michael opened the ranking interface. It had changed again.","[11. Michael Norman]","Michael’s eyes slowly moved upward.","[10. ...]","Then higher. Nine. Eight. Seven. All the way to one.","Curiosity sharpened behind his eyes. However, this time Michael didn’t challenge anyone again.","Michael slowly closed the ranking panel. Physically, he could probably force another battle if he really wanted to, but he was mentally drained. Too much had happened in too short a period. He needed to rest. The Top 10 could wait.","More importantly, Rank 11 had already accomplished what he originally came here to do. He wanted people to see him, not just know his name from some universal announcement. He wanted them to understand that the person behind that name wasn’t easy prey.","Rank 11 already did that.","* * *","A/N: Starting from today, though the update times might be irregular, I’ll be updating four to five Chapters a day. I plead with the readers to please show support in any way they can. Voting in particular is very motivating, as it gives the author something to look forward to. So please cast those golden tickets, and thank you for the continued support!"]},{"number":1260,"title":"Chapter 1260: Awakeners With Their Own Cornerstones [1]","paragraphs":["As Michael slowly recovered his energy, his thoughts naturally returned to the battle he had just experienced. To be honest, he had learned a lot. Still, Michael felt a faint sense of regret.","\"Would’ve been better if it taught me something about my Law.\"","That was the one area he had truly hoped to gain insight into. His Law was increasingly important to his strength. Echoed Bestowal had already proven itself capable of producing terrifying results, especially after Universal Pioneer’s boost. If the copy had shown him another application of this Law that he could use to create a skill, this fight would have been so much more fundamental to his growth.","But the reflection hadn’t really shown him anything fundamentally new there. Michael sighed.","\"Can’t have everything.\"","Besides, the battle had already been worth it if he considered the new application of Corpse Explosion. Still, there was also an issue with this method of self-explosion.","Michael looked down at his regenerated limbs. He still found the concept ridiculous. In this arena, where death and damage were erased after the match, the method had been almost perfectly safe. But doing the same outside was another matter entirely.","Unlike here, if something went wrong outside, there was no system protection. So Michael didn’t imagine himself casually blowing up his limbs every time he entered combat.","Maybe it could work as an emergency technique, since if he really had to use this method, it meant he was truly in dire straits. But it couldn’t be used as a regular fighting method.","Still... the skill itself had given him another idea.","Michael’s gaze slowly shifted to Beginning, who was standing nearby. The giant had already reduced his size considerably after the battle, but the violent aura around him hadn’t disappeared completely.","Beginning noticed Michael’s stare and turned to look at him. For several seconds, master and undead simply looked at each other.","Something shifted behind Michael’s eyes.","\"...You.\"","A spark of interest crossed his expression. If there was anyone Corpse Explosion could work absurdly well with, it was Beginning. His Law of Brutal Rebirth was already built around destruction and reconstruction. Beginning could literally destroy his own body repeatedly and return stronger.","His thoughts accelerated. Excitement crept into his expression.","What if Beginning, at the peak of his power, allowed part of himself to die, then detonated that portion through Corpse Explosion while simultaneously using Brutal Rebirth?","The destruction would be far greater than anything he could personally output. This was due to the difference in mass, size, weight, and actual strength.","One had to understand Rank Four existences could reach destructive power comparable to nuclear weapons, while the most exceptional among them could go far beyond that. A modern nuclear bomb was terrifying because of the amount of destruction it released in one instant. A Rank Four supernatural was different, since they could move, think, and adapt.","And most importantly, they could repeatedly release attacks at that level. Beginning was exceptional even among Rank Fours. At the peak of Brutal Rebirth, he had already pushed his combat prowess across the boundary and into the level of a Demigod.","His fighting method, however, remained comparatively simple. There wasn’t much subtlety to it.","But now, thinking of the new application of Corpse Explosion, if he were to teach Beginning this skill, what would happen if a hundred-metre-tall giant used its arm as a bomb?","Michael felt a chill run down his back.","\"...That’s ridiculous.\"","His own arm had produced a respectable explosion, but compared to Beginning, he didn’t have the mass, size, or strength. Beginning’s arm at one hundred meters tall would contain an absurd amount of power.","Thinking about the future made Michael increasingly excited. Fortunately, the arena had not forced him out right after the match ended. He still had nearly three hours remaining.","Michael did not waste the opportunity. For the next three hours, he seriously trained Beginning to the fullest extent he could manage.","Meanwhile, outside the arena, the Fourth Layer had still not calmed down. If anything, the attention surrounding Michael had only intensified.","One had to understand what the Top 1000 Battlefield Ranking represented. The Fourth Layer was meant for Rank Four Awakeners. Among the upper portions of that ranking, especially the Top 300, every Awakener was Level 100.","The peak of Rank Four. Each one stood only a single major advancement away from becoming Rank Five.","This list would have been considered normal if Michael Norman didn’t exist. During the previous opening of the Origin Battlefield, there had already been one name that looked completely wrong among them.","A Level 75 Awakener had somehow appeared in the Fourth Layer among Awakeners a full Rank above him. That alone had drawn attention.","But now the Origin Battlefield had reopened. And in only a short period of time, that same Level 75 Awakener had climbed all the way to Rank 11.","The sight was almost offensive to the eyes. Within the entire Top 100, Michael was the only one not at Level 100. Every other name belonged to a Peak Rank Four Awakener.","Michael stood among them as a Level 75, Rank Three Awakener. And he was not near the bottom, but at the very top, with only ten people above him.","What did this mean?","Many powerful Awakeners had reached the same conclusion Michael himself had suspected earlier: there was a point within the rankings where one needed power that crossed the normal boundary of Rank Four to stay there.","Demigod-level combat prowess. This made Michael’s position far more shocking.","If Rank 11 required Demigod-level combat power, then didn’t that mean a Level 75 Rank Three Awakener possessed Demigod-level strength?","Those who had already investigated Michael became even more cautious. For those who knew almost nothing about Michael, the conclusion was still largely the same: this person truly wasn’t simple, not with all the chaos he’d been causing lately.","It felt to them as though the universe itself no longer seemed normal.","For three days, the heat continued. Michael himself spent those days peacefully, and nothing particularly serious happened.","It was only on the fourth day that something changed."]},{"number":1261,"title":"Chapter 1261: Awakeners With Their Own Cornerstones [2]","paragraphs":["Three days ago.","After settling into Rank 11, Michael had not been idle. The first thing he did was return to Aurora and pay close attention to the situation there.","Unlike the previous opening of the Origin Battlefield, Awakeners were no longer forced to remain inside until the entire period ended. This time, they could leave and return as they pleased. The only restriction was that they had to spend a required amount of time within the Battlefield before the monthly reset. This made things much more convenient for many Awakeners.","Michael knew his sudden rise in the rankings would cause reactions. It was impossible for someone in Rank 11, especially someone like him, to not attract attention. So he returned to Aurora to make sure he wasn’t blind to whatever followed.","Fortunately, the Supernatural Association agents had once again proven useful. Thanks to them allowing him to borrow their source of information, Michael was able to learn a few things.","The results were reassuring. His ranking had done exactly what he wanted it to do.","A significant number of people who had been paying attention to Aurora or considering whether Michael could be pressured had backed away. Many forces that had been quietly testing the waters simply disappeared from the Association’s reports.","It wasn’t that their interest in Michael had vanished. Far from it.","But interest and willingness to act were very different things. Power did matter a lot in this universe.","His Rank 11 placement had not made everyone friendly, but simply making them more cautious, after realizing he had the power to threaten them at a civilization-wide level, had made many neutral.","To Michael, this was enough.","At this point, Michael was certain that as long as he did not trigger another ridiculous event and give the Origin Will another excuse to broadcast his name across the universe, the attention surrounding him would eventually settle. The novelty would fade, and people would adjust to his existence.","This was the outcome Michael wanted. Once that happened, bringing his family back to Aurora would become much safer.","Aunt Mia and Lily had already spent enough time away from their normal lives because of the trouble surrounding him. Michael had no intention of keeping them hidden forever.","When the situation calmed sufficiently, he planned to return them to Aurora, though it might only be Aunt Mia at first. Thanks to Lily’s awakening, her life as a normal teenager had already ended, regardless of what happened next.","With Aurora temporarily stable, and the pressure surrounding his name beginning to move in the direction he wanted, Michael shifted more of his attention to his territory in the Land of Origin. The Eternal Crown Empire had become increasingly important after the establishment of the Subsidiary Territorial Anchor.","Knowing there was a real possibility that the Land of Origin would one day become directly connected to the outside world, Michael did not treat the affairs of the empire casually like before.","With this mindset, Michael turned his attention to the problem that had been bothering him.","Energy Points. The Subsidiary Territorial Anchor was powerful. But that ability came with a cost.","Even though the empire could afford to spend large amounts of resources, the conversion rate remained painful. One high-grade mana crystal only provided one Energy Point.","Even transporting an ordinary person required ten Energy Points, the same as teleporting a Rank Two being. The cost rose dramatically once Rank Three existences became involved.","If Michael only intended to use the Anchor occasionally, this would hardly matter. The Eternal Crown Empire was wealthy enough to support a few expensive transfers.","But Michael wasn’t planning around the present anymore. He was thinking about a possible future where the Land of Origin and the outside world interacted regularly. One should know that if he wanted to sustain the cost of using his talent, he couldn’t rely on himself alone.","Only a force like the empire could provide him with resources he could use, and as he grew stronger he would only need more. Making the empire stronger not only benefited the people, but it benefited him as well.","However, to achieve this goal, he needed to solve the energy issue. Even an empire as big as his could bleed itself dry through repeated consumption at large scale.","This forced Michael to search for alternatives. The description of the Anchor had already given him the clue.","Its Energy Requirement could be fulfilled through any energy source. Mana crystals were simply the most convenient source Michael had tested first. They were never stated to be mandatory.","If the Anchor needed energy, then there was no reason that energy had to come from something that had already been condensed into a crystal.","Living beings contained mana too, so could they also serve as an energy source?","This thought eventually led Michael to the cheapest possible source.","Mages. Or more accurately, people with sufficiently large mana reserves.","Fortunately, testing quickly confirmed his suspicion. The Dominion Conduit could absorb mana directly from an individual and convert it into Energy Points.","The person didn’t even need to belong to the Mage pathway. This changed everything for Michael and the empire.","Mana recovered naturally. Crystals didn’t. A mage who contributed most of their reserve could recover through rest, potions, or simply absorbing ambient mana.","Using people as energy suppliers therefore transformed what had previously been a consumable-resource problem into something closer to manpower management.","Once Michael confirmed this, he promptly issued an imperial order, requiring many kingdoms and subordinate territories under the Eternal Crown Empire to provide mana-capable personnel to support the newly established Anchor.","Michael didn’t demand their strongest people indiscriminately. Each kingdom was simply given a quota.","Either they provided five Rank Two mages or mana-focused supernaturals of equivalent reserves... or one Rank Three mage.","Some kingdoms sent considerably more to flatter him.","Naturally, Michael did not expect them to provide powerful supernaturals for free. Those assigned to the station received imperial compensation.","The greatest one, however, was the chance to cultivate in the Fourth Layer of the Origin Battlefield."]},{"number":1262,"title":"Chapter 1262: Awakeners With Their Own Cornerstones [3]","paragraphs":["For this particular benefit, Michael had initially hesitated. One had to remember that the Land of Origin did not contain only natives.","There were Awakeners there as well. People like him who came from outside worlds. Allowing large numbers of people to gather around something as important as the Subsidiary Territorial Anchor had naturally made Michael uncomfortable at first.","The Universal Cornerstone was already one of the greatest treasures he possessed. The Anchor was directly connected to it.","Letting too many unknown people study the station, work around it, and repeatedly interact with it felt dangerous. For a while, Michael considered restricting the entire area to natives he personally trusted.","But the more he thought about it, the less practical that became, so he decided to be less restrictive.","Most of his confidence came from the fact that his strength had increased tremendously. He was no longer the same person who had to carefully hide every unusual thing he owned and constantly worry that someone much stronger would simply take it from him.","Except for something stronger than Rank Five deciding to intervene, Michael felt he could walk freely anywhere in the universe.","More importantly, guarding something that had already been exposed was exhausting. Sooner or later, other civilizations would claim their own Cornerstones and begin discovering the same functions.","There was no point acting as if the secret could remain unique forever. Michael also had no confidence that his own identity within the Land of Origin was completely hidden anymore.","He had tried his best to keep his identity secret. But there was no certainty in the world.","Ever since he conquered the empire, his movements had become too large. The number of people around him had increased.","The number of Awakeners passing through the Land of Origin was not small. Michael had never caught anyone directly, but he would be foolish to believe that absolutely no one had already connected Michael Norman of Aurora with the Emperor ruling the Eternal Crown Empire.","Once he accepted that, his attitude changed. Instead of wasting too much energy trying to hide everything, Michael decided to push his advantage as far as possible while he still had it.","If other Awakeners were eventually going to understand the true value of Universal Cornerstones, then he wanted his network, territory, transport system, and energy infrastructure to already be far ahead by the time they did.","That meant being more aggressive. Of course, this didn’t mean he could also be careless.","Michael still placed restrictions on who could pass through the Anchor. Anyone he allowed to enter the Origin Battlefield from the Land of Origin would not be allowed outside.","Until another Universal Cornerstone was publicly claimed, Michael intended to keep that group inside the Battlefield. Even if Michael accepted that these functions would eventually become known, he did not intend to be the one who handed every detail to the rest of the universe early.","The same concern influenced how he organized the people supplying energy to the Anchor. Rank Two mages and other Rank Two mana-focused supernaturals were allowed to travel into the Origin Battlefield and contribute directly from the Eternal Crown side.","Rank Three practitioners were handled differently. They recharged the network from the Land of Origin.","Rank Three individuals were simply too capable. They were far more likely to notice details that weaker practitioners missed.","By restricting Rank Three contributors to the empire-side Anchor, Michael could make use of their enormous mana reserves without exposing the inner structure of the cornerstone to them.","It was an imperfect solution. But Michael had never expected perfect secrecy.","What he wanted was delay. Every extra day before the rest of the universe caught up to him was another day of advantage.","Within a single day, the Anchor’s reserves had risen to a rate Michael had never achieved through crystals. By the end of the third day, the shared network reserve had reached:","[Stored Energy Points: 186,740]","Michael was immensely satisfied with the result. The amount wasn’t infinite.","Once large-scale Rank Three or Rank Four transfers became common, even hundreds of thousands of Energy Points could disappear quickly. But that wasn’t what mattered.","The important thing was that he had found a renewable source. And this was only the beginning.","At the current rate, the amount was already substantial.","An ordinary person or Rank Two existence required only ten Energy Points for a transfer.","With 186,740 Energy Points stored, Michael could transport 18,674 of them before exhausting the reserve completely.","Rank Three existences were far more expensive.","Each required 1,000 Energy Points.","That meant the same reserve could transport 186 Rank Three existences, with 740 Energy Points remaining afterward.","For only three days of accumulation, this was already impressive.","Michael had intended to continue building that advantage on the fourth day. Only a few hours into the new day, however, a notification suddenly appeared before his eyes.","[Universal Milestone Update.]","[Congratulations to Aurelius Veyr for successfully claiming the second Universal Cornerstone.]","Michael froze. A wave of surprise ran through him. For a moment, he simply stared at the panel.","Someone else had finally done it. He had expected it eventually, of course. The Origin Battlefield had already exposed the existence of Universal Cornerstones to everyone. With countless civilizations, geniuses, and powerful forces searching for them, it had only been a matter of time.","Still, seeing it actually happen felt different.","Michael quickly opened the Territory Ranking. The familiar panel appeared.","[Origin Battlefield Territory Ranking]","[1. The Eternal Crown: Michael Norman]","[2. Sovereign’s Reach: Aurelius Veyr]","Michael studied the name for a moment.","Aurelius Veyr. Michael felt at once that this person was unlikely to be simple.","He opened the Fourth Layer ranking and searched the name. To his surprise, he found it right away.","[18. Aurelius Veyr]","[Realm: Star Nation]","Rank 18. That was much closer to him than he had expected.","More importantly, the realm name was familiar.","Star Nation. Michael recognized it at once as the home realm of the Star Race. They were especially famous for technology and were one of the top ten civilizations in the universe."]},{"number":1263,"title":"Chapter 1263: Spirit Tamer [1]","paragraphs":["In the universe, there was a difference between a race and a civilization. Regardless of the distinction, both were commonly divided into four broad levels.","Low. Mid. High. Top.","The two rankings did not necessarily match. A race could belong to a Top-level civilization while remaining naturally weak.","Likewise, an exceptionally gifted race could exist within a civilization that had failed to develop properly. Aurora was a good example.","Humans there were considered somewhere around a low-Mid-level race by universal standards. Aurora itself, however, had already developed into a high-Mid-level civilization.","Humans were the most widespread race Michael knew of in the universe. Their greatest advantage was numbers.","Humans lacked many of the overwhelming natural advantages possessed by stronger races. Elves generally had high magical affinity and long lifespans. Dragons possessed exceptional bodies, high magical affinity, powerful bloodlines, and inherited racial memories.","Humans were comparatively ordinary. They were only clearly superior to some weaker races in overall potential.","Goblins were one example. Like humans, ordinary goblins were not particularly impressive individually. Like vampires, a good part of them could be said to belong to the monster race.","Much like Starborn were to the human race, only variants of the goblin race usually reached the upper levels of supernatural society. Yet this did not stop goblins from developing powerful civilizations.","There was even a Goblin civilization whose technological advancement could be compared with the Star Nation. Starborn possessed terrifying natural intelligence and an innate ability to easily interact with rare forms of energy, particularly light and several higher derivatives related to it.","Their mental development was remarkably fast. By around eight years old, a Starborn’s brain was already fully mature and could reason better than adults of other races.","This intelligence was one of the foundations behind the Star Nation’s technological dominance. But their gift came with an equally severe curse.","Their lifespan was extremely short. Most Starborn could only live for around forty years naturally.","Even after becoming supernaturals, their lifespan remained unusually poor compared to others at the same Rank. A human, elf, or other supernatural of equivalent strength could often outlive a Starborn by a considerable margin.","That was the contradiction of their race.","In any case, seeing that Aurelius Veyr was not only ranked highly among the many other Rank Four existences in the universe, but was also a Starborn belonging to the Star Nation, made his identity even more interesting.","Did he claim it alone like I did?","The thought only lasted a moment before Michael shook his head.","It wasn’t that he underestimated others. But if the difficulty of claiming another Universal Cornerstone was anywhere near what he had experienced, accomplishing it alone was incredibly difficult.","Michael had only succeeded because he possessed advantages that were difficult to reproduce. Even then, the process had not been simple.","Someone else succeeding only four days after the Origin Battlefield reopened made Michael suspect there had been more involved. Perhaps Aurelius had encountered a situation similar to the one Michael had witnessed, where several powerful Awakeners grouped together to attack the monsters protecting a cornerstone.","The difference could simply be that this time, the assault had succeeded. The other possibility was that Aurelius might have received direct support from the Star Nation.","That possibility actually seemed more likely. Not everyone developed the way Michael did.","He had grown from an ordinary Awakener into a realm-shaking civilization power in roughly a year, and he had done most of it without any powerful organization carrying him forward. Even Director Arven, who did not strike Michael as someone with exceptional social skills, still belonged to an organization.","Michael had little doubt that if someone like Arven genuinely decided to claim a Universal Cornerstone and the academy supported him fully, success would only be a matter of time.","Aurelius Veyr came from the Star Nation. A Top-level civilization. With that kind of background, manpower and resources were the least surprising things he could possess.","The more Michael considered it, the more certain he became that Rank 18 had probably not claimed Sovereign’s Reach entirely alone.","Unfortunately, no matter how curious Michael became, there was nothing else to learn. The ranking had only given him a rank and realm.","Beyond that, Aurelius Veyr remained a mystery.","Just as Michael was thinking about what changes this new rival might bring, something else caught his attention. He turned his head slightly toward the sky and smiled.","\"She’s awake?\"","Almost at the same moment, far away in another location, Michael’s other body opened his eyes.","Golden fields stretched endlessly around him. Soft wind moved through the grass, sending waves across the plain beneath the dark sky of the Mausoleum. Above, the heavens were painted in shifting aurora hues.","Green, violet, blue, and faint traces of gold drifted slowly across the darkness like enormous ribbons of light, casting a soft glow over the entire field. The colors reflected faintly across the tips of the grass, making the plain look almost unreal.","Several meters away, beneath that strange glowing sky, a figure lay unconscious among the golden grass. Michael had been waiting there for some time.","The moment he sensed the change, he stood. His attention went at once to the figure lying several meters away.","Arianne. It had already been three days since Arianne returned from the trial.","Michael couldn’t help but think back to that moment. It had happened shortly after he returned from the ranking arena, after spending the remaining three hours teaching Beginning how to combine Corpse Explosion with Brutal Rebirth and repeatedly testing just how destructive the combination could become.","Not long after, the Awakening Temple had finally sent him the notification he had been waiting for.","[A participant has successfully completed the Awakening Trial.]","After confirming that she was alive, Michael had spent a long time reprimanding her for the reckless decisions she had made inside the trial.","Arianne’s experience gave him his first proper understanding of how the Awakening Temple worked from the participant’s perspective."]},{"number":1264,"title":"Chapter 1264: Spirit Tamer [2]","paragraphs":["Once his frustration settled, Michael was able to learn far more about the Awakening Temple than he knew before.","It also revealed more about the nature of the Awakening Trials themselves.","Externally, Arianne had only been inside for around five hours. For her, however, five years had passed.","Fortunately, despite several difficulties and more than one close brush with death, Arianne had managed to complete two of the three Trial Tasks.","The final evaluation had been Exceptional, granting her a tamer class as she wanted, fifty Attribute Points, a maxed-out Rank Zero, and a trait. There were a few more rewards, but these were the major ones.","Squatting beside Arianne, Michael cast Detect on her.","[Spirit Tamer Level 10]","Even with his prejudice against the Hell difficulty, Michael had to admit that its rewards were very good.","He had no idea what someone would receive from Normal, Hard, or Extreme difficulty with the same Exceptional evaluation, but he highly doubted it would be comparable.","Arianne had gotten almost exactly what she wanted. A taming-related class.","More specifically, a variant class Michael had never heard of before. From everything Arianne had told him, it was clearly superior to the ordinary Beast Tamer class.","The easiest way to see that was through her attributes. The trial had directly pushed her to Level 10, the maximum of Rank Zero, and had also rewarded her with fifty free Attribute Points.","Her total attributes now reached 170. Michael only needed a thought to understand the division.","Arianne’s new body had been created using his blood. Because of that, her racial foundation was already comparable to a High Human, granting six Attribute Points per level.","Across ten levels, that accounted for sixty points. Removing the fifty points directly rewarded by the trial left another sixty points.","That meant her class itself had also been providing six Attribute Points per level. Only special classes had that kind of growth.","An ordinary Beast Tamer class gave four Attribute Points per level while Spirit Tamer gave six. Just from that alone, there was already a considerable gap between the two classes.","And attributes were usually only the most obvious difference. The mechanics of the class only made that difference more obvious.","A Beast Tamer was simple enough from the name alone. They formed contracts with beasts, strengthened them, fought alongside them, and developed abilities centered around controlling or supporting those contracted creatures.","Spirit Tamers were different. According to Arianne, they could contract not only beasts, but also spiritual beings obtained from the Spirit Realm or created through artificial means.","Michael knew a little about the Spirit Realm. It was another separate dimension with its own laws, much like the Netherworld.","But unlike Hell, which was closely associated with demons, or Heaven, which was associated with angels, the Spirit Realm remained far more mysterious, like the Netherworld, and wasn’t easy to gain access to.","Arianne’s trial had revealed much more to him. Spirit beings could generally be obtained in two ways.","The first was through a ritual. During the ritual, a portion of the Spirit Tamer’s consciousness or spirit would enter the Spirit Realm and search for a compatible spirit to contract.","The Spirit Realm itself was divided into two known layers: the Dark Layer, and the Light Layer.","The Dark Layer was chaotic. The difference in strength and potential between spirits there could be enormous.","A weak Spirit Tamer with poor talent might still enter the Dark Layer, but they would have very little control over what happened afterward. In many cases, they couldn’t even properly see the spirits around them.","They could only release their presence and intent, then wait for something compatible to respond. Only after a contract was successfully completed would the true form of the spirit become visible to them.","The Light Layer was completely different. It could almost be considered the true world of the Spirit Realm.","Rare spirits that would be considered treasures elsewhere could be encountered naturally. There were even terrifying existences such as Elemental Kings and other high-ranking spiritual beings.","The stronger and more talented the Spirit Tamer, the greater their chance of accessing the Light Layer during a ritual.","Michael was left in awe while listening to Arianne explain all of this. The trial world was absurdly detailed.","Its power system was not some shallow imitation created only for a test. It had history, culture, and so on, just like any other real place. Even information about dimensions that existed in the real universe.","That made Michael realize another major advantage the Awakening Temple possessed over natural awakening.","Experience. A naturally awakened person might receive a class and several skills, but they still had to learn how to use everything afterward.","Arianne had spent five years living with the foundation of her future profession before returning. Even ignoring the rewards, that alone was valuable.","There was also the suspected lack of an age restriction. If the Awakening Temple truly allowed anyone who met its requirements to undergo a trial regardless of age, then its value was even greater than Michael had originally believed.","It didn’t simply awaken people. It could produce experienced Awakeners from the moment they emerged.","As for why Arianne was currently unconscious, it was because Michael had just finished evolving her contracted spirits. Spirit Tamers were closely connected to their spirits.","Unlike a necromancer’s undead or a beast tamer’s tamed creatures, contracted spirits could not simply advance on their own. Their growth was tied to the Rank of their tamer.","This was Michael’s first time encountering such a restriction. Still, grade evolution was different from Rank advancement.","Over the past three days, Michael had sacrificed several Evolution Essence Crystals on Arianne’s spirits. By the end, however, the results were more than worth it.","All of Arianne’s currently contracted spirits had been pushed to Epic Grade ★★★ at level 10.","* * *","A/N: Two more Chapters will be uploaded in a while after editing. Another will be uploaded much later in the night on my end, which is about ten hours from now. The two are coming much faster. Thank you for the continued support!!"]},{"number":1265,"title":"Chapter 1265: Difference Between Natural and Artificial Awakening [1]","paragraphs":["This was the first time Michael had personally come across something like this. From what he could tell, there was nothing stopping him from pushing Arianne’s spirits even higher in grade.","If he had been willing to spend the resources, he could have used a Legendary-grade Evolution Essence Crystal and attempted to raise one of them directly to Legendary Grade while it was still only Level 10.","A Legendary Grade creature at Level 10.","Normally, something naturally born with that kind of grade and potential would already begin life around Rank Two at the very least. It would then require comparatively little time to enter Rank Three and, depending on its race and bloodline, could naturally mature around Rank Four without encountering the kinds of barriers ordinary creatures struggled with.","Yet Arianne’s spirits were sitting at Level 10. That contradiction fascinated Michael.","Michael took the matter seriously. Anything capable of interacting with Infinite Evolution in an unusual way deserved his attention. His talent had already shown multiple times that the evolution could produce very different results depending on the circumstances surrounding it.","Arianne’s contracted spirits introduced another variable entirely.","One had to know that when a contracted creature advanced in Rank, classes such as Necromancers and Beast Tamers could receive a certain amount of feedback from that advancement. Even something as ordinary as a Common Grade ★★★ undead or tamed beast advancing to Rank One would still strengthen its master to some extent.","The higher the grade of the creature, the greater that feedback became. There was no perfectly accurate formula for it, but Michael had noticed a rough pattern. If a Common Grade creature gave one portion of feedback, then a Rare Grade creature could be seen as giving roughly twice as much, Extraordinary Grade around twice that of Rare, Epic Grade around twice that of Extraordinary, and Legendary Grade around twice that of Epic.","The actual result varied depending on race and individual foundation, but the general trend was about the same.","According to Arianne, Spirit Tamers also benefited from this mechanic. Arianne currently possessed three Epic Grade ★★★ spirits, all trapped at Level 10 only because she herself had not advanced.","Once she completed her Rank One advancement, they would be able to follow.","And when they did... the feedback she received from several Epic Grade spirits advancing together would be enormous compared to what an ordinary tamer experienced.","Her own racial foundation was already strong. Now her contracted spirits had also been forcefully evolved far beyond what someone at Rank Zero should normally possess.","Michael could already imagine how ridiculous her foundation might become after a single major advancement. The spirits themselves would benefit just as much.","An Epic Grade ★★★ existence fighting at the same Level and Rank as an ordinary creature was already naturally superior in nearly every fundamental aspect. Once Arianne reached Rank One and removed the restriction holding them back, Michael doubted many supernaturals at the same level would be able to compete with her spirits at all.","This included his cousin.","In fact, it was because of Lily that Michael had paid even more attention to this discovery. From her previous entry into the Origin Battlefield, Michael had already realized that no matter how much he strengthened the beasts she could tame, there was a limit.","It was similar to his own early days.","But Arianne’s situation offered Michael another possibility. If he could understand the principle behind the restriction placed on her spirits and reproduce something similar for Lily, then his cousin’s strength could take another enormous leap.","Fortunately, the past three days had not been without gains. Throughout the entire evolution process, Michael had repeatedly used the Eye of Truth.","Several ideas had already taken root in his mind. What Michael needed now was time to digest everything he had seen and determine whether he could create something similar.","If he succeeded, Lily would benefit immediately. And perhaps more importantly, Michael’s own understanding of Infinite Evolution would deepen.","His talent was still filled with mysteries. Every unusual interaction he understood brought him one step closer to truly controlling its possibilities instead of merely using whatever functions appeared before him.","Arianne’s eyelids slowly fluttered. For a few seconds, her green eyes remained unfocused as she stared at the shifting aurora above.","\"I’m still not used to it.\"","Her voice was soft and slightly hoarse.","A moment later, Arianne finally noticed Michael crouching beside her.","\"Michael?\"","The surprise lasted less than a second. Arianne suddenly reached out, wrapped both arms around him, and dragged him down into the golden grass with her.","Michael could have stopped her easily, but there was simply no reason to. He allowed himself to fall beside her as Arianne pressed close, her arms tightening around him.","The familiar scent surrounding her reached him at once. Michael’s body relaxed almost subconsciously.","As he rested there, Michael couldn’t help thinking back to how awkward he had been around Arianne only a few days earlier.","He knew his feelings for her were deep.","Arianne was his first love. And from everything between them, Michael knew she felt the same.","Of course, their relationship was also unusual. Arianne’s current body had been reconstructed from something originating from Michael’s own flesh, blood, and soul.","That connection had inevitably influenced the closeness between them to some degree. Michael was aware of that. But he had never believed it completely explained what existed between them. Perhaps he was deceiving himself, but he loved this feeling. It was new and special.","Still, Michael could not deny that the time spent between them was not long. Three days ago, he had been bothered by something after Arianne returned from the trial.","Time.","From Michael’s perspective, she had disappeared for only five hours. For Arianne, five years had passed.","Five years was enough for someone to change completely. Anything could have happened.","Fortunately, those worries had disappeared after Michael properly understood how the Awakening Trial affected its participants.","*","Sorry for the late update dear readers!"]},{"number":1266,"title":"Chapter 1266: Difference Between Natural and Artificial Awakening [2]","paragraphs":["The trial world seemed to function somewhat like an extremely vivid dream after someone returned.","This was another detail Michael had learned from Arianne. For one, a participant did not necessarily enter the trial using their actual body.","Arianne had possessed another identity inside. While inside, everything had been completely real to Arianne.","Every experience had carried the same weight as reality. But after returning, according to Arianne, those five years now felt closer to an extraordinarily vivid dream.","She remembered them clearly. She could recall what she learned and the experiences she had gone through.","Yet they no longer overwhelmed her sense of self. Michael could roughly understand why.","The Awakening Temple was supposed to create Awakeners, not people who returned with mental issues. If someone spent decades inside a sufficiently difficult trial, came back after only a few external hours, and still emotionally processed both lives equally, the consequences could be disastrous.","They might feel disconnected from their real identity. Their personality could completely shift. Some might even reject their original identity.","Making the trial experience settle into something resembling an intensely realistic dream probably prevented that. The experiences remained. But the participant’s original sense of identity stayed dominant.","Knowing this had removed most of Michael’s earlier awkwardness. The Arianne holding him now had lived through five years of experiences. But she was still Arianne.","With this knowledge, Michael felt he could be a bit more at ease with letting Aunt Mia use the Awakening Temple, if she was interested in becoming an Awakener. At first, knowing that there was still a possibility of death, he had dismissed the idea and settled with buying a class scroll instead.","Though it was expensive, Michael had a lot of treasures he could exchange for it. This was also the advantage of having a territory as big as the empire behind him.","Still, if there was no need to endure such a cost, there was no need to force it. Since the trial likely did not carry the kind of risk that could leave Aunt Mia a stranger to herself, he would consider using it if he had to.","Michael’s thoughts settled before turning his attention fully back to Arianne.","\"How do you feel?\"","Arianne remained pressed against him for a moment before lifting her head slightly.","\"Great. The experience was painful, though.\"","Unlike Michael or his undead, who bore the experience of their evolution alone, Arianne had to integrate with her spirit beings and guide their evolution. Of course, this guiding wasn’t some omnipotent ability. The current Arianne was still far from that. It was more like a way to deepen the connection between spirit and tamer.","The mechanics were a bit complex for Michael to grasp, but he understood the gist of it.","Arianne’s expression quickly brightened. She began praising Michael right away, especially when she thought about what he had done to her spirits.","From her perspective, she had already returned with a powerful class and an exceptional foundation. Now Michael had taken the three spirits she depended on and evolved all of them to Epic Grade ★★★ while they were still only Level 10.","The power ceiling in the spirit world was weaker than the main world, but they followed a similar structure. Perhaps it was the trial’s way of deepening an Awakener’s understanding, but thanks to her experience there, Arianne had even more knowledge than Michael did when he first awakened.","Michael’s ability to bring her spirits to a level said to only exist in legends was so absurd that even Arianne, who had only spent a few years inside a world built around Spirit Tamers, understood how ridiculous it was.","Michael naturally felt good hearing her praise.","Still, he remembered to warn her.","\"Don’t reveal what happened here to anyone. If possible, hide your spirit grades too.\"","He was not especially worried about ordinary people. The problem was what would happen if someone knowledgeable discovered the uniform grade of Arianne’s spirits.","That kind of thing was far too abnormal. Even without knowing about Infinite Evolution, it could make Arianne a target for investigation.","Arianne nodded at once.","\"Okay.\"","Michael relaxed slightly after seeing her accept the warning.","Michael then smiled at her.","\"What are you waiting for? I want to see them.\"","Arianne’s eyes lit up at once. She had clearly been waiting for him to ask.","She sat up from the golden grass and closed her eyes for a moment. A faint spiritual fluctuation spread from her body and three figures slowly emerged.","The first two appeared together.","A boy and a girl.","Twins.","Both looked around seven or eight years old, with nearly identical facial structures that made their relationship obvious at a glance. Their faces were delicate and youthful, their features almost too refined for ordinary children.","The boy had short black hair that fell naturally over his forehead and striking silver eyes. His skin was pale, and he wore simple dark clothing that seemed to have formed naturally alongside his spiritual body.","Beside him stood his twin sister.","Unlike her brother, her hair was completely white.","It fell past her shoulders in soft strands, creating a sharp contrast against the boy’s black hair. Her eyes were the same silver as his, carrying a faint reflective quality. She looked slightly more expressive than her brother, her eyes moving curiously between Arianne and Michael.","At first glance, both children appeared completely real. Even their breathing and subtle movements were convincing enough that someone unfamiliar with spirits could easily mistake them for living children.","Only upon approaching closely would the differences become noticeable. Their bodies possessed an almost imperceptible translucence around the edges. The golden grass beneath their feet could faintly be seen through them whenever their spiritual forms fluctuated.","They looked alive. But it was clear they weren’t human.","The third spirit was completely different. A small red lion appeared beside them.","It was still clearly a cub, barely reaching Arianne’s knee, with soft crimson fur and a short mane beginning to grow around its neck. Its large golden-red eyes moved curiously between Michael and Arianne.","Compared to the twins, the little lion was far less restrained. The moment it fully manifested, its tail flicked excitedly, and it moved closer to Arianne right away."]},{"number":1267,"title":"Chapter 1267: Difference Between Natural and Artificial Awakening [3]","paragraphs":["After greeting Arianne, the little lion cub lingered beside her for only a moment before its attention shifted back toward Michael.","Its ears twitched. Then it took a small step toward him. There was a hint of hesitation in its movements.","Arianne noticed the little lion’s actions.","\"Liora?\"","The crimson cub paused when its name was called, glanced back at her, then continued edging closer to Michael.","Michael raised an eyebrow. When Liora finally came within reach, he extended one hand toward it.","The cub sniffed his fingers before lightly pressing the side of its head against his palm.","The sensation was familiar.","It was not exactly the same as touching ordinary flesh. There was a faint coolness and an almost weightless resistance beneath his hand, something very similar to the feeling he experienced whenever Lunara’s spiritual body came into contact with his own.","Michael gently ran his hand over Liora’s head. The little lion relaxed in comfort.","Not far away, though the twins did not approach him, their silver eyes remained fixed on him.","Arianne stared at the scene with confusion.","\"Why does it seem like Liora likes you?\"","It wasn’t that she didn’t like what was going on, but when she had first brought the three spirits out, none of them had wanted to get close to him. Since they didn’t need to be out for her to use the evolution crystals, this was only the second time she was summoning them in front of Michael.","Michael did not say anything in response to Arianne’s confusion.","He, however, had a certain suspicion.","Though the three spirits had no soul contract with him, all three had undergone evolution through Evolution Essence Crystals created by Infinite Evolution. Perhaps that had left something behind.","Perhaps not merely as deep as a soul connection, but maybe some faint affinity had been formed between them, due to him being the source responsible for their transformation.","These three were Arianne’s spirits. Liora, the small crimson lion. The black-haired boy, Cael. And his white-haired twin sister, Miki.","Michael’s gaze shifted between their current appearances, noting how far it differed from their initial appearance.","According to Arianne, the twins had been her starting spirits, the first companions she received on her path as a Spirit Tamer.","Liora was different. Arianne had obtained the little lion much later in the trial.","Thanks to her performance in the trial, Arianne had been able to bring them out as Rare Grade spirit beings.","All of a sudden, Arianne exclaimed in surprise.","\"So powerful.\"","After checking the three spirits properly, she quickly summarized what had changed in their panels.","If Michael could see Arianne’s panel, it would look something like this:","[Name: Cael]","[Race: Yangborn Spirit]","[Grade: Epic ★★★]","[Level: 10]","[Skills:]","[Spirit Possession]","[Extreme Yang Body Reinforcement]","[...]","For one, Cael’s race had changed. That much did not surprise Michael.","Race changes were something Infinite Evolution had caused many times before. What truly caught his attention was one of Cael’s skills.","According to Arianne, Humanoid Spirits were generally regarded as some of the weakest spirits in the Spirit Realm.","Most of that reputation came from Human Spirits, but fortunately, the twins had been different.","Their usefulness came from two core skills. Spirit Possession, which was a staple for all spirit beings, and an enhancement ability.","Michael quickly compared Spirit Possession to Lunara inhabiting his body, based on Arianne’s description of the skill.","The principle was similar. A spirit could merge with the tamer’s body and lend its abilities directly.","The tamer could remain in control and simply use the spirit’s power, or allow the spirit to take over more directly.","Spirit Tamers had different styles of combat. Some relied on spirit possession as their main combat style. Others treated their spirits as independent fighters.","Of course, one could switch between both depending on the situation.","Cael’s enhancement was physical in nature. Back when Cael had still been Common Grade, the enhancement skill could increase Arianne’s physical attributes by twenty-five percent for a limited period.","The cost was that it consumed mana rapidly. Arianne could not maintain it for long.","Even so, that boost had been one of the main reasons she survived the early stages of the trial.","Later, after Cael reached Rare Grade, the enhancement increased to fifty percent.","For Arianne, this skill had allowed her to do a lot early in her trial.","But now the old enhancement skill was gone. In its place was something else.","[Extreme Yang Body Reinforcement]","[Effect: Upon Possession, ninety percent of the user’s available mana will be converted into Yang Essence and used to reinforce the physical body.]","[While active, physical attributes will be significantly increased.]","[Endurance, recovery speed, resistance to physical damage, vitality, and bodily resilience will be greatly enhanced.]","[The greater the amount of mana converted, the stronger the reinforcement.]","[Can only be used when the user’s mana pool is at least 80 percent.]","This was completely different from the old version. Before, Cael had simply provided a flat percentage increase to her physical attributes while consuming mana.","Now the skill practically transformed mana itself into physical strength, providing an extreme enhancement the previous skill couldn’t have matched.","However, Cael was not the only one who had changed. Miki’s panel was almost a mirror image of her brother’s.","[Name: Miki]","[Race: Yinborn Spirit]","[Grade: Epic ★★★]","[Level: 10]","[Skills:]","[Spirit Possession]","[Extreme Yin Body Reinforcement]","[...]","Miki’s special skill was also an enhancement type like her brother’s, but unlike him, hers targeted the user’s mana. When her grade was ordinary, she could increase the mana pool by twenty-five percent, and at Rare Grade, she could do the same at fifty percent while also boosting recovery speed.","However, just like her brother, Miki’s special skill had also mutated.","[Extreme Yin Mana Reinforcement]","[Effect: Upon Possession, a large portion of the user’s physical vitality will be converted into Yin Essence used to greatly reinforce the user’s mana pool and magical output.]","[While active, mana capacity, mana recovery speed, spell power, energy control, perception, and resistance to mental interference will be significantly increased.]","[The greater the amount of physical vitality converted, the stronger the mana reinforcement.]"]},{"number":1268,"title":"Chapter 1268: Difference Between Natural and Artificial Awakening [4]","paragraphs":["Yin and Yang.","The thought appeared in Michael’s mind as he looked between the twins.","The concept itself was ancient and incredibly broad. Yin and Yang were not simply opposites.","They represented two contrasting forces that existed together, restrained each other, and in many cases completed one another.","Yang was often associated with activity, heat, strength, vitality, expansion, and the physical.","Yin leaned toward stillness, cold, spirit, energy, perception, internal force, and the immaterial.","The exact meaning changed depending on the system using it, but the principle was usually similar.","Opposites. Yet connected. Separate. Yet complementary.","Looking at Cael and Miki, Michael could see that idea almost perfectly reflected in them.","Cael had black hair and represented Yang, yet his ability sacrificed mana to strengthen the body.","Miki had white hair and represented Yin, yet her ability did the opposite, sacrificing physical vitality to strengthen mana and magical output.","Even their appearances felt like mirrors of one another. One dark. One light.","Their abilities did not merely contrast. They balanced each other.","\"The abilities are good,\" Michael praised.","\"You’re not wrong. Their special abilities are worlds away from what they could do. I’ve not tested it yet, but I know the effect will be much stronger!\" Arianne agreed, but there was a trace of concern on her face.","\"However, it seems like what used to be a normal skill has now turned into a trump card, though.\"","The strength of both skills was obvious. The cost was just as obvious.","Compared to their old versions, the new abilities were much more extreme. Michael understood where Arianne’s concern came from.","\"Even though the skills changed, you two should still be able to use the old versions, right?\"","Before Arianne could answer, the twins did.","\"Master, yes.\" Cael stated.","Miki nodded beside him.","\"We’ve become much stronger, but we can still use all of our previous abilities.\"","Arianne’s expression brightened at once.","The twins explained that evolution had not erased their old enhancement methods. The original physical and mana boosts still existed.","They could still use the weaker twenty-five or fifty percent enhancement styles when needed, with far lower costs. The new Extreme abilities were simply another level above them.","With this, Arianne could use the old skills for ordinary battles. And when something truly dangerous appeared, she could use the evolved versions as trump cards.","Michael nodded slowly. This was a very good enhancement to Arianne’s combat potential.","Arianne seemed to come to the same conclusion. She reached out and playfully rubbed both twins on the head.","Cael accepted it quietly, while Miki leaned into her hand with a faint smile.","Liora, who was lying by Michael’s side, noticed this right away, and the little crimson lion pushed forward between them, clearly unwilling to be left out.","Arianne laughed and used her other hand to scratch beneath its chin.","Seeing the scene, Michael couldn’t help but smile.","Although the entire trial now felt like an extremely vivid dream to Arianne, the three spirits had come back with her. More importantly, they had inherited the memories of those five years too.","If the spirits had vanished when the trial ended, perhaps those feelings would have settled into something distant a few hours after the trial. But their presence changed this.","What might otherwise have remained a surface-level attachment formed inside a trial had become something much deeper and more real.","As the five of them continued playing around, Michael shifted his attention toward Liora’s information. The little lion had changed just as much as the twins.","[Name: Liora]","[Race: Crimsonflame Lion Spirit]","[Grade: Epic ★★★]","[Level: 10]","[Skills:]","[Spirit Possession]","[Crimsonflame State]","[...]","Like the twins, one of this lion’s core skills had also mutated.","[Crimsonflame State]","[Effect: Upon activation, physical attributes are increased by 100%.]","[Fire affinity and fire magic output are increased by 100%.]","[Fire resistance, physical resilience, and recovery speed are significantly enhanced.]","[All fire-based attacks gain increased destructive power while the state is active.]","Compared to Cael and Miki, Liora’s ability was much more straightforward. There was no complicated conversion between mana and vitality.","No tradeoff between the physical body and magical output. It simply made Liora, or Arianne while possessed by Liora, far stronger in both close combat and fire magic.","[Name: Arianne Evermoon]","[Race: High Human]","[Class: Spirit Tamer]","[Level: 10 (MAX)]","[Title: Watched By The Will]","Thanks to a strange presence surrounding you, you have attracted the gaze of the Origin Will. Effect: Gain 1.5 times more experience points.","[Strength: 15.3]","[Agility: 18.5]","[Constitution: 14.7]","[Intelligence: 20.6]","[Attribute Points: 170]","[Skills: ...]","[Traits: Iron Mind]","[Contract Slots: 2 / 5]","[Gifts: Mark of Origin]","Arianne herself was not bad either. In fact, when Michael looked over her current panel, he had to admit that her foundation was already far better than his had been more than a year ago when he had just awakened.","Her individual stats might still look small compared to what Michael was used to seeing now, but that was only because his perspective had become distorted after reaching his current level.","For a Level 10 Awakener, Arianne was very strong.","The same could be said for Lily. Thinking about how his cousin also possessed a ridiculous foundation while still at Level 10, Michael could not help but feel that background truly mattered a lot.","Talent, luck, and effort mattered as well. But having someone powerful behind you could completely change your starting point.","With a tall enough tree shielding you from the wind and rain, one person’s beginning could already be another person’s ending point.","Michael had started with almost nothing. He had needed to struggle for resources, information, undead, and every small advantage he could get.","Arianne and Lily were different.","They had him.","This was what having a background meant.","*","A/N: Two Chapters left! A certain misconception has been going on about the author for months. Many accuse him of doing four Chapters a day and then taking a day off, when in reality this author hasn’t missed a single day of updates in close to two years. This misconception comes from different time zones and a bit of inconsistency on the author’s part.","It’s been three days since I said I’d start doing at least four Chapters a day, and with the remaining two Chapters to upload, that’s a total of twelve Chapters. Readers can go verify. This author might be a bit unreliable, but he tries his best. Please vote to motivate the author, and thanks for the continued support!"]},{"number":1269,"title":"Chapter 1269: Difference Between Natural and Artificial Awakening [5]","paragraphs":["Now that Arianne had officially become an Awakener, there were two major goals ahead of her.","The first was increasing her Rank.","At Level 10, Arianne had already reached the limit of Rank Zero. No matter how much experience she accumulated, she would not be able to level up again until she completed her Rank Advancement Quest.","Fortunately, the quest generated by Spirit Tamer was not especially unreasonable. At least, not by Michael’s standards.","One requirement was to personally defeat ten monsters at least five levels above her without relying on outside assistance. The second was to successfully teach new skills to her contracted spirits.","Between the two, Michael actually considered the first one easier.","For an ordinary Level 10 Awakener, that would probably sound ridiculous, since even something like a hobgoblin with a natural growth limit around Level 14 could beat an inexperienced Rank Zero Awakener senseless if they were careless.","After all, the attribute points provided per level could only make an Awakener so strong. The stronger they became, the less effect each additional point provided, so Awakeners actually needed to use methods outside advancement task rewards to accumulate stat points if they didn’t want to be the weakest at their level.","A five-level difference was already dangerous at the lower Ranks.","But Arianne was not ordinary.","Without even considering Spirit Possession, Michael felt she could already exchange blows with some Rank One creatures.","If he gave her a few Evolution Essence Crystals and strengthened her stats further, she could become even more exaggerated. Reaching a point where she alone could contend with ordinary Rank Two creatures was not impossible.","Once her spirits were factored in, the difficulty of the first advancement requirement dropped even further. This was also exactly why Michael did not want Arianne to settle for merely completing the minimum condition.","Ten Level 15 monsters? That was too easy.","If she could defeat Level 20 monsters, then she should fight those instead. If she could handle Level 30 monsters, then there was even less reason to stop earlier.","As long as she carefully selected her opponents, Michael believed Arianne had a genuine chance of pushing far beyond the intended difficulty.","Rank Advancement Quests rewarded performance. The harder the conditions exceeded the minimum requirement, the better the final evaluation and rewards could become.","That alone could shave away a considerable amount of the time she would normally need to reach Rank Two.","However, Arianne did not have unlimited time on her hands. There was another matter she now had to deal with, which was her second major goal.","The Origin Battlefield. Since Arianne had officially become an Awakener, she was also subject to its monthly requirement. She would need to enter the Origin Battlefield and spend the necessary amount of time there before the reset.","Through Arianne, Michael had started noticing differences between natural Awakeners like himself and those who awakened through external methods. That likely included people awakened through Class Scrolls as well.","On the surface, there was barely any difference. They had levels, classes, stats, skills, advancement quests, Marks of Origin. Everything looked normal.","But there was one major distinction. Arianne could not enter the Land of Origin.","This meant she only had one body. Her original body.","Michael had spent some time thinking about whether this should be considered a disadvantage.","Strictly speaking, he did not think it was one. But it certainly was not an advantage either.","Natural Awakeners like Michael gained something incredibly valuable once they reached Rank Two. From that point onward, with two bodies they effectively possessed twice the usable time.","Growth between the two was synchronized. The one thing the original body lacked that the second body had was a terrifying degree of safety.","If something happened to the body in the Land of Origin under normal circumstances, the Awakener would not truly die. They would only lose around ten percent of their total attributes and temporarily lose access to the Land of Origin.","When they were eventually allowed to return, the Origin Will would recreate their body somewhere else.","Before the existence of the Origin Battlefield, Michael would not have considered this difference particularly overwhelming. The Land of Origin had always been separated from the greater universe. That limited what the second body could actually do.","But things were changing. The Universal Cornerstone had changed them.","Michael had already created a route from the Land of Origin into the Origin Battlefield. That meant the body created by the Origin Will was no longer necessarily trapped inside the Land of Origin.","As long as an Awakener registered that body with a Universal Cornerstone and obtained permission to create or use Subsidiary Territorial Anchors, then theoretically, their second body could leave.","Michael did not think his exact method was the only possible one. Even if another Awakener could not reproduce what he had done, future Cornerstone owners would almost certainly discover their own routes. After all, in matters of the soul, likely all Rank Four Awakeners in the Fourth Layer were more knowledgeable than him.","Once a station existed, an Awakener’s second body could enter the Origin Battlefield. From there, it could potentially use another Anchor to step into the greater universe itself.","This led Michael to the advantage he discovered other Awakeners like himself possessed over people like Arianne.","What was the greatest advantage of the bodies created by the Origin Will?","Outside that their growth was synchronized, it was that under ordinary circumstances, death was not truly death. As long as some extraordinary method capable of affecting the original soul was not used, destroying the Land of Origin body only resulted in a penalty.","Once the second bodies of Awakeners could operate on a wider scale, what stopped an Awakener from hiding their original body somewhere extremely secure and allowing the Origin Will body to act in their place?","Aside from situations where the original body was specifically required, such as official Battlefield ranking matches, the second body could theoretically do almost everything else. But if that body died, the Awakener would only suffer a loss. They would remain alive.","For many Awakeners, wouldn’t that effectively become a second life?","As long as the original body remained hidden and protected, death of the clone was merely temporary. Repeated carefully enough, it almost resembled a strange form of immortality.","Wasn’t this just a supernatural version of the respawn mechanics of games?"]},{"number":1270,"title":"Chapter 1270: Four Pieces [1]","paragraphs":["Truly, with the existence of the Origin Battlefield, the life of an Awakener, which Michael had never really felt was like a game even as he grew stronger, was starting to feel a bit more like one.","However, outside of this game-like immortality, which a certain part of him suspected arianne might not have due to being a native of the land of origin, Michael had not noticed any other major advantage natural Awakeners like him possessed over people like her.","Maybe there were more differences hidden deeper within the system, or there were restrictions Arianne would only discover after reaching higher Ranks. For now, there was no point guessing. Only the future could answer that.","What Michael needed to focus on was the present. As several thoughts passed through his mind, he looked toward Arianne.","\"So, what now?\"","Something flickered across Arianne’s face.","A few days ago, before Michael began evolving her spirits, the two of them had already discussed the Origin Battlefield.","The first thing Michael had done after confirming that Arianne could access it was give her a choice. She could enter right away and begin fulfilling her required monthly time.","Or she could wait for Michael to strengthen her spirits as much as possible, after which she would have to compress nearly all of her remaining required time into the rest of the month.","Arianne had chosen the second option.","Now that Cael, Miki, and Liora had all completed their evolutions, there was no longer any reason to delay.","A serious expression appeared on Arianne’s face.","\"I’m ready.\"","Michael felt a faint worry rise inside him. If something happened to her in the Origin Battlefield, only death awaited.","Still, none of that appeared on Michael’s face. He remained calm.","In any case, he had already warned her about all this before she awakened.","\"Stay safe. You don’t need to fight anyone. Just spend the required time there and come back.\"","Arianne nodded obediently without arguing.","\"I’ll be careful.\"","Michael studied her for another second before finally relaxing.","\"In that case, go take a bath first.\"","Michael’s lips curved slightly.","\"You’ve been unconscious for more than half of the three days we spent here. Don’t tell me you’re planning to enter the Origin Battlefield looking like this.\"","Arianne looked down at herself at once. She saw several strands of golden grass caught in her clothes and hair.","Her eyes narrowed.","A moment later, a punch was already headed at Michael’s chest, which he easily blocked with a loud laugh.","A second later, a portal opened beneath them and they disappeared into it.","Over the next hour, Michael brought Arianne back to the Land of Origin and prepared everything he could for her.","He used several Evolution Essence Crystals to strengthen her attributes further. If not for the Rank limitation that only allowed him to use Common Grade Evolution Essence Crystals at Rank One, he would have pushed all her stats to two hundred points. Still, using eighty of her attribute points brought all of her attributes up to forty each, which was already very strong.","After strengthening Arianne’s foundation, Michael opened the imperial treasury.","Arianne was given several sets of armor suitable for her current Rank. Her Mark of Origin’s storage space was also filled with supplies: healing potions, mana-restoration potions, food, water, protective items, a few weapons, and various consumables Michael felt might become useful.","By the time everything was prepared, evening had arrived in the Land of Origin.","The two eventually appeared on one of the palace balconies.","Below them stretched the capital.","Golden evening light covered the enormous city, reflecting from rooftops, towers, statues, and distant walls. Streets were crowded with people returning home while carriages and mounted soldiers moved through the broader avenues.","The palace stood high enough that much of the capital could be seen from here.","Michael and Arianne stood beside each other near the balcony railing.","For a while, neither seemed particularly eager to move.","Eventually, Arianne looked toward him.","\"I have to go.\"","Michael nodded.","\"Be careful.\"","Arianne smiled faintly.","She leaned closer. Michael met her halfway, and their lips touched briefly before Arianne pulled back.","A moment later, light began surrounding her body. Her figure became increasingly transparent before breaking apart completely into countless motes. Within a second, she was gone.","Michael remained standing.","The evening wind passed across the balcony as he continued staring at the capital below him. Several thoughts moved through his mind.","After a while, he sighed.","\"Maybe I shouldn’t let Aunt Mia become an Awakener.\"","Worry lined his face.","\"Also, where the hell is Lily? That silly girl. Couldn’t she at least come out and greet me?\"","Several days had already passed. Yet his cousin was still nowhere to be seen. If not for Jester, he would have thought the worst had happened.","Michael turned to look at the clear sky while sighing again.","\"Is the Zeroth Layer really that good to her?\"","Meanwhile, the Lily Michael was wondering about was standing over a white-skinned youth with bear-like characteristics spread across his body.","The young man was unconscious.","Around him, several more figures lay scattered across the ground. Some were groaning. Others were completely still.","A few had limbs bent at unnatural angles, obviously broken, while one figure had been thrown hard enough into a nearby stone ridge that cracks spread around the point of impact.","Lily stood in the middle of all of them, breathing a little heavily.","Only moments ago, she had finished killing an Epic Grade Level 10 creature guarding a strange stone pillar inside a Level Three region of the Zeroth Layer.","It had been the fourth such pillar she had found.","The first three had gone smoothly. This time, however, she had barely finished the battle when a group of people ambushed her.","At first, Lily had only wanted to drive them away.","She did not like killing people. Two days ago, she had no choice but to kill someone, and she didn’t like the feeling.","Even after spending so much time inside the Origin Battlefield, that part of her had not changed much.","But being kind did not mean being soft."]},{"number":1271,"title":"Chapter 1271: Four Pieces [2]","paragraphs":["Since Lily knew that people strong enough to fight her would not die just because she broke an arm or shattered a leg, when the group tried to rob her of the opportunity she had worked hard to obtain, with the intention of killing her, she did not hold back.","Outside of their intention to kill her, it was especially because this was the opportunity she’d had, after so long, to use to help her cousin.","Michael had done far too much for her.","She finally found something useful, so why should she simply hand it over because a group of strangers wanted it?","Still, Lily’s anger had remained controlled. That was until the bear-like youth woke briefly and began insulting her.","The others had called him Prince.","At first, Lily had ignored him and his insults and threats even after beating him. But in frustration over being defeated, he said something indecent about her mother.","It had only been a few seconds since then, and now the young prince had stopped talking too, looking like he could barely breathe.","Was Lily a kind soul? Yes. One could even call her timid in many situations.","She disliked unnecessary conflict and hated fighting when there was another option.","But if Michael were standing here now, watching how she had just handled the group, he would have found the sight strangely familiar.","When Michael and Lily were younger, under Aunt Mia’s care, a single mother caring for them had always attracted comments from people who had nothing better to do.","Sometimes children repeated what they heard from adults. Sometimes they invented their own insults.","The previous Michael had usually handled such situations calmly. Most of the time, he would simply report the matter to a teacher and move on.","Lily, on the other hand, had never been quite as patient.","When boys or girls her age insulted Aunt Mia, Lily had a habit of handling the matter personally, after warning them, if they paid no heed.","That usually involved fists.","Sometimes scratching.","On one memorable occasion, biting.","Time had passed, and though she had grown older, quieter, and more restrained, some things had clearly never changed.","One should never underestimate the anger of a child when someone insulted their mother.","Even supernaturals tend to leave an enemy’s mother out of a battle of words.","It was one thing if the enemy’s parents were weak and the enemy themselves didn’t care about them, but if doing so only angered their opponent further while insulting someone much stronger than themselves, they could be done for.","In cases like this, like ordinary people, it was mostly the fathers of the opposing party that were used as a means of attack.","After calming herself down, Lily turned away from the group of almost-dead white bears. Her attention returned to the strange stone pillar.","The pillar was several meters tall and covered from top to bottom in shifting runes. They moved across its surface like living symbols, constantly rearranging themselves into patterns Lily could not understand.","She walked over and placed one hand against the cold stone. The moment her palm touched it, a panel appeared in front of her.","[Fragmented Universal Cornerstone detected.]","[Would you like to claim one fragment of the Universal Cornerstone?]","[Note: Gathering Four fragments will form a complete cornerstone.]","Lily’s eyes brightened at once.","\"Yes.\"","The pillar trembled. The runes covering it began to peel away one after another, turning into streams of light that gathered before her.","A few seconds later, the entire pillar cracked and collapsed into countless particles.","Something solid formed within the light. Lily instinctively reached out and caught it.","It was a strange object, roughly the size of her palm. At first glance, it looked like a quarter of a circular plate.","Its surface was dark, almost black, with faint golden lines running through it. Along the curved edge, tiny runes slowly shifted in and out of existence.","The moment she held it, another panel appeared.","[Universal Cornerstone Fragment]","[Fragment: 1/4]","[Collect four fragments to reconstruct a complete Universal Cornerstone.]","Lily stared at the object for a few seconds, her face slowly breaking into a wide smile.","\"Finally.\"","She quickly reached into her storage space. Three nearly identical fragments appeared.","When placed together, the four pieces clearly belonged to the same circular object. Lily’s smile grew even wider.","\"The fourth piece.\"","She had spent so much time moving from region to region for this.","It wasn’t easy. Sometimes she had to face two or three Epic Grade creatures alone. The one she had just fought was the only one she’d found alone, but it was also the strongest among all the ones she had encountered.","Fortunately, she didn’t need to go through any more of these danger-filled battles, since she had now gathered all four of these pieces.","Lily carefully stored all four fragments again. Her first thought was not about what she could gain from them.","It was Michael. She had finally done something that might actually be useful to her cousin.","These four fragments were probably valuable enough that even he might not casually dismiss them. She was almost sure this was probably what he was looking for too. After all, wasn’t it just a week ago that a universal announcement had been made because of something like this?","Lily looked toward the distant sky.","\"I can finally go home. Hmmm, though I could just give this to my cousin for free, I wonder if I can ask for a few favors instead. Ugh, but what would I even ask for?!\"","Amidst her thoughts, Lily’s body disappeared into motes of light.","*","Back in the Land of Origin, Michael had already returned to his office.","Several documents were spread across the desk in front of him. He had barely gone through a few pages when a knock sounded from the door.","Through his senses, he could tell there were three presences outside.","\"Enter.\"","The door opened.","A Silver Guard stepped inside first, dressed in polished silver armor.","Beside him was a youth who looked no older than seventeen. He wore simple clothes that looked more suited to an ordinary village or poor district than the imperial palace.","His expression was tense. In his arms, he carried someone.","Michael’s gaze moved toward the unconscious figure, then stopped, confusion settling over his face.","The person being carried looked almost exactly like the youth holding him.","Twins like this were quite good on the eyes, but what did they have to do with him?","In confusion, Michael turned to look at the Silver Guard, when he noticed the unconscious youth suddenly \"wake\" up, while the previously conscious one abruptly fell unconscious.","* * *","A/N: The author knows he’s still owing three Chapters! The author will try his best!"]},{"number":1272,"title":"Chapter 1272: Awakeners In The Land Of Origin [1]","paragraphs":["Bok did not know exactly when it had happened.","Was it three days ago? Or four? He could no longer tell.","All he knew was that when he woke up, he was no longer in his room.","Bok’s thoughts returned to the moment he first \"awakened.\"","Instead of the familiar wooden ceiling above his bed, he had opened his eyes to an endless canopy of leaves. Sunlight slipped through the branches in scattered beams, while insects buzzed somewhere within the surrounding undergrowth.","The ground beneath him was cold and slightly damp.","For several long seconds, Bok simply lay there.","His mind felt sluggish, and his body was strangely heavy. There was also an unfamiliar ache in his shoulders, arms, and lower back, as though he had spent the previous day doing hard physical labour.","Yet beneath that soreness was something else, a faint sense that his limbs responded a little too easily, as if lifting himself would take less effort than it should. It wasn’t a large difference. He could have dismissed it as his imagination. But it was there.","When he finally sat up, dried leaves fell from his chest.","His confusion only deepened when he looked down.","He was wearing farmer’s clothes.","The loose brown shirt was made from rough fabric, with patches around the elbows and several dark stains across the front. His trousers were not much better. They were worn, slightly oversized, and held around his waist by a narrow strip of leather.","A cold feeling crawled down his spine.","Had he been kidnapped? The possibility caused him to jump to his feet and look around frantically.","\"Hello?\"","His voice traveled through the forest, but no one answered.","\"Is anyone there?\"","Only the rustling leaves responded.","Bok searched himself for injuries. Aside from the aches across his body, he found none. His clothes were intact, and there were no ropes, chains, or signs that someone had restrained him. But that did little to reassure him.","If he had been kidnapped, why had they abandoned him inside a forest? Unless they had not abandoned him. Perhaps they were watching from somewhere nearby.","The thought made his breathing quicken. He turned in a slow circle, examining every tree and bush. Each shadow suddenly looked like a person waiting to emerge. Every sound caused his heart to leap as another possibility entered his mind.","Was it that someone had discovered what he had done?","Bok’s face lost what little colour it had left. He dropped to his knees at once.","\"I’m sorry!\"","His voice startled several birds from a nearby tree.","They flew into the air as Bok pressed his palms together and looked toward the sky.","\"I swear I’ll never do it again!\"","Three days earlier, he and several of his friends had sneaked out at night to spy on the prettiest widow in the village.","Everyone knew the village chief visited her occasionally. No one said it openly, especially since the village chief already had a wife, but his visits were hardly a secret.","That night, Bok’s friends claimed the two of them would meet beside the river.","They had hidden behind some bushes and waited.","Unfortunately, what they witnessed was considerably more than a simple meeting.","At the time, Bok had found the entire thing exciting.","Now, abandoned in a forest with no idea how he arrived there, he could only assume that some higher power was punishing him.","\"I didn’t suggest it!\" he shouted. \"It was Fern! He said we should follow them!\"","That was true.","It had been Fern’s idea.","However, Bok had agreed almost at once.","He had even brought food so they would not become hungry while waiting.","\"I only watched for a little while!\"","That was less true.","He had watched until the end.","Bok remained on his knees for some time, confessing everything he could remember. He apologized to the widow, the village chief, the village chief’s wife, and any unknown god who might have taken offence.","Nothing happened.","No divine voice responded, nor did any bolt of lightning descend from the sky.","After several minutes, his breathing gradually settled.","Bok rose cautiously and brushed the dirt from his knees. His fear had not disappeared, but it had reduced enough for him to observe his surroundings properly.","The forest was thick, but it was not especially dark. The trees were spread far enough apart for sunlight to reach the ground, and there was little vegetation blocking the path ahead.","A narrow trail ran between the trees.","Bok stared at it. Something about it seemed familiar.","He turned toward a large tree on his left. Its trunk divided into two thick sections several meters above the ground, and one of its roots rose from the earth like the back of a sleeping animal.","He had seen it before.","Bok slowly approached the tree and placed his hand against its bark.","His gaze shifted toward the path again. The more he looked around, the more familiar the forest became.","It was located just outside the village.","People came here to collect firewood, forage for edible plants, and hunt small animals. The area was relatively safe as long as they remained near the outskirts.","Going deeper was dangerous, since there were goblins inside the forest.","The creatures were small, weak, and cowardly. In a one-on-one fight, even an ordinary farmer could kill one with a hoe or pitchfork.","The problem was that goblins rarely fought alone.","They gathered in groups, set crude traps, and attacked from several directions. When villagers discovered more than a few of them nearby, they usually gathered money and sent a request to the Adventurers’ Guild.","Trying to eliminate a group without trained help could end with the entire village being attacked in retaliation.","Bok swallowed and looked toward the path leading out of the forest.","If he wasn’t mistaken, the village was less than half an hour away.","He wondered if he should return, but what if whoever had placed him here was still nearby?","Unfortunately, he could only choose this or venture deeper into the forest."]},{"number":1273,"title":"Chapter 1273: Awakeners In The Land Of Origin [2]","paragraphs":["Bok rubbed his face with both hands.","Remaining in the forest was not an option. Even if the outskirts were considered safe, that did not mean goblins never wandered into them.","He searched the ground and found a fallen branch thick enough to serve as a weapon. It would not be particularly effective, but holding it made him feel slightly less helpless.","Then he began following the path.","With each step, more details entered his mind.","There should be a stream farther ahead.","Beyond it stood an old wooden marker warning villagers not to travel deeper into the forest.","If he continued in the opposite direction, he would eventually reach several farms and then the village itself.","Bok followed that route.","After approximately ten minutes, he heard flowing water and stopped.","The stream appeared exactly where he expected it to be.","The water was shallow and clear enough for him to see the stones beneath its surface. Bok approached it carefully before crouching near the bank.","He had not realized how thirsty he was until then.","After drinking several handfuls, he looked down and finally saw his reflection.","A frightened young face stared back at him.","It was his face.","Mostly.","The features looked familiar, but his skin was fairer, looking nothing like the dark skin he’d had from working beneath the sun. His hair was neater, and his cheeks appeared slightly fuller.","He looked like himself after living an entirely different life.","Bok touched his face.","The reflection did the same.","The face in the water was undoubtedly his own.","The shape of his eyes, the slight curve of his nose, and even the small scar near his chin were exactly as Bok remembered them.","Yet the person staring back at him was also different.","His skin had become considerably fairer. Bok had spent most of his life working beneath the sun, and his skin had long since darkened because of it. Now, much of that darkness had disappeared, leaving behind a soft, untouched complexion that looked as though he had remained indoors for years, doing nothing more strenuous than sitting by a window.","His hair was neater too, despite having woken up on the forest floor. His cheeks looked slightly fuller, and even the roughness around his lips had vanished.","Bok hurriedly rolled up his sleeves.","The calluses on his palms remained, but the scars and burns covering his forearms were gone. He had received most of them while learning how to handle knives, boiling water, and freshly slaughtered animals.","Now, there was no trace of them.","\"What happened to me?\"","He pulled at his cheeks, rubbed his skin, and even struck his forearm twice to make sure it was real.","His heart began beating faster again.","Had someone done something to his body? Was this really his body?","The questions frightened him, but remaining beside the stream would not provide any answers. If he wanted to understand what had happened, he first needed to return to the village.","Bok remained crouched beside the water for several minutes before finally standing.","He tightened his grip around the branch he had collected and continued along the path.","The farther he walked, the more familiar everything became.","He recognized the narrow trail used by the village hunters. He knew where the ground dipped and became muddy after rainfall. He even remembered a berry bush hidden between two large stones, although there were no fruits on it at the moment.","That familiarity helped suppress some of his fear.","Whatever had happened to him, he was at least close to home.","Approximately twenty minutes later, the trees began thinning.","Farmland appeared beyond the edge of the forest. Large stretches of green and yellow crops covered the gently sloping land, separated by narrow dirt paths and low wooden fences.","In the distance stood the village.","Bok stopped walking.","Calling it a village almost felt misleading.","Unlike the smaller settlements scattered across the region, some of which contained only a few dozen households, Bok’s village had a population of more than a thousand people.","Fortunately, the people of the village lived fairly harmoniously despite their number.","There were large families whose names had existed there for generations, individuals who had arrived from elsewhere, elderly residents living alone, and young couples still trying to establish households of their own.","Arguments occurred, but serious conflicts were uncommon.","People worked together when the harvest came, shared food during harsh winters, and contributed money whenever monsters threatened the village.","Naturally, that harmony depended on people keeping their shameful affairs private.","Hundreds of wooden and stone houses filled the land ahead. Smoke rose from chimneys, carts travelled along the wider roads, and several large workshops stood near the village centre.","The surrounding farmland was extensive enough to support most of the population. Hunters brought meat and animal hides from the nearby forest, while merchants regularly passed through on their way to the towns farther east.","The village was not wealthy enough to possess stone walls, but it was prosperous.","More importantly, it was home.","Bok breathed out slowly.","Then he stepped onto the road.","The first person to notice him was an elderly farmer guiding an ox-drawn cart toward the fields.","The man glanced at Bok, looked away, then turned back sharply.","\"Bok?\"","Bok stopped.","\"Yes?\"","The farmer stared at him.","\"What happened to you?\"","The question made Bok tense.","\"What do you mean?\"","\"Your skin.\"","Bok instinctively touched his face.","The farmer squinted at him before laughing.","\"You look like some rich merchant’s sheltered son. Have you been secretly bathing in milk?\"","Bok forced a weak smile.","\"I don’t know. I just woke up like this.\"","The farmer laughed again, clearly assuming he was joking.","\"Tell your master you have found a better profession. Perhaps some noblewoman will hire you to stand around and look pretty.\"","He continued down the road, still chuckling to himself.","Bok watched him leave before walking onward.","Unfortunately, the farmer was not the only person who noticed the changes.","The closer Bok got to the village, the stranger the looks became."]}]);
